// English translations for the language toggle (tools/build_en.py from translations/en.json)
const ITEMS_EN={"1": {"desc": "Slams down hard with a lightning flash", "prompt": "The screen first flashes brightly twice and a lightning bolt appears; the text slams down instantly from 2x size and shrinks back to its original size, trembling slightly on landing, then keeps a soft outer glow. The whole sequence lasts about 2.4 seconds, with a fast, explosive rhythm.", "tag": "Impact · Opening", "style": "Impact Entrance", "txt": "Thunder"}, "2": {"desc": "A laser slices the text in two", "prompt": "A glowing laser line cuts rapidly from left to right across the middle of the text; after it passes, the top half of the text shifts up-left and the bottom half shifts down-right, tilting slightly, pauses for a moment, then comes back together. About 2.6 seconds per cycle, with a crisp sci-fi feel.", "tag": "SF · Severed", "style": "Dissipating Exit", "txt": "Sliced"}, "3": {"desc": "Text flips and bounces like a coin", "prompt": "Each character flips two full turns around the Y axis like a coin and jumps upward, then bounces once more, small, when it lands, with a sequential delay of about 0.14 seconds between characters. About 2.4 seconds per cycle, light and playful.", "tag": "Try Your Luck · Game", "style": "Letter-by-Letter Motion", "txt": "Heads or Tails"}, "4": {"desc": "Text explodes and flies in all directions", "prompt": "The text first swells slightly to build up energy, then each character explodes randomly in a different direction, spinning, shrinking and fading out; after a pause, the characters fly back into place to form the text again, alternating between the primary color and an accent color. About 2.8 seconds per cycle, with a strong sense of impact.", "tag": "Impact · Chorus", "style": "Dissipating Exit", "txt": "Explode"}, "5": {"desc": "Text dissolves into particles", "prompt": "From left to right, each character blurs in turn, drifts up and to the right, and fades out, while many small square particles appear around it and float away; after disappearing, the text re-emerges. About 3 seconds per cycle, dramatic.", "tag": "Annihilation · Drama", "style": "Dissipating Exit", "txt": "Vanish"}, "6": {"desc": "Zooms with a heartbeat and spreads ripples", "prompt": "The text zooms in twice in a row like a heartbeat — “thump-thump” — then returns to its original size; with each beat, two circular ripples spread out from the center at the same time and fade away. About 1.3 seconds per beat.", "tag": "Moving · Drama", "style": "Impact Entrance", "txt": "Throb"}, "7": {"desc": "Text rotates in a kaleidoscope", "prompt": "The same word is copied 12 times, arranged radially around a center point in the shape of a flower; the whole group keeps rotating slowly while each copy stretches outward and breathes back in at the same time, forming a kaleidoscope effect, with adjacent copies alternating between light and dark tones. One full rotation takes about 7 seconds.", "tag": "Psychedelic · MV", "style": "3D Spatial Rotation", "txt": "Kaleido"}, "8": {"desc": "Countdown numbers slam down hard", "prompt": "The countdown “3, 2, 1, GO!” appears in sequence; each number slams down forcefully from 3x size and rebounds to its original size, about 0.75 seconds per number, with GO! highlighted in an accent color. Bold black type, with a strong opening feel.", "tag": "Opening · Countdown", "style": "Impact Entrance", "txt": "3,2,1,GO!"}, "9": {"desc": "Text undulates like a wave", "prompt": "Each character rises and falls in sequence and sways slightly from side to side, forming a continuously flowing wave, with the characters alternating between two tones. About 1.4 seconds per wave, with a relaxed, joyful summer feel.", "tag": "Joyful · Summer", "style": "Letter-by-Letter Motion", "txt": "Waves"}, "10": {"desc": "Shakes frame by frame, like stop-motion animation", "prompt": "Each character trembles and rotates slightly at random in a discontinuous, frame-by-frame jumping manner (like stop-motion animation, with no smooth transitions), with each character offset in rhythm from the others. About a 0.9-second loop, with a handmade toy feel.", "tag": "Handmade · Toy", "style": "Letter-by-Letter Motion", "txt": "Stop Motion"}, "11": {"desc": "Text falls like rain", "prompt": "The entire block's background is covered with vertical columns of kana text falling continuously from top to bottom like rain, each column at a different speed (about 3–5 seconds to fall), a few columns in an accent color and the rest in low-contrast tones, for a fantastical background feel.", "tag": "Fantasy · Background", "style": "Flowing Background", "txt": "あいうえおかきくけこさしすせそたちつてとなにぬねのはひふへほまみむめもやゆよらりるれろ"}, "12": {"desc": "Magnifies text with a magnifying glass", "prompt": "A circular magnifying glass moves back and forth, left and right, across the text; the text inside the lens is enlarged about 1.5x and switches to an accent color, while the text outside the lens is fainter; the magnifying glass has a handle. About 6 seconds per round trip, with an explanatory / discovery feel.", "tag": "Explainer · Discovery", "style": "Textured Fill", "txt": "Magnified"}, "13": {"desc": "Decodes from gibberish into real text", "prompt": "The text starts as constantly jumping gibberish (katakana, symbols and numbers), then decodes from left to right, character by character, into the correct text and switches to an accent color, pauses, then starts over. A pixel dot-matrix font, with a hacker sci-fi feel.", "tag": "Hacker · SF", "style": "Text Switching", "txt": "Decoded"}, "14": {"desc": "Text topples like dominoes", "prompt": "Each character pivots on its bottom-right corner and topples to the right in sequence by about 72 degrees, falling in a chain like dominoes, then all stand back up together after a pause. There is a floor line beneath the text. About 3.2 seconds per cycle.", "tag": "Humor · Chain Reaction", "style": "Dissipating Exit", "txt": "Dominoes"}, "15": {"desc": "A gradient flows through the text", "prompt": "The text is filled with a multi-color gradient that keeps flowing from left to right inside the letters. Large bold type, about 3 seconds per flow cycle, with a fashionable headline feel.", "tag": "Title · Trendy", "style": "Textured Fill", "txt": "Flowing Colors"}, "16": {"desc": "Rings of text rotate in opposite directions", "prompt": "Two rings of circularly arranged text: the outer ring rotates slowly clockwise and the inner ring rotates faster counterclockwise, with the inner and outer rings distinguished by different tones. The outer ring takes about 9 seconds per revolution and the inner ring about 6 seconds, with a hypnotic logo feel.", "tag": "Logo · Hypnotic", "style": "3D Spatial Rotation", "txt": "CIRCLE TEXT ✦ "}, "17": {"desc": "A reflection swaying on the water's surface", "prompt": "Below the text is a thin horizontal line; beneath the line is an upside-down reflection that is semi-transparent and fades out as it goes down, continually tilting and swaying side to side like ripples on water, while the text above also floats slightly. A calm night-scene feel.", "tag": "Nightscape · Calm", "style": "Textured Fill", "txt": "Water"}, "18": {"desc": "Text bounces letter by letter", "prompt": "Each character in sequence squashes flat, springs up, lands and squashes and rebounds again, with the squash-and-stretch elasticity of a small ball, only one character jumping at a time. About 2.2 seconds per cycle, with a cute MV feel.", "tag": "Cute · MV", "style": "Letter-by-Letter Motion Canva Style Canva Bounce Bounce", "txt": "Bouncy Letters"}, "19": {"desc": "Text flutters like a flag", "prompt": "There is a flagpole at the left side of the text; each character flips in 3D and tilts in sequence, forming a wave like a flag fluttering in the wind. About 1.3 seconds per wave, with a powerful cheering feel.", "tag": "Powerful · Cheering", "style": "Letter-by-Letter Motion", "txt": "Fluttering Flag"}, "20": {"desc": "Gravity reverses and it bounces upward", "prompt": "Each character first accelerates as it “falls” upward to the top and flips upside down, pauses, then drops back into place and flips upright, with a small bounce on landing, the characters staggered in sequence from each other. About 3 seconds per cycle.", "tag": "Surprise · SF", "style": "Letter-by-Letter Motion", "txt": "Gravity Flip"}, "21": {"desc": "Text is pulled in as if by a magnet", "prompt": "The text starts spread far apart, blurred and semi-transparent, then, as if pulled in by a magnet, accelerates toward the center, overshoots slightly, and snaps into place; after a pause it spreads apart again. The last two characters use an accent color as the focal point. About 2.8 seconds per cycle.", "tag": "Focus · Logo", "style": "Impact Entrance", "txt": "Drawn In"}, "22": {"desc": "A grid of text expands with a wave", "prompt": "The same character is arranged in an 8×4 grid, expanding in sequence in rings from the center outward, brightening, then shrinking and dimming again, forming a pulsing ripple. About 1.8 seconds per wave, with a rhythmic background feel.", "tag": "Background · Rhythm", "style": "Flowing Background", "txt": "Pulse"}, "23": {"desc": "Thin text gradually grows bolder", "prompt": "The text slowly changes from an extremely thin font weight to the heaviest font weight, pauses, then returns to thin again (a variable-weight font is required). About 3 seconds per cycle, emphasizing the sense of transformation.", "tag": "Emphasis · Change", "style": "Textured Fill", "txt": "Bolder"}, "24": {"desc": "The same character opens out like a fan", "prompt": "The same character is copied 7 times and stacked together, opening out into a fan shape pivoting below the character, pausing, then folding closed again. The center copy is opaque and the rest are semi-transparent. About 3 seconds per cycle, with a Japanese-style entrance feel.", "tag": "Japanese Style · Entrance", "style": "3D Spatial Rotation", "txt": "Fan"}, "25": {"desc": "A small ball bounces, lighting up each character", "prompt": "A small glowing ball jumps to the right above the text, character by character; each time it lands on a character, that character lights up from dim with a glow, like karaoke subtitles. About 0.38 seconds per character; after jumping through the whole line, it starts again.", "tag": "Song · Subtitles", "style": "Letter-by-Letter Motion", "txt": "Bouncing Ball"}, "26": {"desc": "Swings like a pendulum from a point above", "prompt": "Each character has a small dot at its top, and the character swings left and right like a pendulum from that pivot point by about ±14 degrees, with each character's swinging offset from the others. About 1.7 seconds per swing, lazy and cute.", "tag": "Cute · Lazy", "style": "Letter-by-Letter Motion", "txt": "Swaying"}, "27": {"desc": "Turns into blocks, dissolves away, then restores", "prompt": "The text is covered with small squares on top of it; the squares appear randomly, one by one, to hide the text, then disappear one by one to bring the text back, with a few accent-colored squares mixed in, like a pixel dissolve. About 3 seconds per cycle, with a digital feel.", "tag": "Digital", "style": "Dissipating Exit", "txt": "Pixelated"}, "28": {"desc": "Switches words inside a ring", "prompt": "The character inside the rounded square at the center switches in sequence (e.g., Spring → Summer → Autumn → Winter), each switch with an up-and-down flipping motion, while a ring of text around it keeps rotating slowly. One switch about every 1.3 seconds.", "tag": "Time · Seasons", "style": "Text Switching", "txt": "春夏秋冬"}, "29": {"desc": "Races past trailing afterimages", "prompt": "The text rushes at high speed from outside the left of the screen into the center, leaning in italics, stops briefly, then rushes out to the right, dragging 4 layers of semi-transparent blurred afterimages behind it, while horizontal speed lines flash across the background. About 2.6 seconds per cycle, with a sense of racing speed.", "tag": "Speed · Racing", "style": "Flowing Background", "txt": "Racing"}, "30": {"desc": "Checkerboard text flips in a wave", "prompt": "The same character is arranged in a 10×4 checkerboard grid, with dark and light blocks alternating, flipping around the Y axis in sequence from top-left to bottom-right, forming a diagonal tile-flipping wave. About 2.6 seconds per cycle, with a patterned background feel.", "tag": "Pattern · Background", "style": "Flowing Background", "txt": "Text"}, "31": {"desc": "Text races along an ∞ track", "prompt": "Each character runs in sequence along a dashed “∞”-shaped track, turning to follow its direction of travel, linked head-to-tail like a little convoy. About 4.5 seconds per lap, with a joyful racing feel.", "tag": "Racing · Joyful", "style": "Flowing Background", "txt": "Rolling"}, "32": {"desc": "Text swaps positions, then lines up neatly", "prompt": "Each character of the text swaps positions randomly with a little bounce and tilt; after shuffling several times in a row, it returns to its place and lines up neatly, pauses, then starts shuffling again. Each swap takes about 0.6 seconds, with a game-puzzle feel.", "tag": "Game · Puzzle", "style": "Letter-by-Letter Motion", "txt": "Shuffled"}, "33": {"desc": "Text rotates along a spiral", "prompt": "Text is arranged along a spiral line, gradually growing larger from small characters at the center outward; the whole vortex keeps rotating, and the characters' opacity alternates between bright and dark in turn. About 9 seconds per revolution, with a fantastical drawn-in feel.", "tag": "Fantasy · Drawn In", "style": "3D Spatial Rotation", "txt": "Spiral"}, "34": {"desc": "Shakes, then gradually settles", "prompt": "The text first shakes violently left, right, up and down and rotates; the shaking gradually gets smaller until it finally settles and stops, pauses for a while, then starts shaking again. About 2.4 seconds per cycle, with a startled, tense feel.", "tag": "Scary · Tense", "style": "Letter-by-Letter Motion", "txt": "Trembling"}, "35": {"desc": "Text stretches vertically into a wave", "prompt": "With its base at the bottom, each character stretches vertically in sequence to about 1.7x and then shrinks back, while narrowing horizontally at the same time, forming an elastic wave; the last character uses an accent color. About 1.3 seconds per wave, with a pop-music feel.", "tag": "Pop · Music", "style": "Letter-by-Letter Motion", "txt": "Stretchy Wave"}, "36": {"desc": "Ink bleeds into shape", "prompt": "The text is like ink dropped on paper: it starts as a blurred, bleeding blob of ink and gradually converges into a clear, sharp character shape, pauses, then bleeds out and disappears, with each character staggered in sequence. About 3.4 seconds per cycle, with a Japanese-style handwritten feel.", "tag": "Japanese Style · Handwritten Feel", "style": "Textured Fill", "txt": "Ink Bleed"}, "37": {"desc": "Scattered text gathers together", "prompt": "Each character of the text flies in from all over the screen with rotation, blur and enlargement, gathering one by one into its correct position and sharpening into focus, pauses, then scatters apart again. About 3.2 seconds per cycle, with a title-intro feel.", "tag": "Headline · Intro", "style": "Impact Entrance", "txt": "Gather"}, "38": {"desc": "Different fonts light up in sequence", "prompt": "8 characters are arranged in a 4×2 grid, each cell using a different font (sans-serif, serif, dot-matrix, rounded, brush, and so on), lighting up inverted and enlarging slightly one cell at a time in sequence, then dimming back down. About 3.2 seconds per cycle.", "tag": "Font Specimen · Design", "style": "Textured Fill", "txt": "愛夢光風花月海空"}, "39": {"desc": "Text crumbles and falls", "prompt": "Each character first tilts slightly, then falls downward in sequence as if crumbling, accelerating under gravity, rotating and fading out, then drops back from above into its original place to reassemble. About 3.4 seconds per cycle, with an ending feel.", "tag": "Ending · Twist", "style": "Dissipating Exit", "txt": "Crumble"}, "40": {"desc": "Floats light and airy", "prompt": "Each character floats slowly up, down, left and right at a different speed and rotates slightly, with a soft glow, like a feather drifting lightly. About 3–4.5 seconds per cycle for each character, with a soothing, dreamy feel.", "tag": "Healing · Dreamy", "style": "Letter-by-Letter Motion", "txt": "Fluffy"}, "41": {"desc": "A word pops out with a thump", "prompt": "The text rapidly pops out from 0, enlarges to 1.25x, then returns to its original size, while a ring of short lines radiates outward from the center, flying apart and disappearing. About 1.8 seconds per cycle, emphasizing the highlight.", "tag": "Emphasis · Highlight", "style": "Impact Entrance Canva Style Canva Pop Pop Out", "txt": "Impact"}, "42": {"desc": "Letters slam in one by one", "prompt": "The text slams down into place one character at a time from above at large size, each character squashing slightly and rebounding as it lands, spaced about 0.2 seconds apart in sequence; after all have appeared, they fade out together. About 3 seconds per cycle.", "tag": "Rhythm·Lyrics", "style": "Impact Entrance", "txt": "Slam Down"}, "43": {"desc": "Stamped on one by one like a seal", "prompt": "Two stamped texts with thick borders slam down diagonally with a bang from 2.4x size, settling after shrinking back slightly, the stamp faces with a slightly distressed texture, the two stamps coming down in sequence. About 2.8 seconds per cycle.", "tag": "Announcement·Decision", "style": "Impact Entrance Canva Style Canva Stomp Smash", "txt": "Approved"}, "44": {"desc": "Flies out from deep inside, trailing afterimages behind it", "prompt": "The text rushes forward at high speed from deep in the frame (tiny and blurred), overshooting slightly as it enlarges before rebounding into place, trailing 4 layers of semi-transparent afterimages behind it. About 2.2 seconds per cycle, with a strong opening emphasis.", "tag": "Opening·Emphasis", "style": "Impact Entrance", "txt": "Breakthrough"}, "45": {"desc": "Words fly in one by one and stack up", "prompt": "Three lines of words fly in with rotation from the left, right, and below respectively, stacking in sequence into a centered layout, each line at a different font size with the middle line in an accent color; after lingering, they fade out together. About 3.4 seconds per cycle, with an MV lyric feel.", "tag": "MV·Lyrics", "style": "Impact Entrance", "txt": "Through the Night Let's Go"}, "46": {"desc": "Dives into the letters, connects to the next word", "prompt": "A word scales up from small to normal size, then accelerates and enlarges until it fills the frame and fades out, like the camera diving into the letters; the next word then appears from far away to follow. About 1.2 seconds per word.", "tag": "Transition·Sense of Speed", "style": "Text Switching", "txt": "Into the Words Next"}, "47": {"desc": "Squashes flat like rubber, then swaps the word", "prompt": "The text squashes flat into a line like rubber, then springs up tall and rebounds into place; after pausing, it squashes flat again, swapping to the next word at its flattest point. About 1.5 seconds per cycle, an elastic switch.", "tag": "Elastic·Switching", "style": "Per-Character Motion", "txt": "Rebound Elastic"}, "48": {"desc": "Huge text crosses the screen, one fast and one slow", "prompt": "Text at an oversized scale (larger than the frame) continuously drifts slowly from right to left across the frame, while a thin strip at the bottom carries small text sliding faster in the opposite direction. The large text takes about 9 seconds per cycle, giving a distant background feel.", "tag": "Background·Distant View", "style": "Flowing Background", "txt": "Night in Taipei"}, "49": {"desc": "Vertical text flows in opposite directions", "prompt": "Multiple columns of vertical text, thick and thin columns alternating, adjacent columns flowing in opposite directions — one up, one down — in a serif (Mincho) typeface. The large columns are slow (about 11 seconds), the small columns fast (about 6 seconds), an Eastern sense of stillness and motion.", "tag": "Eastern·Stillness and Motion", "style": "Flowing Background", "txt": "Silence"}, "50": {"desc": "Diagonal bands, text running in reverse", "prompt": "Two diagonal text bands cross through the frame, distinguished by different background colors, the repeated text on the bands continuously sliding in opposite directions, the bands casting shadows. About 7–9 seconds per cycle, with a playful transition feel.", "tag": "Transition·Playful", "style": "Flowing Background", "txt": "Before Dawn"}, "51": {"desc": "Text flows along a wavy line", "prompt": "A wide, semi-transparent wavy ribbon crosses the frame, and text continuously flows forward along the wavy curve. It flows through a segment in about 2.4 seconds, with a decorative, musical rhythm.", "tag": "Decoration·Soundtrack Feel", "style": "Flowing Background", "txt": "Move to the Beat"}, "52": {"desc": "Bands with different fonts and speeds layered together", "prompt": "Four horizontal marquee bands layered together, each with a different font, font size, speed, and direction, with thin divider lines between the bands. Speeds vary from 5–11 seconds per cycle, like a street bulletin board.", "tag": "Announcement·Street", "style": "Flowing Background", "txt": "Limited Sale New Arrivals Pre-order Last Day"}, "53": {"desc": "Three layers of vertical text flowing together", "prompt": "Three layers of vertical text flowing vertically: the back layer is small, very faint, and fast; the middle layer is semi-transparent at medium speed; the front layer is large, opaque, and slow, creating a parallax depth of field, in a serif (Mincho) typeface. A nighttime Eastern feel.", "tag": "Night·Eastern", "style": "Flowing Background", "txt": "Rainy Night Street Lights"}, "54": {"desc": "Taped text crossed into an X", "prompt": "Two caution tapes with thick borders cross into an X shape, the repeated text on the tapes sliding in opposite directions, with shadows. About 6–8 seconds per cycle, with a warning, cordoned-off feel.", "tag": "Warning·Street", "style": "Flowing Background", "txt": "No Entry"}, "55": {"desc": "Pass through the middle of the text", "prompt": "Multiple layered copies of the same word continuously scale up from tiny at the center, growing larger until they rush out of the frame and fade, one layer after another, like passing through a text tunnel, adjacent layers alternating between two color tones. About 3.6 seconds per layer.", "tag": "Opening·Sci-Fi", "style": "3D Spatial Rotation", "txt": "Pass Through"}, "56": {"desc": "Floor and walls are all text, moving forward all the way", "prompt": "A corridor in 3D perspective, its floor, ceiling, and left and right walls all covered in repeated text, the text continuously flowing toward the viewer, with a dark gradient at the vanishing point in the center. About 6 seconds per cycle, an immersive forward-moving feel.", "tag": "Immersive·MV", "style": "3D Spatial Rotation", "txt": "Forward"}, "57": {"desc": "Text cylinders rotate in opposite directions", "prompt": "Three 3D cylinders made of text (the same character ringing a full circle), rotating along a horizontal axis, adjacent cylinders in opposite directions, the middle one in an accent color. About 4 seconds per revolution, with a three-dimensional logo feel.", "tag": "3D·Logo", "style": "3D Spatial Rotation", "txt": "Spin Around"}, "58": {"desc": "Rings of text rush toward you", "prompt": "Multiple rings made of text scale up one by one from tiny at the center, rushing toward the viewer and fading out, each ring itself also rotating, adjacent rings in opposite directions. About 4.2 seconds per ring.", "tag": "Opening·Sci-Fi", "style": "3D Spatial Rotation", "txt": "TUNNEL•"}, "59": {"desc": "A single word orbits with depth of field", "prompt": "Text circles along an elliptical dashed orbit, growing larger and sharper as it comes to the front and smaller and fainter as it goes to the back, creating depth of field. About 5 seconds per orbit, with a logo title feel.", "tag": "Logo·Title", "style": "3D Spatial Rotation", "txt": "Orbit"}, "60": {"desc": "A cube with text on four faces flips vertically", "prompt": "A 3D cube with one character written on each of its four faces flips 90 degrees around a horizontal axis each time to switch to the next face, pausing after each flip, at a slightly tilted viewing angle, the cube with thick borders. About 1.5 seconds per face.", "tag": "Switching·3D", "style": "Text Switching", "txt": "Spring Summer Fall Winter"}, "61": {"desc": "The thickness of 3D letters rotates a full turn", "prompt": "Thick 3D extruded text, its front brighter and its sides built from multiple layers of shading from dark to light to form the thickness; the whole set of letters slowly rotates a full turn around a vertical axis, letting the side thickness be seen. About 5 seconds per revolution.", "tag": "Title", "style": "3D Spatial Rotation", "txt": "3D"}, "62": {"desc": "Flips into place like a station timetable", "prompt": "Each character sits in a split-flap cell (with a divider line in the middle) and, like a station timetable, rapidly flips through many random characters, stopping in sequence from left to right on the correct character; after lingering, it flips again. The flipping is fast, with everything settled in about 1.5 seconds.", "tag": "Retro·Station", "style": "Text Switching", "txt": "On Time"}, "63": {"desc": "Cards flip over one by one to change the text", "prompt": "Each character is a card that flips in sequence around the Y axis, front and back in contrasting color schemes; after flipping into another set of text it lingers, then flips back. About 3.4 seconds per cycle, with an announcement-switching feel.", "tag": "Switching·Announcement", "style": "Text Switching", "txt": "Sleepless Night"}, "64": {"desc": "Typed out character by character, then replaced", "prompt": "Text appears over two lines character by character like a typewriter, with a blinking cursor behind it; after finishing and lingering, it is quickly deleted character by character and the next sentence is typed. Serif (Mincho) typeface, the second line fainter, typing at about 0.14 seconds per character.", "tag": "Story·Subtitles", "style": "Text Switching Canva Style Canva Typewriter Typewriter", "txt": "Before Dawn Goodbye"}, "65": {"desc": "Reels spin and come to a stop", "prompt": "Each character sits in a slot-machine reel window (the windows have inner shadows at the top and bottom); the reels rapidly scroll upward through many random characters, then slow down and stop in sequence from left to right on the result characters (with a slight rebound); after lingering, they spin again. About 4 seconds per cycle.", "tag": "Result Reveal", "style": "Text Switching", "txt": "Great Fortune"}, "66": {"desc": "Numbers scroll upward and increase", "prompt": "For numbers such as 'Cumulative total: 12,480 people', each digit sits in a small cell, the numbers scrolling upward and incrementing like an odometer, with a slight rebound. It increases about once every 1 second.", "tag": "Results·Numbers", "style": "Text Switching", "txt": "Total"}, "67": {"desc": "News headlines swap one for another", "prompt": "A 'Breaking News' label stays fixed on the left, while news headlines in the frame on the right slide in from below as the old headline slides out upward, one replacing another. A new headline about every 1.6 seconds.", "tag": "Breaking News·Commentary", "style": "Text Switching", "txt": "Fully Free Live Tonight 3 Days Only"}, "68": {"desc": "Electronic text made of dots", "prompt": "Text made of a dot matrix like an electronic billboard, continuously scrolling from right to left, with clear contrast between lit and unlit dots. Medium scrolling speed, with a retro tech feel.", "tag": "Retro·Tech", "style": "Flowing Background", "txt": "Latest News •"}, "69": {"desc": "Hollow text fills up line by line", "prompt": "The frame is covered with multiple lines of repeated outlined hollow text, each line slowly shifting horizontally in a different direction, and filling with color line by line from top to bottom before returning to hollow. About 3.2 seconds per cycle, with a textured MV feel.", "tag": "Texture·MV", "style": "Flowing Background", "txt": "Storm and Fury"}, "70": {"desc": "Large text is cut into several offset slices", "prompt": "The large text is normally still, but occasionally it suddenly cuts into 6 horizontal slices, each slice offset randomly left or right with chromatic aberration (RGB split), flashing once before recovering, at an irregular frequency. The glitch flickers about every 0.1 seconds, with an impactful MV feel.", "tag": "Impact·MV", "style": "Dissipating Exit", "txt": "Glitch"}, "71": {"desc": "Text becomes a window, stripes flow through inside", "prompt": "The text is like a window, filled inside with diagonal stripes alternating in two colors, the stripes continuously flowing sideways. Bold typeface, flowing through one stripe cycle in about 1 second, with a playful festival feel.", "tag": "Playful·Festival", "style": "Textured Fill", "txt": "Festival"}, "72": {"desc": "A long, long shadow turns a full circle", "prompt": "A very long flat shadow trails behind the text, the shadow's direction continuously rotating a full circle around the text. About 7 seconds per revolution, in a flat design style.", "tag": "Flat Style", "style": "Textured Fill", "txt": "Light and Shadow"}, "73": {"desc": "Hollow text is slowly filled with liquid", "prompt": "At first there is only outlined hollow text; liquid slowly fills the letters from bottom to top; after filling and lingering, it empties and starts over. About 3.4 seconds per cycle, with a fresh MV feel.", "tag": "Fresh·MV", "style": "Textured Fill", "txt": "Full"}, "74": {"desc": "A highlighter sweeps across behind the text", "prompt": "For text on a card, a highlighter line sweeps from left to right behind the lower half of the letters, lingers, then fades out. The sweep takes about 1 second, the whole cycle about 3 seconds, with an emphasis-and-commentary feel.", "tag": "Emphasis·Commentary", "style": "Textured Fill", "txt": "Power of Words"}, "75": {"desc": "A diagonal line sweeps across and the two areas swap", "prompt": "The frame is divided into two areas by a diagonal line, the two areas' background and text colors in contrast with each other; the diagonal line sweeps across the frame from left to right, swapping the text's two color schemes. One sweep about every 3.4 seconds, with a title-switching feel.", "tag": "Switching·Title", "style": "Text Switching Canva Style Canva Block Block", "txt": "Invert"}, "76": {"desc": "Each character slides up from below a mask", "prompt": "The text is split into individual characters, each placed inside a clipping mask, sliding up in sequence from below the mask (about 0.06 seconds between characters, with strong deceleration); after lingering, they slide out upward. (GSAP: SplitText with type chars + mask, from yPercent: 110, ease power4.out, stagger)", "tag": "SplitText", "style": "Canva Style Canva Ascend Rise Rise", "txt": "Rise Letter by Letter"}, "77": {"desc": "Scrambled characters gradually resolve into the correct text", "prompt": "The text starts as a string of constantly jittering scrambled characters (katakana, symbols, numbers) and gradually resolves into the correct text from left to right, the scrambled characters and the resolved ones distinguished by different colors; after lingering, it scrambles again. Dot-matrix typeface. (GSAP: ScrambleTextPlugin, revealDelay, speed, newClass)", "tag": "ScrambleText", "style": "", "txt": "Decoded"}, "78": {"desc": "Type, delete, swap to the next sentence", "prompt": "Like a typewriter, type out a sentence character by character, the cursor blinking behind it; after lingering for about 1 second, delete it character by character from the end, then type the next sentence, cycling through three sentences. (GSAP: TextPlugin typing + a timeline chaining the deletions)", "tag": "TextPlugin", "style": "Canva Style Canva Typewriter Typewriter", "txt": "Typing with GSAP"}, "79": {"desc": "Letters fall from the sky and wobble elastically", "prompt": "Each character drops from above the frame in random order, with random rotation, wobbling elastically like jelly as it lands before settling into place; after lingering, they all drop down and fade out together. (GSAP: SplitText chars, ease elastic.out(1,0.35), stagger from random)", "tag": "Stagger·Elastic", "style": "Canva Style Canva Bounce Bounce", "txt": "Bouncing Drop"}, "80": {"desc": "Each character enters flipping around the X axis", "prompt": "Each character enters with a 3D flip around the X axis (flipping from the back to the front, with a slight rebound), spaced 0.07 seconds apart in sequence; after lingering, it flips forward and disappears. (GSAP: SplitText chars, rotationX, transformOrigin with Z depth, ease back.out)", "tag": "SplitText·3D", "style": "", "txt": "Flipping In"}, "81": {"desc": "Letters fly in from everywhere, then scatter apart", "prompt": "Each character flies in from random positions all over the frame, with random rotation and size, decelerating strongly to assemble into the text; after lingering, it bursts apart to random positions. (GSAP: SplitText chars, \"random(-400,400)\" function-based values, ease expo, stagger from random)", "tag": "Stagger random", "style": "", "txt": "Scatter and Gather"}, "82": {"desc": "Cells scale in waves outward from the center", "prompt": "The same character is arranged in a 10×5 grid, shrinking, rotating, and fading in waves outward from the center, then enlarging and rotating back inward from the edges, forming a ripple. (GSAP: stagger { grid: [5,10], from: \"center\" / \"edges\", amount: 1 })", "tag": "Grid stagger", "style": "", "txt": "Motion"}, "83": {"desc": "A fixed prefix, with the word after it rotating through replacements", "prompt": "A fixed prefix \"We make\", with the word after it rotating inside a mask: each new word slides up letter by letter from below, stays for a while, then slides up and out, followed by the next word; the rotating words use the accent color. (GSAP: SplitText chars + mask, a timeline chains each word in sequence)", "tag": "SplitText mask", "style": "", "txt": "Design Animation Interaction Experience"}, "84": {"desc": "Numbers count up in a rolling fashion while a progress bar fills in sync", "prompt": "The large number below the label quickly counts up from 0 to 128,450, slowing down as it gets closer to the end, while the progress bar below fills in sync; after a pause it fades out and starts over, with the number in tabular figures. (GSAP: tween an object's value + onUpdate writes it with toLocaleString, ease power3.out)", "tag": "Tween Value", "style": "", "txt": "Downloads"}, "85": {"desc": "Letters are pushed away as the cursor approaches", "prompt": "When the cursor comes near the text, nearby letters are pushed outward and switch to the accent color — the closer the cursor, the farther they are pushed — and when the cursor leaves, they smoothly return to their original positions. (GSAP: SplitText chars, each letter's x/y controlled with gsap.quickTo, with the push force calculated from the cursor distance)", "tag": "quickTo", "style": "", "txt": "Come Closer"}, "86": {"desc": "Lines flip up one by one from beneath a mask", "prompt": "Multiple lines of text flip up one by one from beneath their own masks, with a slight rotation, the last line in the accent color; a thin line below is drawn from left to right, and after a pause the whole block sweeps upward and away. (GSAP: each line wrapped in overflow hidden, from yPercent:115, stagger 0.14)", "tag": "Mask·Stagger", "style": "", "txt": "Animation Brings Interfaces to Life"}, "87": {"desc": "Squashes flat on landing, stretches on rebound", "prompt": "The text drops from above, squashing flat like rubber when it lands and stretching out as it rebounds, bouncing a few times before coming to rest, while the ground shadow scales with its height. (GSAP: CustomBounce.create generates two eases, bounce and squash, applied to y and to scaleX/scaleY respectively)", "tag": "CustomBounce", "style": "", "txt": "Bounce Bounce Bounce"}, "88": {"desc": "A hand-drawn circle and underline are drawn in", "prompt": "A hand-drawn-style line draws a circle around the key text, then draws an underline beneath it; after a pause, the lines retract in the direction of their starting point, with round line caps. (GSAP: DrawSVGPlugin, drawSVG \"0%\"→\"100%\", then to \"100% 100%\")", "tag": "DrawSVG", "style": "", "txt": "Key Point Here"}, "89": {"desc": "Circle, star, heart and cloud morph into each other", "prompt": "A block of color smoothly morphs between a circle, a star, a heart and a cloud, changing to a different color with each morph, while the whole thing rotates slowly. (GSAP: MorphSVGPlugin, morphSVG switches the paths, ease expo.inOut)", "tag": "MorphSVG", "style": "", "txt": ""}, "90": {"desc": "A paper plane flies along a curve, turning as it goes", "prompt": "A paper plane flies across the screen along a dashed curve with a loop, its nose turning to follow the path's direction, and starts over after it flies off-screen. (GSAP: MotionPathPlugin, path/align specify the SVG path, autoRotate:true)", "tag": "MotionPath", "style": "", "txt": ""}, "91": {"desc": "Smoothly rearranges between a grid and a single row", "prompt": "8 blocks switch between two layouts — a \"4×2 grid\" and \"a single row\" — while their order is randomly shuffled at the same time; each block smoothly slides to its new position and new size. (GSAP: Flip.getState to record → change the class and DOM order → Flip.from to tween)", "tag": "Flip", "style": "", "txt": ""}, "92": {"desc": "Fades in when scrolled to, with the progress bar in sync", "prompt": "In a scrollable region, the progress bar at the top fills in proportion to scrolling; each paragraph of text fades in from the left when it is scrolled to 85% of the viewport, and fades out again when scrolling back up. (GSAP: ScrollTrigger toggleActions \"play none none reverse\", the progress bar uses scrub:true)", "tag": "ScrollTrigger", "style": "", "txt": "Scroll Reveal"}, "93": {"desc": "Scroll down, and the content slides left", "prompt": "When scrolling down, a whole row of work cards instead slides horizontally to the left, so that scrolling to the very bottom lands exactly on the last card, like a horizontal portfolio showcase. (GSAP: ScrollTrigger pin (or sticky) + scrub, the x travel distance = track width − viewport width)", "tag": "ScrollTrigger scrub", "style": "", "txt": "Horizontal Scroll Showcase Works"}, "94": {"desc": "Far, middle and near layers move at different speeds", "prompt": "When scrolling, large background text in the far layer, dots in the middle layer and the title in the near layer move up and down at different speeds — the near layer fastest, the far layer slowest — creating depth-of-field parallax. (GSAP: one timeline bound to a ScrollTrigger with scrub, the three layers each set to a different yPercent range)", "tag": "ScrollTrigger scrub", "style": "", "txt": "Parallax"}, "95": {"desc": "The button is pulled toward the cursor and springs back", "prompt": "When the cursor approaches the button, the button is pulled toward the cursor's direction, while the text inside the button moves less, creating a layered effect, and it switches to the accent color at the same time; when the cursor leaves, it returns to its original position with elasticity. (GSAP: gsap.quickTo controls x/y, ease elastic.out(1,0.4))", "tag": "quickTo·Elastic", "style": "", "txt": "Press Me"}, "96": {"desc": "Trailing dots and an inverted-color circle", "prompt": "Behind the cursor follows a string of trailing dots, from fast to slow, plus a larger circle laid over the text in an inverted-color blend mode, so the text turns inverted in color as it passes over. (GSAP: multiple gsap.quickTo with different durations, the large circle uses mix-blend-mode:difference)", "tag": "quickTo", "style": "", "txt": "Follow the Cursor"}, "97": {"desc": "Cards can be dragged and tossed with inertia", "prompt": "Several cards can be dragged with the mouse or a finger; on release they glide with inertia according to the toss velocity, decelerating and bouncing back at the boundaries, and the card being dragged floats to the top layer. (GSAP: Draggable.create { bounds, inertia:true, edgeResistance }, requires InertiaPlugin)", "tag": "Draggable·Inertia", "style": "", "txt": "Try Dragging"}, "98": {"desc": "Cards are dealt from the bottom and unfold into a fan", "prompt": "5 cards are dealt in sequence from the bottom of the screen, unfolding into an angled fan with a slight rebound, and after a pause they are gathered back to the bottom, starting from the last card. (GSAP: timeline + stagger, xPercent / rotation use function values (i)=>(i-2)*115)", "tag": "Timeline·Stagger", "style": "", "txt": "Spring Summer Autumn Winter Snow"}, "99": {"desc": "A burst of confetti affected by gravity", "prompt": "As the text elastically scales up, a large handful of paper pieces bursts out from below; the pieces fall in gravity-driven parabolas, rotating and fading out toward the end, once every 2 seconds. (GSAP: Physics2DPlugin velocity / angle / gravity, randomized with random)", "tag": "Physics2D", "style": "", "txt": "Congrats"}, "100": {"desc": "The wheel or dragging speeds up the marquee and tilts it", "prompt": "Two lines of infinite marquee (one solid, one hollow outline, running in opposite directions); when the user scrolls the wheel or drags, they speed up and tilt according to the direction, and after stopping they slowly return to their original speed. (GSAP: Observer obtains velocityY, adjusting tween.timeScale and skewX)", "tag": "Observer", "style": "", "txt": "Scroll to Speed Up"}, "101": {"desc": "Side navigation dots light up with scrolling; click one to jump to that section", "prompt": "Scroll navigation / side navigation dots (Scroll Spy / Dot Navigation, also called anchor navigation or page progress navigation): a row of small dots is fixed on the right side of the page, each dot corresponding to one section; whichever section is scrolled to, its corresponding dot enlarges and fills with the accent color, with a pill label showing that section's name floating out beside it; between the dots there is a thin track, and the progress bar inside the track grows downward in proportion to the whole page's scrolling; clicking any dot smoothly scrolls to that section, and hovering the mouse over a dot also shows its name. The sections alternate between light and dark background shades. (GSAP: one ScrollTrigger per section, start \"top center\", end \"bottom center\", onToggle toggles active; the progress bar uses scaleY with scrub:true; clicking uses gsap.to(scroller,{scrollTop}) or ScrollToPlugin)", "tag": "ScrollTrigger", "style": "Scroll Navigation Side Navigation Dots Anchor Navigation Page Progress Navigation Scroll Spy Navigation Dot Navigation", "txt": "About Works Services Contact"}, "102": {"desc": "On hover the letters roll up one by one, the button inverts, and the arrow turns", "prompt": "A pill-shaped button, with text on the left and a circular arrow on the right. When the mouse moves over it, each letter of the button text rolls upward in sequence (each letter delayed by about 0.035 seconds), with an identical copy of the text filling in from below; at the same time, the button's background and text colors swap to the accent scheme, the circle on the right also inverts its colors, and the arrow rotates to point up-right at 45 degrees; when the mouse leaves, everything rolls back in reverse. The whole thing takes about 0.55 seconds, with ease-in-out (cubic-bezier(.7,0,.2,1)). (CSS: each letter wrapped in a span, ::after{content:attr(data-t);top:100%} creates the second copy of the text, the outer layer has overflow:hidden, on :hover translateY(-100%), and transition-delay uses calc(var(--i)*.035s) to stagger the letters)", "tag": "CSS hover", "style": "Button hover Hover Rolling Text Roll Text Button Hover Stagger CTA", "txt": "View Works"}, "103": {"desc": "Spreads to fill from the point where the mouse entered, and retracts toward the exit point on leave", "prompt": "An outlined pill button. When the mouse moves in, an accent-colored circle enlarges starting from \"the exact point where the cursor entered the button\", spreading until it fills the whole button, while the text color switches at the same time to a color that contrasts with the fill; when the mouse moves out, the circle shrinks away centered on \"the point where the cursor left\", so the color retracts toward whichever side it exits from. About 0.55 seconds, ease-in-out. (How it works: the button has overflow:hidden; on pointerenter / pointerleave, getBoundingClientRect is used to calculate the cursor's coordinates inside the button and write them into the CSS variables --x and --y, the circle's diameter is taken as \"distance to the farthest corner × 2\" to ensure full coverage; the circle uses transform:scale(0→1) as a transition)", "tag": "CSS + JS", "style": "Button hover Direction-aware Spread Fill Ripple From Mouse Position Direction Aware Hover Fill Ripple Button CTA", "txt": "Contact Now"}, "104": {"desc": "A group of cards floats up in sequence from top-left to bottom-right, going from blurry to clear", "prompt": "Work cards in 3 columns × 2 rows (a thumbnail on top, a title and two lines of text below); on entrance, each card floats up from a state 30px below, at 95% size, blurred and transparent, becoming clear, in a sequence staggered diagonally from top-left to bottom-right (about 0.6 seconds in total); the thumbnail, title and text lines inside each card then catch up one by one with a slight extra delay; after a pause, they fade out upward in reverse, starting from the last card. Ease-out (power3.out). (GSAP: stagger { grid:[2,3], from:\"start\", amount:0.6 }, fromTo y / opacity / scale / filter:blur; on a real site, pair this with ScrollTrigger so it plays when scrolled into view, or use ScrollTrigger.batch to bring lists in in batches)", "tag": "Grid stagger", "style": "Card Group List Entrance In Sequence Staggered Emerge Fade In Stagger Fade Up Grid Reveal List Entrance", "txt": "Brand Website App Poster Packaging Illustration"}, "105": {"desc": "On hover the image tilts in 3D following the cursor, with layered parallax scenery, a glare, and a caption sliding out", "prompt": "An image card: when the mouse moves over the image, the whole image tilts in 3D in the direction of the cursor position (up to about ±10 degrees) and scales up slightly; the far, middle and near scenery inside the image shift in the opposite direction at different rates, forming parallax depth; a soft glare follows the cursor; at the same time, the caption text at the bottom (a small label + a title) slides up from below. When the mouse leaves, everything smoothly returns upright and the caption retracts. (GSAP: gsap.quickTo controls rotationX / rotationY / scale, the parent layer has perspective set; each layer is displaced with quickTo at a different coefficient; the glare uses a radial-gradient positioned with the CSS variables --gx and --gy; the caption uses a transform transition)", "tag": "quickTo·3D", "style": "Image Photo hover Hover 3D Tilt Parallax Glare Tilt Parallax Glare Image Hover Card", "txt": "Mountain Mist Sunset"}, "106": {"desc": "Several blurred glows drift and blend slowly, flowing like an aurora", "prompt": "In a Hero section background, place 3–4 large circular glows that overlap and blend into each other after heavy blurring, each slowly drifting, scaling up and down and swaying back and forth at a different speed (about 9–16 seconds), forming a gradient that keeps flowing like an aurora; the foreground title stays clear and readable. (CSS: each glow is a large circle + filter:blur + mix-blend-mode:screen, each set to a different animation-duration and a negative animation-delay, with animation-direction:alternate)", "tag": "CSS blur", "style": "Background Aurora Gradient Glow Aurora Mesh Gradient Blob Glow Hero Background", "txt": "Aurora"}, "107": {"desc": "A fine grid-line background, with the grid lines near the cursor lit up with a soft glow", "prompt": "The background of the whole section is a faint fine grid; the ring of grid lines around the cursor's position lights up in the accent color, with a soft glow, the lit area following the cursor and fading out naturally at the edges; when the cursor leaves, the lit area disappears. (How it works: two identical grid-line background layers, the upper layer in the accent color, then mask:radial-gradient(circle at var(--mx) var(--my)) reveals only the area near the cursor; --mx and --my are updated on mousemove)", "tag": "CSS mask", "style": "Background Grid Grid Lines Spotlight Cursor Glow Spotlight Grid Pattern Cursor Glow SaaS", "txt": "Spotlight"}, "108": {"desc": "Floating particles automatically connect when close; the cursor attracts nearby particles", "prompt": "Dozens of small particles in the background drift slowly and randomly, bouncing off the boundaries; when two particles are close enough they automatically connect with a line — the closer they are, the clearer the line, the farther, the fainter; when the cursor moves in, nearby particles are gently drawn toward it and connect to it, forming an effect like a constellation network. The foreground title stays clear. (Canvas 2D: requestAnimationFrame updates the positions every frame, lines are drawn by computing pairwise distances with opacity adjusted by distance; note the canvas size should be set according to devicePixelRatio)", "tag": "Canvas 2D", "style": "Background Particles Connecting Lines Network Constellation Particles Network Constellation particles.js Canvas", "txt": "Network"}, "109": {"desc": "A diagonal sheen sweeps across the button on a timer; on hover it speeds up and the button lifts", "prompt": "On a solid button there is a diagonal translucent highlight that quickly sweeps from left to right about every 2.4 seconds, like a reflection on metal or glass; when the mouse moves over it, the sheen sweeps faster, and the button lifts slightly while its shadow deepens at the same time. (CSS: the button has overflow:hidden, ::after creates a gradient highlight band with skewX(-20deg), and keyframes change its left position; :hover shortens the animation-duration and adds translateY)", "tag": "CSS hover", "style": "Button Sheen Reflection Light Sweep Flash Shine Sweep Glint Shimmer Button CTA", "txt": "Buy Now"}, "110": {"desc": "The gradient light on the button's border keeps rotating around it, with a soft outer glow", "prompt": "The border of a pill button is a ring of multicolored gradient light, and the gradient keeps rotating around the border (about 3 seconds per revolution), with a layer of blurred soft glow behind the border; inside the button are a solid background and text; when the mouse moves over it, the rotation speeds up. (CSS: @property registers the angle variable --ang, the background uses conic-gradient(from var(--ang)), and keyframes rotate --ang to 360deg; an inner span covers the middle so only the border shows; ::before duplicates the background and blurs it for the outer glow)", "tag": "@property", "style": "Button Border Gradient Rotation Glow Glow Border Conic Gradient Animated Border Button", "txt": "Get Started"}, "111": {"desc": "Clicking the heart makes it bounce and scale up, spraying small dots and a ring of light around it", "prompt": "When the \"Like\" button is clicked, the hollow heart instantly fills and bounces up from small to large, while 8 small dots spray outward from around the heart and a ring of light expands and disappears, and the number beside it goes +1; clicking again cancels it, the heart returns to hollow and the number goes −1. The whole thing takes about 0.5 seconds, with an elastic feedback feel. (CSS: toggling the .on class; the heart uses a scale bounce keyframes, the small dots use rotate(var(--r)) translateY to fly outward while shrinking and fading, the ring uses scale + opacity; before replaying, remove the class first and trigger a reflow)", "tag": "CSS keyframes", "style": "Button Like Favorite Heart Click Feedback Micro-interaction Like Heart Burst Micro-interaction Twitter", "txt": "Like"}, "112": {"desc": "On hover the card lifts and its shadow deepens, and the thumbnail zooms inside its frame", "prompt": "A row of work cards (a thumbnail on top, a title and a line of text below). When the mouse moves over a card, the card lifts up a little and a deeper, larger shadow appears, and the thumbnail slowly zooms to about 1.15× inside its original frame (the frame stays the same, the image is cropped); when the mouse leaves, it smoothly returns to its original position. About 0.45–0.6 seconds, ease-out. (CSS: the card transitions transform and box-shadow, on :hover translateY(-8px); the thumbnail's frame has overflow:hidden, and the inner image uses transform:scale(1.14))", "tag": "CSS hover", "style": "Card hover Lift Shadow Thumbnail Zoom Hover Lift Card Shadow Zoom Portfolio Product", "txt": "Brand Website Illustration"}, "113": {"desc": "As the cursor passes, the card's border and interior are lit by a pool of light", "prompt": "A row of understated cards: when the cursor moves near a card, the stretch of the card's border closest to the cursor is lit by a pool of light (in the accent color), and inside the card there is also a very faint glow following the cursor; the light only illuminates the area near the cursor and gets darker the farther away it is, so the edges of neighboring cards can also be seen faintly lit at the same time. (How it works: on mousemove, calculate the cursor's coordinates relative to each card and write them into --x and --y; ::before uses radial-gradient(circle at var(--x) var(--y)) with mask-composite to show only the border ring, and ::after creates the soft interior glow)", "tag": "radial-gradient", "style": "Card Glow Border Spotlight Cursor Glow Spotlight Card Glow Border Linear Vercel", "txt": "Design Development Marketing"}, "114": {"desc": "A skeleton is shown before the content loads; after a sheen sweeps across, the real content fades in", "prompt": "While the data is loading, the card first shows a low-contrast skeleton: a circular avatar, two text bars of different lengths, and a large image area, with a soft highlight continuously sweeping across the skeleton from left to right; when loading completes, the skeleton fades out, and the real avatar, title, time and image fade in while sliding slightly upward into place. (CSS: the skeleton elements use a linear-gradient highlight band + background-size:300%, with keyframes moving the background-position; when loading completes, a class is switched so the skeleton goes to opacity 0 and the content to opacity 1 + a translateY transition)", "tag": "Skeleton", "style": "Skeleton Loading Reading Placeholder Skeleton Loading Shimmer Placeholder Loader", "txt": "Let's Design Motion Together"}, "115": {"desc": "The image is uncovered from bottom to top, while scaling down from enlarged to its original size", "prompt": "When the image enters, its frame is uncovered from bottom to top like a curtain, while the picture inside the frame slowly scales down from about 1.35× to its original size, creating the layers of \"uncovering + camera pulling back\"; after a pause, it is then gathered up and disappears from bottom to top. The uncovering takes about 1.2 seconds, ease-in-out (cubic-bezier(.7,0,.2,1)). (CSS: the frame uses clip-path:inset() keyframes from inset(100% 0 0 0) to inset(0); the inner image uses transform:scale 1.35→1; on a real site, this can be played only when scrolled into view)", "tag": "clip-path", "style": "Image Photo Mask Reveal Entrance clip-path Image Reveal Mask Wipe Zoom", "txt": ""}, "116": {"desc": "Drag the handle in the middle to compare the difference between two images, left and right", "prompt": "Two images of the same size overlap, with a straight line and a circular handle (with left and right arrows) in the middle, BEFORE marked in the top-left corner and AFTER in the top-right; when the handle is dragged, the dividing line moves left and right with it, the left side showing the original image and the right side the edited image, making the differences easy to compare; when not operated, it can sway slowly left and right to hint that it is draggable. (How it works: the upper image uses clip-path:inset(0 0 0 var(--p)), on pointerdown/pointermove the cursor's proportion inside the frame is calculated and written into --p; the handle uses setPointerCapture to ensure dragging continues even when dragged outside the frame; on mobile, set touch-action:pan-y)", "tag": "clip-path·Drag", "style": "Image Comparison Contrast Before and After Slider Drag Before After Compare Slider Image Comparison", "txt": ""}, "117": {"desc": "When scrolling down, the navigation bar gets shorter, the Logo shrinks, and a frosted-glass background is added", "prompt": "The header navigation bar is fixed at the very top (sticky). At the top of the page the navigation bar is taller, the Logo is larger and the background is transparent; as soon as you scroll down past a certain distance, the navigation bar smoothly becomes shorter, the Logo shrinks, and a translucent frosted-glass background and a faint shadow appear; scrolling back to the top restores the original state. About a 0.35-second transition. (How it works: listen to scroll, and add a .shrink class when scrollY exceeds a certain value; CSS transitions padding, font-size, background and box-shadow, with the background using backdrop-filter:blur)", "tag": "Sticky", "style": "Navigation Bar Header Menu header navbar Scroll Shrink Sticky Frosted Glass Sticky Shrink Header On Scroll", "txt": "LOGO"}, "118": {"desc": "Notifications pop in and stack from the bottom-right corner in sequence, then slide out and disappear after a few seconds", "prompt": "When an operation completes, a notification pops up in the bottom-right corner of the screen (a checkmark in a circle icon on the left, a message in the middle, a \"just now\" time on the right), entering from below with a slight scale and elastic feel; a new notification stacks below, pushing the old ones up; at most 3 are shown at the same time, and each one slides out to the right and fades away after about 3.4 seconds, with the remaining notifications smoothly moving up to fill the gap. (CSS + JS: the notification wrapper uses display:grid + grid-template-rows 1fr→0fr to collapse the height so filling the gap is smooth; entrance uses keyframes translateY + scale; for exit, add an .out class and then remove the element)", "tag": "Toast", "style": "Notification Prompt Message Toast Pop-up Toast Notification Snackbar Alert Stack", "txt": "Changes Saved"}, "119": {"desc": "A small dot cursor expands into a circle with text in it when moved over a work", "prompt": "Hide the system cursor and use a small dot that follows the mouse instead (with a slight lag); when the cursor moves over a work thumbnail, the small dot smoothly expands into a circle about 3× larger, with prompt text such as \"VIEW\" appearing in the center of the circle, and the work itself shrinks slightly in response; when leaving the work, it shrinks back to a small dot and the text fades out. The expansion takes about 0.35 seconds, ease-out. (How it works: the container is set to cursor:none; the custom cursor uses position:fixed + transform to follow mousemove; when hovering a target, add a class so the inner circle goes scale(0.16→1) and the text opacity 0→1; this effect should be disabled on touch devices)", "tag": "Custom cursor", "style": "Cursor Custom Cursor Enlarge Hover VIEW View Custom Cursor Hover Expand Portfolio", "txt": "VIEW"}, "120": {"desc": "When skimming a work list, a preview image floats out following the cursor and tilts as it moves", "prompt": "A large-text work list (each row has the work's name on the left and its number on the right, with thin divider lines between rows), with unselected rows in fainter text; when the cursor slides onto a row, that row's text becomes clear and pushes slightly to the right, while a preview image of that work scales up from small and floats beside the cursor, following its movement — the faster it moves left or right, the more the image tilts in the direction of movement; when moving to another row, the preview image changes to another one, and when leaving the list, the image shrinks and fades out. (How it works: the preview image uses position:absolute + pointer-events:none, on mousemove it is translated to the cursor position, its rotate is calculated from the horizontal velocity with an upper limit; image switching uses opacity / scale transitions)", "tag": "Hover preview", "style": "Cursor List List Preview Image Emerge Follow Hover Image Reveal List Preview Follow Cursor Portfolio", "txt": "Brand Identity Website Design Packaging Illustration"}, "121": {"desc": "A line trails behind the cursor, growing thinner and fainter", "prompt": "When the cursor moves, a smooth line trails behind it — thicker and clearer the closer it is to the cursor, thinner and more transparent toward the tail, like a comet's tail; when the cursor stops, the tail gradually retracts to the cursor's position; the cursor itself is a small dot. (Canvas 2D: each frame, push the cursor coordinates into an array and keep only the most recent ~28 points, draw line segments in sequence, with line width and opacity increasing with the index; set the canvas size according to devicePixelRatio; the container uses cursor:none)", "tag": "Canvas trail", "style": "Cursor Trail Trajectory Line Afterimage Cursor Trail Line Comet Canvas", "txt": ""}, "122": {"desc": "Clicking anywhere on screen spreads a ripple from the click point", "prompt": "When clicking anywhere inside the section, a translucent solid circle and an outline ring spread out from the click point at the same time (the outline ring slightly later, by 0.12 seconds), both scaling from 0 up to several times the size of a thumb and fading out, in about 0.85 seconds with strong deceleration, giving the user clear click feedback; rapid repeated clicks are possible, and the ripples overlap. (How it works: on pointerdown, create circular elements at the click coordinates, CSS keyframes do scale(0→1) + opacity(1→0), and the elements are removed when the animation ends)", "tag": "Click ripple", "style": "Cursor Click Ripple Wave Feedback Click Ripple Wave Feedback Material", "txt": "Click Anywhere"}, "123": {"desc": "A ring of text keeps rotating around the cursor", "prompt": "Hide the system cursor and replace it with a small dot, surrounded by a ring of text arranged along a circle (for example \"SCROLL · EXPLORE ·\" repeated); the text ring keeps rotating slowly (about 8 seconds per revolution), and the whole assembly follows the cursor with a slight lag; the large background heading stays very faint, making the cursor the focus. (How it works: an SVG circular path + textPath, using textLength so the text exactly fills one revolution; the outer layer's transform follows the cursor, and the inner svg uses a CSS rotation animation)", "tag": "SVG textPath", "style": "Cursor Text Ring Circular Text Rotation Circular Text Rotating Text Ring Circular Text Cursor Badge SCROLL", "txt": "SCROLL · EXPLORE"}, "124": {"desc": "The screen is dark, with hidden content lit up only near the cursor, like a flashlight", "prompt": "The whole section is almost dark, with the big headline only faintly visible; wherever the cursor is, it lights up a soft-edged circular area like a flashlight, and inside that area a brighter version hidden underneath is revealed (a clear headline and gradient background). The flashlight follows the cursor, revealing wherever it shines. (How to: two stacked layers with the same layout; the top layer is the vivid version, using mask: radial-gradient(circle at var(--mx) var(--my), #000 55%, transparent) to show only the area near the cursor; update --mx and --my on mousemove)", "tag": "CSS mask", "style": "Cursor Flashlight Searchlight Spotlight Reveal Mask Flashlight Spotlight Reveal Mask Cursor Hidden", "txt": "You found me"}, "125": {"desc": "Elements in a section gently appear from top to bottom in reading order", "prompt": "When a content section (kicker, main heading, two lines of body copy, and a button) enters, each element gently rises from about 18px below and fully transparent and fades in, following top-to-bottom reading order, with about 0.14 seconds between elements, about 0.9 seconds each, easing out smoothly (power2.out), with no bounce and no scaling, so the eye is naturally led from the heading to the button. (GSAP: fromTo y:18 / opacity:0 → y:0 / opacity:1, stagger 0.14; on a real site, pair it with ScrollTrigger to play once when the section enters the viewport)", "tag": "Fade up", "style": "Section Paragraph Heading Rise Fade In Gentle Soft Light Guidance Flow Gaze Reading Order Low-key Subtle Gentle Soft Entrance Visual Flow Hierarchy Canva Style Canva Rise Rise", "txt": "Let design tell the story"}, "126": {"desc": "A paragraph becomes clear line by line from a slight blur, setting a reading rhythm", "prompt": "When a multi-line passage enters, each line in turn slowly becomes clear and fades in from about 10px below, slightly blurred and transparent, with about 0.28 seconds between lines (slower than a typical stagger, close to reading speed), about 1.1 seconds per line, easing out smoothly. The overall feel is quiet and breathable, suited to a brand philosophy or quote section. (GSAP: one element per line or SplitText with type lines, fromTo y:10 / opacity:0 / filter:blur(4px) → clear, stagger 0.28, ease power2.out)", "tag": "Line fade", "style": "Paragraph Body Line-by-Line Blur Copy Gentle Soft Light Guidance Flow Gaze Reading Order Low-key Subtle Gentle Soft Entrance Visual Flow Hierarchy Canva Style Canva Fade Clarify Fade In Clear", "txt": "Good motion doesn't grab attention it gently guides your gaze to the next step"}, "127": {"desc": "A line extends downward, and each step appears as the line reaches it", "prompt": "A vertical timeline: a thin line on the left slowly extends downward from the top (about 2.4 seconds, ease-in-out); whenever the line extends to a node, that node's dot, heading, and description row gently slide in and fade in from about 10px to the left, letting the eye follow the line all the way down through the process. (GSAP: the line scaleY 0→1, with transform-origin at the top; each node does fromTo x:-10 / opacity:0 at its corresponding time point; on a real site, ScrollTrigger scrub can be used so the line's length follows scroll progress)", "tag": "Timeline", "style": "Timeline Process Steps Journey Line Extend Gentle Soft Light Guidance Flow Gaze Reading Order Low-key Subtle Gentle Soft Entrance Visual Flow Hierarchy", "txt": "Discovery Concepts Design Launch"}, "128": {"desc": "A homepage layout appears in sequence following a Z-pattern reading order", "prompt": "When a homepage hero enters, the elements fade in and rise in sequence following a Z-pattern reading path: logo at top left → navigation menu at top right → main heading and body copy on the left → hero image on the right → call-to-action button at bottom left → secondary link at bottom right. Each element is spaced about 0.4 seconds apart, rising gently from about 12px below, with an even rhythm and no exaggerated displacement, so the user's gaze moves in the designed order. (The thin lines in the preview only illustrate the Z path and are not needed on a real site. GSAP: arrange the elements in an array in reading order, fromTo y:12 / opacity:0, stagger 0.42, ease power2.out)", "tag": "Z-pattern", "style": "Homepage Hero Layout Z Shape F Shape Reading Pattern Logo Navigation Image Action Button Gentle Soft Light Guidance Flow Gaze Reading Order Low-key Subtle Gentle Soft Entrance Visual Flow Hierarchy", "txt": "Let the flow happen naturally"}, "129": {"desc": "After the connector line between step cards draws across, the next step appears", "prompt": "Three step cards arranged horizontally (numbers 01, 02, 03 + a heading + one line of description). On entry, the first card fades in from about 14px below, then a thin connector line draws from left to right to the second card, which only then fades in, then the line draws to the third card, which fades in; the rhythm is steady, so users clearly understand 'what to do first, then what.' (GSAP: a timeline chained in sequence; cards fromTo y:14 / opacity:0, connector lines scaleX 0→1 with transform-origin on the left, ease power1.inOut / power2.out)", "tag": "Steps", "style": "Steps Process 1 2 3 Connector Line Tutorial Checkout Onboarding Gentle Soft Light Guidance Flow Gaze Reading Order Low-key Subtle Gentle Soft Entrance Visual Flow Hierarchy", "txt": "Choose a Plan Enter Details Complete Payment"}, "130": {"desc": "After the content appears, a halo gently spreads around the button, drawing the eye to it", "prompt": "A content section (heading, two lines of body copy, and a button) first fades in and rises gently in sequence; about 0.3 seconds after everything has appeared, a translucent halo softly spreads out from around the call-to-action button and fades away, twice in a row, while the button lifts slightly by 3px and returns to place, as if gently reminding 'the next step is here,' then stays still without flashing continuously. (GSAP: first a staggered fade-in, then tween the CSS variable --ring 0→1 to control the spread and opacity of the ::after box-shadow, repeat:1; the whole sequence plays only once)", "tag": "CTA cue", "style": "CTA Call to Action Button Cue Halo Diffusion Attention Gentle Soft Light Guidance Flow Gaze Reading Order Low-key Subtle Gentle Soft Entrance Visual Flow Hierarchy", "txt": "Free Trial"}, "131": {"desc": "An image is revealed from left to right by a soft gradient edge", "prompt": "When an image enters, a gradient mask with a feathered edge slowly sweeps from left to right, softly revealing the image (not a hard straight cut), while the image slowly settles back to its original size and position from 1.08x, slightly left of place, over about 1.9–2.3 seconds, easing out smoothly — quieter and more refined than a hard-edged mask. (CSS + GSAP: the outer frame uses mask:linear-gradient(90deg, #000 var(--p), transparent calc(var(--p) + 25%)); use GSAP to tween --p from -25 to 100; the inner image scale 1.08→1, x -8→0)", "tag": "Soft mask", "style": "Image Photo Mask Soft Edge Gradient Reveal Feather Gentle Soft Light Guidance Flow Gaze Reading Order Low-key Subtle Gentle Soft Entrance Visual Flow Hierarchy", "txt": ""}, "132": {"desc": "Figure-and-text rows appear alternating left and right, the gaze moving down in a Z pattern", "prompt": "Figure-and-text rows stacked vertically, alternating left and right (first row image left / text right, second row image right / text left, and so on). On entry they appear top to bottom in sequence, each row gently sliding in about 20px inward from its own side and fading in, spaced about 0.35 seconds apart, about 0.9 seconds per row, easing out smoothly, so the gaze reads downward in a Z pattern. (GSAP: fromTo x alternating ±20 by index / opacity:0, stagger 0.35, ease power2.out; on a real site, ScrollTrigger.batch can be used so each row appears only when scrolled to)", "tag": "Zigzag", "style": "Image and Text List Left and Right Alternating Z Shape Downward Intro Features Gentle Soft Light Guidance Flow Gaze Reading Order Low-key Subtle Gentle Soft Entrance Visual Flow Hierarchy", "txt": "About Work Services Contact"}, "133": {"desc": "Upload your own line SVG and watch it drawn stroke by stroke, as if by a pen", "prompt": "Turn the line SVG I provide (pasted after these instructions) into a 'drawn with a pen' entrance: each path is traced one after another in its original drawing order, with each stroke's drawing time allocated by length (longer lines draw longer, shorter ones quicker), the strokes slightly overlapping as they connect, about 3 seconds overall, ease-in-out; after finishing, it can hold then fade out and replay, or play only once. All shapes are changed to stroke only, no fill, with round line caps and joins. (GSAP: DrawSVGPlugin; for each path / line / polyline / circle, fromTo drawSVG \"0%\"→\"100%\" in sequence, with duration calculated in proportion to getTotalLength(); pure CSS can also do this with stroke-dasharray + stroke-dashoffset)", "tag": "DrawSVG·Upload", "style": "SVG Upload Custom Line Stroke Hand-drawn Stroke Logo Illustration Line Drawing Stroke Draw Upload Custom", "txt": ""}, "134": {"desc": "A pen tip writes along a signature path, finishing with an underline", "prompt": "A cursive signature line path is slowly written out starting from where the pen first touches, with a small round pen tip following at the very front of the path, as if someone is really writing (about 2.6 seconds, ease-in-out); once the signature is finished, the pen tip disappears and a slightly curved underline is quickly drawn underneath to finish. Suited to a portfolio hero or brand signature. (GSAP: DrawSVGPlugin draws the signature path while MotionPathPlugin moves the pen-tip dot along the same path, with identical timing and ease for both; the signature must be a single-stroke outline path, not outlined letterforms)", "tag": "DrawSVG·MotionPath", "style": "Signature Handwriting Cursive Writing Pen Tip Signature Handwriting Cursive Pen Write On", "txt": ""}, "135": {"desc": "A line illustration is drawn stroke by stroke, then the main subject softly appears", "prompt": "A line illustration made of multiple lines (for example, a cup of coffee giving off steam: the saucer, cup body, handle, and three wisps of steam) is traced one stroke at a time in order from bottom to top, from the main subject to the details, about 0.9 seconds per stroke with about 0.32 seconds between strokes; once all are drawn, the main subject is softly given a layer of translucent fill, and the steam lines drift gently up and down once. Quiet overall, with a handmade feel. (GSAP: DrawSVGPlugin staggers the drawing across the paths; the fill uses another path of the same shape fading in from opacity 0)", "tag": "DrawSVG", "style": "Illustration Line Illustration Stroke by Stroke Drawing Hand-drawn Diagram Line Art Illustration Draw Sketch", "txt": ""}, "136": {"desc": "Hovering over a line icon redraws its strokes and lifts it slightly", "prompt": "A row of line icons (home, search, heart, notifications), each placed inside a rounded-corner square frame; when the mouse moves over an icon, that icon's lines are redrawn from the beginning (about 0.7 seconds, multiple strokes staggered by 0.12 seconds), the frame border and the lines simultaneously switch to the accent color, and the icon lifts slightly by 6px and returns. (GSAP: on pointerenter, for that icon's path / circle elements, fromTo drawSVG \"0%\"→\"100%\", with overwrite:true to avoid conflicts when hovering across quickly)", "tag": "DrawSVG hover", "style": "Icon icon Line Icon hover Redraw Stroke Menu Navigation Icon Stroke Draw Hover Menu", "txt": ""}, "137": {"desc": "Dashed connectors between nodes keep flowing, with small dots traveling along the lines", "prompt": "In a flowchart or system architecture diagram, the nodes (circles + labels underneath) are connected with smooth curves; the connectors are dashed lines whose dashes keep moving in the direction of the data flow, and small dots also travel back and forth along each connector, expressing that data is flowing; the speed is steady and loops without stopping. (CSS: set stroke-dasharray on the paths and use keyframes to continuously change stroke-dashoffset; the small dots use SVG animateMotion or CSS offset-path to move along the same path, each with an offset start time)", "tag": "stroke-dashoffset", "style": "Flowchart Architecture Diagram Node Connector Dashed Line Flow Data Flow Flow Diagram Connector Dashed Line Data Flow", "txt": "User Frontend Backend Database"}, "138": {"desc": "Multiple wave layers at the bottom of a section flow slowly at different speeds", "prompt": "A wave shape separates two sections. The wave is made of 3 layers — the back layer paler and taller, the front layer more solid and lower — and the three layers flow slowly left and right at different speeds (about 6, 9, and 13 seconds per cycle), in not entirely the same direction, creating a sense of depth like water, looping seamlessly. (CSS: each layer is an SVG path 200% wide containing two full wavelengths, using a linear infinite animation of translateX(0 → -50%) for seamlessness; different layers are given different animation-duration and direction)", "tag": "SVG wave", "style": "Wave Divider Section Separator Water Wave Ocean Wave Wave Divider Section Separator Liquid", "txt": "Wave Divider"}, "139": {"desc": "A ring draws to a specified percentage while the number in the middle counts up in sync", "prompt": "A circular progress chart, with a low-contrast track ring underneath. On entry, the progress arc starts at the very top and draws clockwise to a specified percentage (for example 78%), with a rounded line cap; the percentage number in the middle counts up in sync from 0 to 78%, with small text underneath labeling the item's name; about 1.8 seconds, ease-in-out, stopping at the result. (GSAP: DrawSVGPlugin drawSVG \"0%\"→\"0% 78%\", the SVG as a whole rotate(-90deg) so the start point is at the top; the number tweens an object value + onUpdate to write it in, with the same timing and ease as the arc)", "tag": "DrawSVG", "style": "Progress Ring Percentage Gauge Data Statistics Progress Ring Donut Percentage Gauge Stats", "txt": "Project Completion"}, "140": {"desc": "A circle is drawn first, then a checkmark pops, and finally a success message appears", "prompt": "The success state after submitting or completing payment: first a circle is drawn (about 0.8 seconds), then a checkmark is quickly drawn inside the circle (about 0.45 seconds); the instant the check finishes, the whole icon pops slightly bigger by 8% and back, while the 'Payment Successful' text below fades in from 8px below. Clean, clear, and reassuring. (GSAP: DrawSVGPlugin draws the circle and the check path in sequence; the icon scale 1→1.08 yoyo; the text fromTo y:8 / opacity:0)", "tag": "DrawSVG", "style": "Success Complete Checkmark Tick Confirm Submit Payment State Success Check Done Confirm Tick", "txt": "Payment Successful"}, "141": {"desc": "As the round knob slides to the other side it stretches slightly, and the track switches state along with it", "prompt": "A toggle switch on an app settings page: when clicked, the round knob slides from one side to the other; during the slide, the knob first stretches horizontally and then shrinks back (like elastic jelly), overshooting slightly on arrival before settling into place; the track simultaneously switches to the accent color of the on state, and returns to a low-contrast state when off. About 0.35 seconds. (CSS: a button with role=\"switch\"; the knob uses a left transition with cubic-bezier(.5,1.4,.5,1) for the overshoot, plus keyframes that widen it at 50%; remember to update aria-checked)", "tag": "CSS switch", "style": "Toggle Switch switch toggle Settings iOS Round Knob App Mobile Mobile Device Micro-interaction Mobile App Micro-interaction", "txt": "Notifications"}, "142": {"desc": "Pull a list down, a spinning icon appears, and on release it loads and springs back", "prompt": "When you pull down at the top of a mobile list page, the list follows the finger downward (the further you pull, the greater the resistance), and a circular loading icon is revealed above; the icon's rotation angle increases with the pull distance. On release, the icon keeps spinning to indicate loading; when loading finishes, the list smoothly springs back to the top, and the newest item is briefly highlighted before fading back. (GSAP: get the pull distance from the gesture using Draggable or Observer and multiply it by a damping coefficient; on release, a timeline: spinner rotation → list y back to 0 (power3.out) → the new item's background fades out)", "tag": "Pull to refresh", "style": "Pull Down Refresh Reload List Gesture Pull Refresh Spinner Gesture App Mobile Mobile Device Micro-interaction Mobile App Micro-interaction", "txt": ""}, "143": {"desc": "The background dims and a menu slides up from the bottom with a little spring", "prompt": "After tapping an action such as 'Share,' the screen gets a translucent overlay that gradually darkens, and a menu panel slides up from the bottom of the screen with a slight bounce (about 0.6 seconds). The panel has a small handle at its top, and the options inside fade in in sequence from 8px below; on close, the panel slides quickly down and out (about 0.35 seconds, accelerating) and the overlay fades out. (GSAP: panel yPercent 100→0, ease back.out(1.1); options stagger 0.06; closing uses power2.in; in a real app, the user can drag the handle down to close it)", "tag": "Bottom sheet", "style": "Bottom Sheet Bottom Menu Popup Share Action Menu Bottom Sheet Action Sheet Drawer Modal App Mobile Mobile Device Micro-interaction Mobile App Micro-interaction", "txt": "Share to"}, "144": {"desc": "When a tab is tapped, the pill indicator stretches and slides to the new position, and the icon pops", "prompt": "An app's pill-shaped bottom navigation bar has 4 icons, with a pill indicator under the current tab; when another tab is tapped, the indicator first stretches toward the target, covering both the old and new positions at once (about 0.18 seconds), then contracts onto the new tab (about 0.34 seconds, decelerating), flowing across like liquid; the new tab's icon simultaneously pops back from 0.7x to its original size, contrasting with the indicator. (GSAP: a two-stage timeline changes the indicator's x and width; the icon scale uses back.out(3))", "tag": "Tab bar", "style": "Bottom Navigation Bar Tabs tab bar Navigation Indicator Switch Bottom Navigation Indicator Gooey App Mobile Mobile Device Micro-interaction Mobile App Micro-interaction", "txt": ""}, "145": {"desc": "Swiping a list item left reveals delete; swiping all the way collapses and removes it", "prompt": "List items can be swiped left with a finger, revealing a warning-colored 'Delete' button behind the item; if released with less than half the distance swiped, it springs back into place; if released past the threshold (about 30%), the item slides entirely off the screen to the left, then that row's height collapses to 0 and the items below smoothly move up to fill in. (GSAP: Draggable type:\"x\", restricted to leftward only, edgeResistance 0.8; onRelease, judge the threshold, then xPercent:-100, then tween height to 0; on mobile, set touch-action:pan-y so vertical scrolling is not affected)", "tag": "Draggable", "style": "Swipe Delete Swipe Left List Gesture Collapse Swipe Delete Gesture List Dismiss App Mobile Mobile Device Micro-interaction Mobile App Micro-interaction", "txt": "Meeting Reminder Billing Notice New Message"}, "146": {"desc": "On press, the button shrinks into a spinning circle, then a checkmark appears on completion and it restores", "prompt": "When the 'Submit' button is clicked, the button first presses in gently (scaling to 95%), the text fades out, and the button's width contracts into a circle (about 0.4 seconds) with a spinning loading ring appearing inside it; when done, the loading ring disappears and is replaced by a checkmark being drawn, and the button pops slightly; after holding for about 0.8 seconds, it expands back to its original width and the text fades in. This prevents duplicate clicks and lets the user clearly know the state. (GSAP: a timeline tweens in sequence the width, the spinner rotation, and the DrawSVG checkmark; the width uses fromTo with fixed units)", "tag": "Loading state", "style": "Button Loading Submit Spinner Success Checkmark State Loading Button Submit Spinner Success Morph App Mobile Mobile Device Micro-interaction Mobile App Micro-interaction", "txt": "Submit Order"}, "147": {"desc": "Tapping plus or minus gives button feedback, and the number rolls up or down to switch", "prompt": "A quantity selector for a shopping cart: minus and plus round buttons on the left and right, and a number in the middle; when a button is pressed, the button shrinks and switches to the accent color as feedback, and the number scrolls to switch according to direction — when increasing, the old number slides out upward and the new number slides in from below; when decreasing, the direction is reversed — about 0.3 seconds; at the upper and lower limits, the number no longer changes. (CSS: the number container has overflow:hidden; the old and new numbers each use keyframes with translateY ±100% to enter and exit, and the old element is removed when finished)", "tag": "Stepper", "style": "Quantity Plus Minus Stepper Cart Count Stepper Counter Quantity Plus Minus Cart App Mobile Mobile Device Micro-interaction Mobile App Micro-interaction", "txt": "Quantity"}, "148": {"desc": "When you tap into an input, the hint text shrinks and floats up, and the underline expands from the center", "prompt": "A form input normally shows only a hint label like a placeholder; when you tap in (focus), the label shrinks and floats up above the input, while the underline expands from the center out to both sides in the accent color and the cursor starts blinking; after entering content and leaving, the label stays in the small-text state above, returning to its original position only when the field is cleared. About 0.3–0.4 seconds, decelerating. (CSS: the label is absolutely positioned, using :focus-within or :not(:placeholder-shown) to change top and font-size; the underline uses transform:scaleX(0→1))", "tag": "Floating label", "style": "Input Form Label Floating Focus Floating Label Input Focus Form Material App Mobile Mobile Device Micro-interaction Mobile App Micro-interaction", "txt": "Email"}, "149": {"desc": "When a rating is selected, the stars light up in sequence from left to right and pop", "prompt": "Five hollow stars: when the user taps star N, stars 1 through N fill in from left to right in sequence and each pops larger from small (about 0.08 seconds between each), while the rest stay hollow; matching text feedback appears below in sync (for example 'Very good' or 'Amazing!'). When fewer stars are selected, the extra stars turn hollow again. (CSS: toggle .on for the fill color and .pop for the pop keyframes, staggered by index using setTimeout or transition-delay; each star is a button with an aria-label)", "tag": "Rating", "style": "Rating Stars Review Feedback Rating Stars Review Feedback App Mobile Mobile Device Micro-interaction Mobile App Micro-interaction", "txt": "Rate this experience"}, "150": {"desc": "The launch logo pops out and breathes, then zooms through the screen into the home page", "prompt": "When the app opens, the logo in the center of the screen pops out from small (back.out) and breathes gently once; then the logo accelerates and zooms until it fills the whole screen and fades out, as if passing through the logo into the app, while the home content underneath (hero card, list) fades in and rises in sequence from top to bottom. The whole sequence is about 2 seconds, ending on the home screen. (GSAP: timeline: logo scale 0.6→1 → yoyo 1.06 → scale 14 (power3.in) + the splash layer opacity 0 → home elements stagger fromTo y:10 / opacity:0)", "tag": "Splash", "style": "Splash Screen Opening splash Loading Logo Home Transition Launch Screen Intro Zoom Through App Mobile Mobile Device Micro-interaction Mobile App Micro-interaction", "txt": "M"}, "151": {"desc": "On an input error, the field shakes left and right and an error message slides out below", "prompt": "When the password is wrong at login, the input field shakes rapidly left and right a few times (like shaking its head no, about 0.45 seconds, with the amplitude growing then shrinking), the border simultaneously switches to the error color, and the error message below fades and slides in from 4px above; after the input is corrected, the border and message return to normal. (CSS: keyframes use translateX to move left and right across 10%–90%, cubic-bezier(.36,.07,.19,.97); before replaying, remove the class and trigger a reflow; it can be paired with phone vibration via navigator.vibrate)", "tag": "CSS keyframes", "style": "Error Shake Shaking Validation Password Login Form Shake Error Validation Wrong Password Login App Mobile Mobile Device Micro-interaction Mobile App Micro-interaction", "txt": "Incorrect password, please try again"}, "152": {"desc": "The characters of a paragraph brighten one by one from faint as you scroll", "prompt": "A passage in large type is fixed at the center of the screen, with all characters very faint at first; as the user scrolls down, the characters become clear in sequence starting from the first one — scroll progress equals the proportion lit — and scrolling back dims them in sequence again, like copy presentation on Apple's official site. (GSAP: SplitText splits the characters, fromTo opacity 0.15→1, stagger 0.1, ease none, bound to ScrollTrigger scrub:true; the section is fixed with pin or position:sticky, and the outer height is about 3–4 viewports)", "tag": "ScrollTrigger scrub", "style": "Character by Character Light Up Paragraph Copy Apple Official Site Text Reveal Highlight On Scroll Scroll Scroll scroll ScrollTrigger scrub Scroll-triggered", "txt": "Great motion design lights up word by word as you scroll, guiding your eyes down through this sentence."}, "153": {"desc": "A small image zooms with scrolling until it fills the screen, then a heading appears", "prompt": "A small image with rounded corners at the center of the screen (about 40% wide) gradually enlarges as you scroll down until it fills the whole screen; its corners simultaneously shrink to square corners, and the image content slowly scales back from 1.3x to its original size (so it does not look blurry when enlarged); late in the enlargement, a heading fades in from below, overlaid on the image; scrolling back reverses everything. (GSAP: a timeline bound to ScrollTrigger scrub:true, with the section pinned or sticky; tween width / height / borderRadius and the inner layer's scale; clip-path inset can also be used)", "tag": "ScrollTrigger scrub", "style": "Image Zoom Full-bleed Full Screen Expand Zoom Image Expand Full Screen Fullbleed Scroll Scroll scroll ScrollTrigger scrub Scroll-triggered", "txt": "Into the Scenery"}, "154": {"desc": "Cards scroll up one by one and stack over each other, while the one below shrinks and darkens", "prompt": "A set of large cards arranged in sequence; when each card scrolls to near the top of the screen it sticks (each card's resting position is offset slightly further down, so the edge of the previous card is visible); when the next card scrolls up and stacks on top of it, the covered card simultaneously shrinks to about 90% and darkens, creating the depth of a stack of cards; scrolling back restores it. (CSS position:sticky + top increasing by index; with GSAP, each card gets a ScrollTrigger that scrubs its scale and brightness over the range 'from the next card entering the viewport to its reaching the top')", "tag": "Sticky·scrub", "style": "Cards Stacking Sticky sticky Stacked Service Intro Stacking Cards Sticky Stack Deck Scroll Scroll scroll ScrollTrigger scrub Scroll-triggered", "txt": "Research Design Develop Launch"}, "155": {"desc": "Numbers only start counting up from zero when the data section scrolls into view", "prompt": "A results-data section in the middle of the page (three cells: a number + a label). When scrolled to the point where the data section is about 80% into the viewport, the three cells fade in from below in sequence while the numbers count up from 0 to their target values at the same time (for example 128, 99%, 4.9, decimals allowed), about 1.6 seconds, decelerating; scrolling back up out of view resets it, so it plays again the next time it is scrolled to (or plays only once). (GSAP: ScrollTrigger.create { start:\"top 80%\", onEnter, onLeaveBack }; the number tweens an object value + onUpdate, using toFixed to control the number of decimal places)", "tag": "ScrollTrigger", "style": "Data Statistics Count Numbers Results KPI Count Up Stats Numbers On Scroll Scroll Scroll scroll ScrollTrigger scrub Scroll-triggered", "txt": "Projects Completed Client Satisfaction Average Rating"}, "156": {"desc": "The navigation bar hides when scrolling down and slides out immediately when scrolling back up", "prompt": "The header navigation bar is fixed at the top; when the user scrolls down (reading content), the navigation bar slides up out of the screen to make room; as soon as they scroll up (looking for the menu), it immediately slides back in from the top, and it is always shown at the very top; about 0.35 seconds, decelerating. Very common on mobile. (How to: compare the current and previous scrollY to judge direction, or use ScrollTrigger's self.direction; toggle a class so the header uses translateY(-100%), with a transition)", "tag": "ScrollTrigger direction", "style": "Navigation Bar Header Menu header navbar Hide Show Direction Headroom Hide On Scroll Down Show On Scroll Up Scroll Scroll scroll ScrollTrigger scrub Scroll-triggered", "txt": "LOGO"}, "157": {"desc": "A curve draws its way down with scrolling, connecting each section", "prompt": "In the page background there is a curve winding left and right through the whole stretch of content, with a very faint track underneath it first; as you scroll down, the accent-colored line draws along the track, drawing as far as you have scrolled, and retracts when you scroll back; several nodes along the line (dots + headings) fade in alternately from both sides as the line approaches. Suited to brand stories, journeys, and history introductions. (GSAP: DrawSVGPlugin drawSVG 0%→100% bound to ScrollTrigger scrub; the SVG is the same height as the content, preserveAspectRatio:none; each node fades in with its own toggleActions)", "tag": "DrawSVG scrub", "style": "Path Curve Line Drawing Timeline Journey Story Scroll Path Draw SVG Line Journey Story Scroll Scroll scroll ScrollTrigger scrub Scroll-triggered", "txt": "Start Explore Grow Arrive"}, "158": {"desc": "An image moves inside its frame more slowly than the scroll, creating depth", "prompt": "A column of images arranged top to bottom, each image in a fixed frame that crops the overflow, with the image itself somewhat taller than the frame; when scrolling, the image displaces in reverse inside the frame at a slower speed (from about +12% to −12%), looking like scenery outside a window and giving more depth than scrolling as one whole block; there is a short caption below each image. (GSAP: the frame has overflow:hidden, the inner image is about 128% tall; each image gets its own ScrollTrigger, start \"top bottom\", end \"bottom top\", scrubbing yPercent -12→12)", "tag": "ScrollTrigger scrub", "style": "Image Parallax Frame Photo Depth Image Parallax Frame Inner Parallax Gallery Scroll Scroll scroll ScrollTrigger scrub Scroll-triggered", "txt": "Morning Afternoon Night"}, "159": {"desc": "Three lines of large text move left and right in opposite directions with scrolling, the middle one hollow", "prompt": "There are three lines of extra-large repeated text on screen (the middle line is hollow outline), and when scrolling, the first and third lines move left while the second line moves right, with the distance moved entirely following scroll progress (stopping when scrolling stops), creating a tense layout rhythm. (GSAP: a timeline bound to ScrollTrigger scrub:0.6, each line fromTo xPercent 0↔-40; the section is pinned or sticky)", "tag": "ScrollTrigger scrub", "style": "Big Type Horizontal Shift Marquee Reverse Heading Scroll Marquee Big Type Horizontal Text Kinetic Scroll Scroll scroll ScrollTrigger scrub Scroll-triggered", "txt": "MOTION LIBRARY"}, "160": {"desc": "When scrolled to different sections, the whole page's background and text scheme switch along with it", "prompt": "The page is divided into several sections, each with its own background and text color theme; when a section scrolls to the middle line of the screen, the whole page's background and text smoothly transition over about 0.6 seconds to that section's theme, and scrolling back switches back to the previous one, so each chapter has a clear mood change. (GSAP: one ScrollTrigger per section, start \"top 50%\", end \"bottom 50%\", switching CSS variables or a class onToggle; CSS adds a transition to background / color)", "tag": "ScrollTrigger toggle", "style": "Background Theme Switch Section Block Section Theme Background Change On Scroll Chapters Scroll Scroll scroll ScrollTrigger scrub Scroll-triggered", "txt": "Prologue Philosophy Work Contact"}, "161": {"desc": "When scrolling, a circular mask expands from the center, revealing the next chapter", "prompt": "A transition between two sections: when scrolling, the next section appears from the center of the screen through a circular mask; the circle expands with scroll progress from 0 until it covers the whole screen, while the previous section's heading slowly shrinks and fades and the next section's heading scales back from 1.2x to its original size; scrolling back shrinks the circle back. (GSAP: a timeline bound to ScrollTrigger scrub, with the section pinned or sticky; tween clipPath \"circle(0% at 50% 50%)\" → \"circle(75% at 50% 50%)\")", "tag": "clip-path scrub", "style": "Transition Circle Mask Expand Reveal Section Circle Reveal Clip Path Transition Section Scroll Scroll scroll ScrollTrigger scrub Scroll-triggered", "txt": "Chapter Two"}, "162": {"desc": "Hovering over a link grows an underline from the left, and leaving retracts it to the right", "prompt": "Text links in a navigation bar: when the mouse moves in, a thin underline grows from left to right; when the mouse moves out, the underline continues retracting to the right (instead of shrinking back the way it came), like a sweep of light passing through; about 0.45 seconds, ease-in-out. (CSS: ::after makes the underline, transform:scaleX(0); on hover, scaleX(1) with transform-origin:left; when not hovering, transform-origin:right, transition cubic-bezier(.7,0,.2,1))", "tag": "CSS hover", "style": "Link Underline Menu Navigation link underline nav menu hover Hover Mouse Enter Hover Interaction", "txt": "Home Work About Contact"}, "163": {"desc": "Hovering over hollow large text fills it solid from left to right", "prompt": "A few lines of extra-large hollow outline text: when the mouse moves over a line, that line fills in to solid from left to right (like ink pouring in), and when the mouse moves away, it retreats back to hollow from right to left; about 0.6 seconds, ease-in-out, suited to portfolio headings or menus. (CSS: the text uses -webkit-text-stroke for the outline, color:transparent; the background uses a solid-color linear-gradient with background-clip:text, and on hover, background-size 0%→100% with a transition)", "tag": "background-clip", "style": "Hollow Text Outline Fill Big Type outline stroke text fill hover hover Hover Mouse Enter Hover Interaction", "txt": "DESIGN MOTION PLAY"}, "164": {"desc": "Hovering over a card flips it in 3D to its back, showing more information", "prompt": "A row of project cards, with the hero visual and heading on the front; when the mouse moves in, the card flips 180 degrees in 3D around the vertical axis to the back, which shows action text such as 'View Project →', with a slight overshoot bounce to the flip; moving out flips it back to the front. About 0.7 seconds. (CSS: the outer layer has perspective, the inner layer transform-style:preserve-3d + a transition on transform, rotateY(180deg) on hover; both faces have backface-visibility:hidden, and the back face is pre-rotated rotateY(180deg))", "tag": "CSS 3D", "style": "Card Flip Turnover Front and Back 3D flip card hover Back Side Hover Mouse Enter Hover Interaction", "txt": "Brand Website Illustration"}, "165": {"desc": "A circular thumbnail expands on hover into a tall rounded card and a title fades in", "prompt": "A row of circular image thumbnails. When the mouse moves over one, the circle smoothly becomes a taller portrait rounded rectangle (growing downward at the same time), the image content scales back from 1.18x to its original size, revealing more of the picture, and the title below fades in; moving away restores the circle. About 0.55 seconds, ease-out. Suitable for team members or work categories. (CSS: outer frame border-radius 50% to a small rounded corner, height transitions in sync; inner image transform: scale 1.18 to 1; title opacity / translateY)", "tag": "CSS hover", "style": "image circle expand thumbnail avatar team image shape expand circle hover hover hover mouse-enter hover-over interaction", "txt": "Morning Afternoon Night"}, "166": {"desc": "As the cursor sweeps over a row of icons, nearby icons magnify and push their neighbors aside", "prompt": "A row of rounded icons like the macOS Dock: when the cursor moves left and right near the icon row, the icon closest to the cursor magnifies to about 1.9x, and the neighboring icons to its left and right magnify in decreasing amounts according to distance, forming a smooth magnification peak and pushing the other icons aside to both sides; when the cursor leaves, all return to their original size. (How to: on mousemove, calculate the horizontal distance between each icon's center and the cursor, scale = 1 + 0.9 × max(0, 1 − distance/influence range), write it into CSS variables controlling width / height so the layout naturally pushes apart; add a short transition to make the change smooth)", "tag": "CSS + JS", "style": "Dock magnify icons menu macOS toolbar magnify icons toolbar hover hover mouse-enter hover-over interaction", "txt": ""}, "167": {"desc": "When you hover over a menu item, a background pill slider follows to that item", "prompt": "A pill-shaped navigation bar. When the mouse moves over an item, a pill background slider smoothly slides over from its original position and changes width to fit that item, and the text simultaneously switches to a color that contrasts with the slider; when the mouse leaves the whole menu, the slider returns to the item for the current page. About 0.4 seconds, with a slight overshoot. (How to: on pointerenter, read the item's offsetLeft and offsetWidth, set the slider's translateX and width, transition cubic-bezier(.2,.9,.3,1.1))", "tag": "CSS + JS", "style": "menu navigation slider pill highlight follow nav pill hover indicator tabs hover hover mouse-enter hover-over interaction", "txt": "Home Work Services Articles Contact"}, "168": {"desc": "A row of narrow image panels; the hovered panel expands wider and shows its title", "prompt": "A row of equally wide vertical-strip image panels. When the mouse moves over one panel, it smoothly expands to about 4 times the width of the others, the other panels narrow in sync, and after the expansion completes the title at the bottom-left of that panel fades in; moving to another panel hands off smoothly. About 0.6 seconds, ease-out. Suitable for work categories or gallery entrances. (CSS: container display:flex, each panel flex:1, on hover flex:4, transition flex; images use object-fit:cover to avoid distortion; title gets a transition-delay)", "tag": "CSS flex", "style": "image panel expand accordion album gallery accordion expanding panels flex hover hover mouse-enter hover-over interaction", "txt": "Mountains Flowers Night Sky Sunset Coast"}, "169": {"desc": "When you hover over an icon, a tooltip pops up elastically from below", "prompt": "A row of circular icon buttons. When the mouse moves over an icon, a tooltip with a small triangular arrow pops up above it, elastically scaling up from about 60% size and a slightly lower position, using the arrow as the origin, and moving up into place (about 0.3 seconds, with a slight overshoot); moving away fades it out and shrinks it back. (CSS: tooltip position:absolute, transform-origin set at the arrow, on hover scale(0.6) to 1 + translateY + opacity, transition cubic-bezier(.3,1.5,.5,1); remember pointer-events:none to avoid flickering)", "tag": "CSS hover", "style": "tooltip tooltip explanation hint bubble popover hover hint hover hover mouse-enter hover-over interaction", "txt": "Help Info Share"}, "170": {"desc": "When you glide over text, each letter you touch bounces once on its own", "prompt": "Title text is split into individual characters. Whichever character the cursor glides over, that character bounces up once and briefly turns into an accent color (about 0.5 seconds, elastic), and a fast horizontal sweep of the cursor forms a wave in succession; each character's animation is independent, and it returns to its original position when finished. (How to: wrap each character in an inline-block span, on pointerenter remove and re-add the animation class to replay it, remove it on animationend; keyframes at 30% translateY(-35%) scale(1.12))", "tag": "CSS keyframes", "style": "text character-by-character bouncing bounce playful letter bounce hover playful hover hover mouse-enter hover-over interaction", "txt": "HOVER ME Try It"}, "171": {"desc": "When you hover over a button, its four borders are drawn in sequence to enclose it", "prompt": "A button with only a very faint thin frame normally. On mouse-enter, an accent-colored border is drawn in sequence starting from the top-left corner: top edge to the right, then right edge downward, then bottom edge to the left, then left edge upward, each segment about 0.18 seconds, joining up to enclose the button, and when the drawing finishes the text also changes to the accent color; on mouse-leave it retracts in the reverse order. (CSS: four absolutely positioned line elements, each using scaleX / scaleY with a different transform-origin; use transition-delay to arrange the order, with opposite delays for the hover and non-hover states)", "tag": "CSS transition", "style": "button border stroke line draw border draw outline button hover hover hover mouse-enter hover-over interaction", "txt": "Learn More"}, "172": {"desc": "Stars fly outward from the center into streaks of light; hovering speeds them up", "prompt": "The Hero background is a field of stars flying toward the camera: each star starts near the center of the screen, gets brighter and larger as it approaches the viewer, and pulls out short radial streaks of light, like a spaceship accelerating through space; when the cursor moves into the section, the speed smoothly increases, and the vanishing point shifts slightly toward the cursor direction, returning slowly to cruising speed after it leaves. The foreground title stays clear. (Canvas 2D: each star has x, y, z, z decreases each frame, projected coordinates = center + x/z × focal length, draw a line from the previous frame's projected position to this frame's; cover the screen with a translucent background color to create afterimages)", "tag": "Canvas 3D", "style": "starfield stars warp space light speed tunnel Starfield Warp Hyperspace Space Canvas particles particles requestAnimationFrame interactive background", "txt": "Warp Ahead"}, "173": {"desc": "Hundreds of fine lines flow slowly along an invisible current; the cursor stirs the flow", "prompt": "The background is filled with hundreds of invisible small particles. Each particle advances according to the 'flow direction' at its location (determined by smoothly varying noise or trigonometric functions, and changing slowly over time) and leaves a very fine trail. The trails fade out gradually, and the whole flows continuously like patterns of wind or water; the flow direction near the cursor is twisted, forming a stirred vortex. (Canvas 2D: each frame first cover the screen with a low-opacity background color to create trails, then let each particle advance a small step according to angle = f(x, y, t) and draw a line; particles respawn when their lifespan ends or they go out of bounds; simplex noise can be used to make the flow field more natural)", "tag": "Canvas trails", "style": "flow field current lines generative art organic Flow Field Generative Art Perlin Noise Lines Canvas particles particles requestAnimationFrame interactive background", "txt": ""}, "174": {"desc": "Petals drift down slowly while rotating; the cursor passing by blows them away", "prompt": "Dozens of petals drift slowly down from the top of the background. Each sways side to side, flips over (simulating a flip with scaling) and rotates individually, with slightly different speeds and sizes; when the cursor passes by, it blows nearby petals away according to its movement direction and speed, after which the petals slowly return to their natural falling. It can also be swapped for weather particles such as snowflakes or raindrops. (Canvas 2D: each petal has a position, velocity, angle and sway phase; cursor velocity = the difference between this frame's and the previous frame's coordinates, petals within range receive a push according to distance, which then decays gradually; when a petal falls past the bottom of the screen it returns to the top and respawns)", "tag": "Canvas particles", "style": "petals sakura falling snow weather season Petals Sakura Snow Weather Falling Particles Canvas particles particles requestAnimationFrame interactive background", "txt": ""}, "175": {"desc": "Columns of characters fall like rain, with afterimage trails", "prompt": "The whole section is filled with columns of characters falling down (katakana, numbers, English), each column at a consistent speed with a different starting point. The frontmost character is brightest, and the characters behind it gradually dim, pulling out a trail; after falling to the bottom, it randomly returns to the top and starts again. Tech, hacker feel. (Canvas 2D: number of columns = width / font size, each column records its current y; about every 55ms cover the whole screen once with a translucent background color, then draw a random character at each column's current position, y moves down one cell, and resets randomly after exceeding the screen)", "tag": "Canvas text", "style": "matrix rain hacker code characters matrix tech Matrix Code Rain Hacker Digital Canvas particles particles requestAnimationFrame interactive background", "txt": ""}, "176": {"desc": "Several spheres float and move; when they get close, they stick together like liquid", "prompt": "Several spheres of different sizes float slowly in the background and bounce off the boundaries. When two spheres come close, their edges smoothly stick together like liquid, pulling out a connecting neck, and break apart again when they separate; one of the spheres follows the cursor, so you can go and 'stick' to the other spheres. An organic feel like a lava lamp. (Canvas: on a low-resolution grid, calculate each cell's field strength Σ r²/d², fill with color where it exceeds a threshold and soften the edges for a smooth transition, then scale up and draw to the canvas; or use the gooey technique with a CSS filter blur + contrast)", "tag": "Canvas field", "style": "metaballs liquid goo organic lava lamp Metaballs Liquid Blob Gooey Lava Lamp Canvas particles particles requestAnimationFrame interactive background", "txt": ""}, "177": {"desc": "Text is made of many small dots; the cursor blows them apart up close, and they gather back when it leaves", "prompt": "A large title made up of thousands of small square dots: on entry, the dots fly in from all over the screen and assemble into text; when the cursor approaches, nearby dots are pushed away and scatter, and after it leaves they spring back into place like a spring, and dots pushed away from their original position temporarily switch to an accent color. Suitable as an interactive title on a portfolio homepage. (Canvas 2D: first draw the text on an offscreen canvas, sample opaque points every few pixels as target positions; each particle returns to its target with a spring force, is subject to a repulsive force based on the cursor distance, and has damping added)", "tag": "Canvas particles", "style": "text particles dot matrix scatter assemble interactive title Particle Text Interactive Typography Scatter Canvas particles particles requestAnimationFrame interactive background", "txt": "HELLO"}, "178": {"desc": "A full screen of small dots; as the cursor passes, they are pushed away and grow larger", "prompt": "The background is a neat arrangement of fine dots. When the cursor moves, nearby dots are pushed outward and become larger and switch to an accent color — the closer they are, the farther they are pushed — and after it leaves they return to their original positions with a spring-like motion, forming a dent that flows with the cursor. A low-key background with a strong sense of interaction. (Canvas 2D: each dot records its original position, target position = original position + direction away from the cursor × influence coefficient, use velocity + damping for spring rebound; size and opacity are interpolated according to distance)", "tag": "Canvas spring", "style": "dot grid dots grid magnetic repel interactive background Dot Grid Repel Magnetic Interactive Background Canvas particles particles requestAnimationFrame interactive background", "txt": ""}, "179": {"desc": "Wherever the cursor glides or clicks, the screen ripples like a water surface", "prompt": "The whole section is like a sheet of water. As the cursor glides over it, it creates small ripples along its path; clicking creates larger ripples. The ripples spread outward, interfere with each other and gradually calm down, and the graphics and text beneath the water surface are refractively distorted along with the ripples; when there is no interaction, a drop of water occasionally falls automatically. (Canvas: on a low resolution, use two height buffers to run the classic water ripple algorithm next = (average of the four neighbors × 2 − prev) × damping; when drawing, offset the sampling of the base image's pixels according to the height gradient, then scale up to the canvas)", "tag": "Canvas pixels", "style": "water ripples water surface ripples refraction Water Ripple Wave Refraction Liquid Canvas particles particles requestAnimationFrame interactive background", "txt": "Water Surface"}, "180": {"desc": "Use the cursor or a finger to scratch off the surface layer and reveal the content underneath", "prompt": "The card is covered with a surface layer with a metallic gradient texture and the words 'scratch to see'. Wherever the user holds down the mouse or drags a finger, it is scratched away (a thick brush with a round tip), revealing the prize or offer content underneath; when the scratched area exceeds about half, the remaining surface layer automatically fades out for a full reveal. Suitable for prize draws, coupons and event pages. (Canvas 2D: the surface layer is drawn on a canvas, while dragging use globalCompositeOperation = \"destination-out\" to draw lines along the path and erase; periodically sample the transparent proportion of getImageData to judge whether to reveal; set touch-action:none on mobile)", "tag": "Canvas erase", "style": "scratch card scratch off reveal prize draw coupon gamification Scratch Card Reveal Lottery Coupon Gamification Canvas particles particles requestAnimationFrame interactive background", "txt": "Free Shipping Coupon"}, "181": {"desc": "Fireworks rise to the clicked position and burst; they launch automatically when there is no interaction", "prompt": "A night-sky background. When you click any position, a firework is launched from the bottom of the screen, rises to the clicked spot, and upon arrival bursts into dozens of sparks. The sparks scatter in all directions, fall under gravity, slow down due to drag and gradually fade out, leaving brief trails; when there is no interaction, they launch automatically at random. Suitable for event pages and completion celebrations. (Canvas 2D: the rocket rises with ease-out interpolation, on explosion an array of particles is created, each frame the velocity (× drag, + gravity) and lifespan are updated; each frame the screen is covered with a translucent background color for trails)", "tag": "Canvas particles", "style": "fireworks celebration explosion particles event festival Fireworks Celebration Particles Explosion Click Canvas particles particles requestAnimationFrame interactive background", "txt": ""}, "182": {"desc": "An element slowly scales up and down, cycling like breathing", "prompt": "Text or an element continuously scales up slowly to about 1.07x and then back down, while its opacity fluctuates slightly between 0.82 and 1, one cycle taking about 3.2 seconds, easing in and out at both ends, like breathing. Suitable for emphasizing a key point or an idle state. (CSS: keyframes 0%/100% scale(1), 50% scale(1.07), ease-in-out, infinite)", "tag": "CSS keyframes", "style": "breathing pulse scale up and down idle Pulse Breathing Idle Canva style Canva Breathe breathing presentation social post animation", "txt": "Deep Breath"}, "183": {"desc": "Text fades in from the side, keeps drifting slowly, then fades out", "prompt": "Text fades in from a position about 12% in from the right and decelerates quickly, then instead of stopping it keeps drifting to the left at a very slow constant speed, and at the end fades out while still drifting; the whole sequence takes about 4 seconds, giving a quiet, flowing feeling. Suitable for titles in presentations or social posts. (CSS: in the keyframes, the first 20% fades in with an ease-out curve, 20%–80% is a small linear displacement, then it fades out at the end)", "tag": "CSS keyframes", "style": "drift slow pan fade in and out presentation Drift Slow Slide Fade Canva style Canva Drift drift presentation social post animation", "txt": "Drifting Slowly"}, "184": {"desc": "An image slides in quickly from the side with motion blur, pauses, then slides out the other side", "prompt": "An image card slides in quickly from outside the left edge of the screen (about 0.6 seconds, fast then slow), with a slight motion blur while it slides, then stays clear once in place; finally it accelerates out to the right, again with blur. Like a fast camera pan, suitable for photo switching or transitions. (CSS: keyframes translateX(-140%) to 0 to 140%, with filter:blur appearing during the movement segments, cubic-bezier(.7,0,.2,1))", "tag": "CSS keyframes", "style": "pan slide in slide out motion blur transition Pan Slide Motion Blur Transition Canva style Canva Pan pan presentation social post animation", "txt": "Travel Diary"}, "185": {"desc": "Each character makes its entrance tumbling and rotating from a shrunken state", "prompt": "Each character enters tumbling: starting from about 0.2x size and rotated 200 degrees counterclockwise, it straightens while scaling up to make its entrance, finally overshooting slightly (rotating 10 degrees too far, scaling to 1.08) before settling upright, with a sequential delay of about 0.08 seconds between characters — playful and full of energy. (CSS: each character is inline-block, keyframes rotate(-200deg) scale(.2) to rotate(10deg) scale(1.08) to none, animation-delay increasing by index)", "tag": "CSS keyframes", "style": "tumble rotate entrance character-by-character playful Tumble Spin Rotate In Canva style Canva Tumble tumble presentation social post animation", "txt": "Tumbling In"}, "186": {"desc": "Text flickers irregularly like a neon tube, then lights up", "prompt": "Text is like a neon tube that has just been powered: it starts dark, then flickers quickly twice in an irregular pattern, then lights up stably with a multilayer outer glow (brighter inner layer, diffused outer layer); after that it glows stably most of the time, with an occasional brief flicker to add realism. Suitable for signage and nighttime themes. (CSS: keyframes switch opacity and text-shadow at a few percentages for irregular flickering; the glow uses 2–3 layers of text-shadow with different radii; rounded or bold fonts work better)", "tag": "CSS keyframes", "style": "neon tube flicker glow sign nightclub Neon Glow Flicker Sign Canva style Canva Neon neon presentation social post animation", "txt": "OPEN"}, "187": {"desc": "Photos, tape, stickers and a title are pasted on one by one at slight angles", "prompt": "A layout like a journal collage: two Polaroid photos, a strip of washi tape, a round sticker and a hand-lettered-style title are 'pasted' on one by one in sequence — each element drops quickly from a slightly larger, somewhat higher position, with its own small tilt angle, and bounces slightly when it lands (about 0.5 seconds, at intervals of about 0.28 seconds), then after a pause they all fade out together. Warm, handmade feel. (CSS: each element sets its own rotation angle and delay with CSS variables, keyframes translateY(-30%) scale(1.25) to scale(.95) to 1, keeping rotate(var(--r)))", "tag": "CSS keyframes", "style": "scrapbook collage journal photo sticker tape Scrapbook Collage Sticker Photo Journal Canva style Canva Scrapbook scrapbook presentation social post animation", "txt": "My Summer"}, "188": {"desc": "The top and bottom halves of the text slide in from the left and right respectively, merging into complete characters", "prompt": "A title is cut horizontally into top and bottom halves: the top half slides in and fades in from the left, the bottom half from the right at the same time, precisely aligning in the middle to form the complete text (about 0.9 seconds, strong ease-out), then fades out after a pause. (CSS: the same text is placed twice, using clip-path:inset(0 0 50% 0) and inset(50% 0 0 0) respectively to show only the top half and the bottom half, each with keyframes translateX(∓35%) to 0)", "tag": "clip-path", "style": "merge join top and bottom cut in half left and right slide in Merge Split Halves Join Canva style Canva Merge merge presentation social post animation", "txt": "Become One"}, "189": {"desc": "Characters stacked together spread out from a blur into normal letter spacing", "prompt": "The text starts with extremely tight letter spacing, all characters stacked together and blurred and transparent. Then the letter spacing smoothly expands to normal width while it becomes clear and fades in (about 1.1 seconds, ease-out), as if spreading out and taking shape from the center; it fades out after a pause. (CSS: keyframes letter-spacing:-0.55em to 0.06em, with filter:blur(6px) to 0 and opacity)", "tag": "letter-spacing", "style": "spread letter spacing expand blur focus Spread Letter Spacing Tracking Expand Canva style Canva Spread spread presentation social post animation", "txt": "Spread Out"}, "190": {"desc": "Text skates in at a tilt like ice skating, then straightens after braking", "prompt": "As the text slides in at high speed from the left, the whole leans forward (skewX about -28 degrees); on arrival it slides slightly too far and tilts in the opposite direction (like a body leaning back while braking), then straightens and stops; on exit it accelerates out to the right and leans forward again. A sense of speed and weight. (CSS: keyframes in sequence translateX(-70%) skewX(-28deg) to translateX(4%) skewX(14deg) to skewX(-4deg) to none, with an accelerating curve for the exit segment)", "tag": "CSS keyframes", "style": "skate ice skating tilt brake sense of speed Skate Skew Slide Brake Canva style Canva Skate skate presentation social post animation", "txt": "Skating In"}, "191": {"desc": "An image continuously zooms in slowly and pans slightly, like a documentary push-in", "prompt": "A photo zooms in very slowly inside a fixed frame (over about 9 seconds, to 1.22x) while panning slightly to one side at the same time, then slowly retreats back, cycling back and forth, like a documentary push-in on a still photo, giving a static image a sense of life; the title on the image stays still. (CSS: outer frame overflow:hidden, inner image keyframes scale(1) to scale(1.22) translate(-4%, 2%), ease-in-out, alternate infinite, transform-origin set near the subject)", "tag": "CSS keyframes", "style": "push-in slow zoom pan photo documentary Ken Burns Slow Zoom Pan Photo Canva style Canva Photo Zoom photo zoom presentation social post animation", "txt": "Coastline"}, "192": {"desc": "The logo's circle, square and dot are drawn and assembled in sequence, then the brand name slides out", "prompt": "A brand logo assembles and enters in sequence: the outer circle is drawn first (about 0.9 seconds), then the square in the middle, rotated 45 degrees, is stroked and filled with an accent color, the center dot pops out from 0 and scales up, and finally the brand name slides in from 12px to the left and fades in; after a pause the whole fades out. Suitable for a website opening or a video intro. (GSAP: DrawSVGPlugin draws the circle and rect in sequence, fill-opacity 0 to 1; the dot's scale uses back.out(3); text fromTo x:-12 / opacity:0)", "tag": "DrawSVG", "style": "Logo logo brand opening assemble draw Logo Reveal Brand Intro Build SVG graphic", "txt": "STUDIO"}, "193": {"desc": "A row of bars jumps randomly like an audio waveform", "prompt": "A waveform in an audio player: a row of thin, rounded bars stretches up and down with the center line as a baseline, each bar's height is random, their speeds differ slightly and they keep changing, like sound being played; there is a circular play button on the left, and the time is shown on the right. (GSAP: tween all rects with scaleY:\"random(.12,1)\", duration:\"random(.22,.5)\", repeat:-1, yoyo:true, repeatRefresh:true so each repeat picks new random numbers, transformOrigin centered)", "tag": "SVG bars", "style": "audio waveform music player equalizer Podcast Audio Waveform Equalizer Visualizer SVG graphic", "txt": ""}, "194": {"desc": "A gradient flows continuously along a line, and a point of light travels around the line", "prompt": "A closed, infinity-symbol-shaped curve. The line itself is a multicolored gradient, and the gradient flows continuously along the direction of the line; at the same time a small, bright point of light travels around the line like a comet, with a slight glow. Suitable for brand decoration or a tech-feel background. (SVG: linearGradient set to gradientUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\", spreadMethod=\"repeat\", animate the gradientTransform translation with animateTransform; for the point of light use a second identical path with a stroke-dasharray of one short solid segment, and change stroke-dashoffset with keyframes)", "tag": "SVG gradient", "style": "gradient line flow light point comet infinity symbol Gradient Stroke Flow Comet Infinity Loop SVG graphic", "txt": ""}, "195": {"desc": "The liquid surface inside an icon rises slowly with waves, and the percentage increases in sync", "prompt": "A heart-shaped icon. The liquid inside flows with two layers of waves crossing each other, and the liquid surface slowly rises from the bottom until it fills up, while the percentage number in the center increases in sync from 0% to 100%; outside the liquid surface, the icon's outline is retained. Can be used for upload progress or a goal completion rate. (SVG: use clipPath to constrain the waves inside the icon shape; the wave path is two wavelengths wide, CSS translateX loops seamlessly; the liquid surface height is controlled by a GSAP tween of the outer g's y, and the number tweens in sync)", "tag": "SVG clipPath", "style": "liquid fill wave progress percentage loading Liquid Fill Wave Progress Loading Icon SVG graphic", "txt": ""}, "196": {"desc": "A scanning fan sector keeps circling, and dots light up where it sweeps past", "prompt": "A radar screen: several concentric circles and crosshairs, and a translucent fan-shaped scanning sector rotates continuously clockwise (about 3 seconds per revolution). Where the scan line passes, dots light up and briefly grow larger, then gradually fade out, lighting up again when the next revolution sweeps past. Suitable for searching, positioning, and tech-style dashboards. (SVG + CSS: the fan-shaped path is placed in a g and rotated around the center; each dot's animation-delay is calculated from its angle as the time the scan line arrives)", "tag": "SVG radar", "style": "radar scan search positioning tech map Radar Scan Sweep Ping Search Tech SVG graphic", "txt": ""}, "197": {"desc": "A line chart is drawn from left to right, data points pop out in sequence, and the area below fades in", "prompt": "Line chart entrance: there are faint horizontal grid lines in the background, and the line is drawn from left to right (about 1.6 seconds). Each data point pops out from 0 in sequence as the line passes it, and when the line reaches its later section, the area below the line fades in with a gradient, and finally a growth value label floats up above the endpoint. (GSAP: DrawSVGPlugin draws the line path; the data points' stagger time = drawing time / number of points; the area uses the same path, closed along the bottom edge and filled with a gradient fading from top to bottom; on a real website it can be played when scrolled to, paired with ScrollTrigger)", "tag": "DrawSVG", "style": "line chart chart data growth trend Dashboard Line Chart Graph Data Visualization SVG graphic", "txt": "Monthly Revenue Growth"}, "198": {"desc": "Bars grow upward from the bottom in sequence with a slight rebound, and the values accumulate in sync", "prompt": "Bar chart entrance: each bar grows upward from the baseline in sequence (0.1 seconds apart) with a slight overshoot and rebound, while the value at the top of the bar accumulates from 0 to the actual number at the same time, with month labels shown below. Suitable for reports and results pages. (GSAP: the bars' transform-origin is at the bottom, fromTo scaleY 0 to 1, ease back.out(1.6); the values tween an object value + onUpdate; it can be played when scrolled to, paired with ScrollTrigger)", "tag": "Stagger", "style": "bar chart column chart chart data statistics Dashboard Bar Chart Column Graph Data SVG graphic", "txt": "Monthly Page Views"}, "199": {"desc": "A donut chart is drawn segment by segment, and the legend slides in in sequence", "prompt": "Donut chart entrance: starting from the very top, the arc segment of the first category is drawn clockwise, then the next segment continues drawing from the previous segment's endpoint, completing the whole circle in sequence, with small gaps kept between segments and each segment in a different category color; the center shows the total and title, and the legend on the right slides in from the right in sequence. (GSAP: each segment is a full circle, drawn to the specified section with DrawSVGPlugin's drawSVG \"start% start%\" to \"start% end%\"; the SVG is rotate(-90deg) so the starting point is at the top)", "tag": "DrawSVG", "style": "pie chart donut chart donut proportion chart data Donut Pie Chart Segments Data SVG graphic", "txt": "Traffic Sources"}, "200": {"desc": "A circle, square and triangle bounce and flip in sequence as a loading indicator", "prompt": "A loading indicator: three outlined geometric shapes (circle, square, triangle) in a row. In sequence, like a wave, they first squash down to build up energy, jump up and flip 360 degrees, then squash and rebound when they land, playing in a loop — more characterful than an ordinary spinner icon. (CSS: a single set of keyframes includes scale squashing, translateY jumping, and rotate flipping, with the three shapes staggered by 0.18 seconds using animation-delay)", "tag": "CSS keyframes", "style": "loading reading loading waiting geometric bounce Loader Spinner Geometric Shapes Bounce SVG graphic", "txt": ""}, "201": {"desc": "Text continuously ripples and distorts as if seen through a water surface", "prompt": "A large title continuously ripples and distorts as if seen through a water surface or a heat haze. The distortion's texture and intensity change slowly; the text remains legible but has a liquid, psychedelic feel. (SVG filter: feTurbulence generates noise, feDisplacementMap displaces the source image according to the noise, use animate to cycle baseFrequency and scale between values; apply it to HTML elements with CSS filter:url(#id); watch performance, and avoid applying it to large areas or many elements)", "tag": "feTurbulence", "style": "filter distortion water ripple liquid heat haze psychedelic SVG Filter Turbulence Displacement Distortion Liquid SVG graphic", "txt": "Rippled Distortion"}, "202": {"desc": "When switching pages, three curtains fall in sequence to cover the screen, then retract downward to reveal the new page", "prompt": "When a navigation click switches the page, three vertical strip curtains fall from the top in sequence (about 0.08 seconds apart) to cover the whole screen — at this moment the page behind is replaced with the new page — then the three curtains retract downward in sequence, and the new page's title and content blocks fade in and float up from top to bottom. The whole sequence takes about 1.4 seconds, giving page changes a complete sense of rhythm. (GSAP: curtains yPercent -101 to 0 to 101, stagger 0.08, ease power3.inOut; switch the content in the callback between the two segments; for an SPA it can be paired with Barba.js or a framework's route transition hooks)", "tag": "Timeline", "style": "page transition page change curtain mask SPA routing Page Transition Curtain Wipe Router layout page web structure", "txt": "Home Work About"}, "203": {"desc": "Three lines transform into an X, and a fullscreen menu expands in a circle from the button", "prompt": "When the hamburger menu button at the top-right is clicked, the three lines transform into an X (the top and bottom lines rotate ±45 degrees and move to the middle, the middle line shortens and fades out), while the fullscreen menu expands with a circular mask centered on the button's position, and the menu items slide in from below and fade in, top to bottom in sequence (about 0.07 seconds apart); clicking again collapses it in reverse. About 0.6 seconds, ease in and out. (CSS: toggle an open class; menu layer clip-path:circle(0% at the button position) to circle(150%); the lines transition top and rotate; the items' transition-delay increases by index)", "tag": "clip-path", "style": "hamburger menu menu fullscreen navigation mobile X Hamburger Menu Overlay Fullscreen Nav Toggle layout page web structure", "txt": "Home Work Services Contact"}, "204": {"desc": "When the menu opens, the whole content page shrinks and pushes to the right, revealing the menu underneath", "prompt": "When the hamburger icon is clicked, the current content page is pushed to the right as a whole and shrinks to about 86%, with rounded corners and a shadow added, pushed open like a card, revealing the menu hidden underneath, and the menu items slide in from the left and fade in, in sequence; clicking again slides the content page back to cover the menu. About 0.55 seconds, ease in and out. (CSS: content layer transform:translateX(38%) scale(.86), transform-origin at the middle of the left side, border-radius transitions along with it; the menu items are staggered with transition-delay)", "tag": "CSS transform", "style": "side menu drawer push shrink off-canvas mobile Side Drawer Push Menu Off Canvas Scale layout page web structure", "txt": "Home Work Services Contact"}, "205": {"desc": "The background blurs and darkens, and a window pops out elastically from a slightly smaller, lower position", "prompt": "After a button is clicked, the background gets a translucent mask and a slight blur (fading in over about 0.35 seconds), and a dialog floats elastically to the exact center from 90% size and a position slightly below center, with a slight overshoot; the content includes a title, a description, and Cancel / Confirm buttons; clicking the mask or either button fades the dialog out and shrinks it back, and the mask fades out. (CSS: toggle an open class; mask opacity + backdrop-filter:blur; dialog transform:translate(-50%,-40%) scale(.9) to translate(-50%,-50%) scale(1), transition cubic-bezier(.3,1.4,.5,1); remember to handle focus and closing with the Esc key)", "tag": "CSS transition", "style": "popup dialog window confirm modal dialog popup background blur Overlay layout page web structure", "txt": "Ready to submit?"}, "206": {"desc": "When a question is clicked, its answer area smoothly expands, the plus turns into an X, and the other questions collapse at the same time", "prompt": "A FAQ list, with a plus icon on the right of each question; when one question is opened, the height of its answer area smoothly expands from 0 to the content height (not an instant jump), the plus rotates 135 degrees to become an X at the same time, and any other expanded questions collapse in sync, so only one is open at a time. About 0.45 seconds, ease-in-out. (CSS: the answer wrapper uses display:grid with a transition on grid-template-rows: 0fr to 1fr, and the inner layer has overflow:hidden; the plus is made of two lines and rotated; details/summary with JS can also be used)", "tag": "grid-template-rows", "style": "Accordion FAQ Expand Collapse Fold Accordion Collapse Expand Details Layout Page Web Structure", "txt": "How do I order? How is shipping calculated? Can I return items?"}, "207": {"desc": "The underline indicator slides to the new tab, and the content alternates sliding left or right depending on the switch direction", "prompt": "A set of tabs; when another tab is clicked, the underline indicator below the tabs smoothly slides to the new tab and adjusts to its width; the content area slides according to the switch direction - when switching to a tab on the right, the old content slides out to the left and fades out, and the new content slides in from the right and fades in, and the opposite when switching left, so the user feels the before-and-after order of the tabs. About 0.45 seconds. (GSAP: compare the old and new indexes to decide the direction d, tween the old content to xPercent -30 x d and fade it out before removing it, bring the new content in from xPercent 30 x d; set the indicator's transform and width using offsetLeft / offsetWidth)", "tag": "GSAP", "style": "Pagination Tab Label tab Switch Direction Content Tabs Directional Slide Indicator Layout Page Web Structure", "txt": "Design Development Marketing"}, "208": {"desc": "When switching categories, works that do not match shrink away and disappear, while the other works smoothly move to fill the gaps", "prompt": "A portfolio with category labels at the top (All / Brand / Website / Illustration); when a category is clicked, works that do not match shrink and fade out, works that match smoothly move from their original positions to new layout positions to fill the gaps, and works that reappear scale up from small and fade in; the selected category label switches to an emphasized state. About 0.6 seconds. (GSAP: use Flip.getState to record all cards, then switch display, then Flip.from, with absolute:true and onEnter / onLeave handling the scale and fade in/out for entering and leaving items)", "tag": "Flip", "style": "Filter Category Portfolio Grid Rearrange Fill Filter Grid Portfolio Isotope Reflow Flip Layout Page Web Structure", "txt": "Brand Website Illustration"}, "209": {"desc": "Hover over one cell of the bento grid and that cell grows while the other cells yield space in sync", "prompt": "A Bento (lunch-box style) 3x2 grid; when the mouse moves over a cell, the column and row containing that cell enlarge (column width about 2.4x, row height about 1.8x), the other cells shrink in sync to yield space, the whole grid smoothly redistributes, and the title in the enlarged cell also grows in sync; when the mouse leaves, it returns to even sizes. About 0.55 seconds, ease-in-out. (CSS: the container's grid-template-columns / rows use fr values; on hover, JS rewrites the fr values of the target column and row, and a transition is added to grid-template-columns and grid-template-rows)", "tag": "CSS grid", "style": "Bento Lunch Box Grid Mesh Expand Enlarge Feature Introduction Bento Grid Expand Hover Feature Layout Page Web Structure", "txt": "Design Development Strategy Brand Data Community"}, "210": {"desc": "The text on the right scrolls down, while the fixed image on the left switches to match the corresponding section", "prompt": "The screen is split into left and right columns: the left column is a fixed (sticky) large-image area, and the right column is text chapters that can be scrolled section by section; whenever a chapter on the right scrolls to the middle of the screen, the image on the left cross-fades into the image for the corresponding chapter and shrinks back from a slightly enlarged state to its original size, creating a synchronized image-and-text storytelling experience. (CSS position:sticky + GSAP ScrollTrigger: each chapter has start \"top 55%\" and end \"bottom 55%\", and onToggle switches the active class of the corresponding image on the left; images use transitions on opacity and scale)", "tag": "Sticky · ScrollTrigger", "style": "Split Screen Left Right Two Columns Fixed Image Switch Storytelling Split Screen Sticky Image Scrollytelling Layout Page Web Structure", "txt": "Morning Afternoon Night"}, "211": {"desc": "After scrolling, a button floats in at the bottom right, its outer ring shows reading progress, and clicking it returns to the top", "prompt": "On a long article page, after scrolling down past a short distance, a circular button at the bottom right elastically scales in from 0; around the button is a progress ring that is drawn full according to the scroll proportion of the whole page (clockwise from the very top), with an upward arrow in the middle; when clicked, the page smoothly scrolls back to the top, and near the top the button shrinks and disappears. (GSAP: DrawSVGPlugin bound to a ScrollTrigger with scrub draws the progress ring, onUpdate toggles visibility based on progress; on click use gsap.to(window, {scrollTo:0}) or window.scrollTo({top:0, behavior:\"smooth\"}))", "tag": "DrawSVG scrub", "style": "Back To Top Top Progress Ring Reading Progress Scroll Progress Back To Top Scroll Progress Ring Button Layout Page Web Structure", "txt": "Reading Progress"}, "212": {"desc": "The middle card is enlarged and clear, the sides are smaller and faded, switch left and right", "prompt": "A set of cards arranged horizontally as a carousel; the current card is centered, largest, and fully clear, the adjacent cards on the left and right shrink to about 82% and become semi-transparent, and cards further out are smaller and fainter still; when switching, all cards slide smoothly together to their new positions and change size (about 0.6 seconds, ease-in-out); below are left and right arrows and dot indicators (the current dot is elongated); it can autoplay, and clicking a side card can switch directly to it. (CSS: each card sets translateX, scale, opacity and z-index according to its distance from the current index, with a transition; when out of range, take the nearest looping direction)", "tag": "CSS transition", "style": "Carousel carousel slider Focus Center Enlarge coverflow Works Carousel Image Cards Group", "txt": "Brand Website Illustration Packaging Photography"}, "213": {"desc": "The top card can be dragged and flung out, and the next one moves up to take its place", "prompt": "A stack of cards; the top card can be dragged with a finger or mouse, and while dragging the card tilts following the horizontal displacement; when dragged right, a \"Like\" stamp fades in at the top-left corner, and when dragged left, a \"Skip\" stamp fades in at the top-right; on release, if it exceeds the threshold it accelerates and is flung off-screen in that direction, and the cards below move up in order to fill in and scale up; if it does not exceed the threshold it springs back to its original position. (GSAP Draggable: onDrag sets rotation and stamp opacity based on x, onRelease checks the threshold then tweens it off-screen, then moves that card to the bottom layer and rearranges the whole stack)", "tag": "Draggable", "style": "Swipe Cards Swipe Left Right Dating Tinder Card Stack Fling Swipe Cards Stack Like Dislike Cards Group", "txt": "Tokyo Kyoto Seoul Tainan"}, "214": {"desc": "A stack of slightly skewed cards fans out into a row to both sides on hover", "prompt": "Five cards stacked in a pile, each skewed at a slightly different angle; when the mouse moves over the stack, the cards fan out to the left and right around the middle card into a fan-shaped row (the further out, the larger the angle and the more they droop slightly downward), with a slight elastic rebound; when the mouse leaves, they gather back into a stack. About 0.6 seconds. (CSS: each card uses the CSS variable --i (-2 to 2) to calculate translateX, rotate and translateY; on hover larger coefficients are used, with transition cubic-bezier(.3,1.3,.5,1))", "tag": "CSS hover", "style": "Stacked Cards Fan Out Fan Shape Expand Portfolio Stack Spread Fan Cards Hover Cards Group", "txt": "Planning Design Development Testing Launch"}, "215": {"desc": "When switching between monthly and yearly payment, each plan's price rolls to update, and the recommended plan stands out", "prompt": "At the top of a pricing page there is a \"Monthly / Yearly\" toggle capsule; when clicked, the slider slides to the other side; the price numbers on the three plan cards roll and accumulate from the old value to the new value (about 0.6 seconds), the unit changes to \"/month\" or \"/year\" in sync, and each card gently floats up and settles back down in sequence; the recommended plan in the middle is enlarged by default and given a border and a \"Recommended\" label. (GSAP: tween a numeric object value and write it in onUpdate; stagger the cards' y yoyo with a delay based on index; the toggle capsule uses a CSS transform transition)", "tag": "GSAP", "style": "Price Plans Subscription Monthly Yearly Pricing Table Pricing Table Plans Toggle Monthly Yearly SaaS Cards Group", "txt": "Basic Professional Enterprise"}, "216": {"desc": "Clicking a card smoothly enlarges it into a detail panel while the other cards fade out", "prompt": "A row of work cards; when one is clicked, it smoothly enlarges from its original position and size into a detail panel that fills the whole area (large image on the left, title and description on the right), while the other cards fade out at the same time; the text inside the detail fades in in sequence around the completion of the enlargement; clicking again shrinks it back to its original position and the other cards fade back in. About 0.6 seconds, ease-in-out. (GSAP Flip: use Flip.getState to record all cards, then toggle the enlarged card's class (changing it to absolute positioning that fills the container with a new layout), then Flip.from to tween, with nested:true so inner elements transform along with it)", "tag": "Flip", "style": "Cards Expand Details Enlarge Shared Element shared element transition Expand Detail Flip Cards Group", "txt": "Work 1 Work 2 Work 3 Work 4"}, "217": {"desc": "Two rows of cards move infinitely in opposite directions, and pause when the mouse moves over them", "prompt": "Two rows of testimonial or client cards move horizontally in an infinite loop, the top row to the left and the bottom row to the right, at a slow, steady speed; when the mouse moves over the card wall both rows pause for easy reading, and continue when it moves away. Suitable for client testimonials and partner logo walls. (CSS: each row's content is duplicated twice on the same track, and keyframes translateX(0 to -50%) linear infinite achieves a seamless loop; the reverse row uses animation-direction:reverse; on :hover, animation-play-state:paused)", "tag": "CSS marquee", "style": "Marquee Card Wall Testimonials Clients Logo Wall Infinite Infinite Marquee Testimonials Logo Wall Cards Group", "txt": "Designer Engineer Marketer Founder"}, "218": {"desc": "The quote fades out and moves up to switch to the next one, avatars switch along with it, and a progress bar keeps time", "prompt": "A client testimonial carousel: in the center is a large quote and attribution, with a row of circular avatars and a progress bar below; about every 2.6 seconds, the current quote fades out upward and the next one fades in and slides up from below, the corresponding avatar enlarges and gains a ring while the other avatars shrink and fade, and the progress bar restarts filling from 0 to keep time; clicking an avatar switches directly to that testimonial. (GSAP: tween the y and opacity of the old and new quotes separately; the progress bar goes scaleX 0 to 1 with ease none, with a duration equal to the auto-switch interval)", "tag": "GSAP", "style": "Testimonials Recommendations Client Testimonials Carousel Quote Testimonial Review Quote Slider Carousel Cards Group", "txt": "Ms. Wang Mr. Chen Designer Lin"}, "219": {"desc": "Masonry cards of varying heights fall into place row by row with a slight rotation", "prompt": "A Masonry gallery entrance: cards in three columns of varying heights, in reading order from top to bottom and left to right, fall one by one from about 30px above with a slight random rotation and fade in, with a slight rebound as they settle (interval about 0.09 seconds), so the whole gallery looks as if it is being placed piece by piece. (GSAP: after sorting by each card's row and column index, stagger 0.09, fromTo y:-30 / opacity:0 / rotation:random(-6,6) back to zero, ease back.out(1.4); on a real site, layout can be done with CSS columns or a masonry library)", "tag": "Stagger", "style": "Masonry masonry Pinterest Gallery Entrance Fall Masonry Grid Cascade Gallery Cards Group", "txt": ""}, "220": {"desc": "When hovering over a card it lifts up, while the other cards fade and shrink", "prompt": "A row of cards; when the mouse moves over one card, it lifts slightly and enlarges to 1.04x, while the other cards simultaneously fade, blur slightly, desaturate and shrink to 95%, focusing attention on the current card; when the mouse leaves the whole row, everything returns to normal. About 0.45 seconds, decelerating. (CSS: when the container is :hover, .card:not(:hover) gets reduced opacity, filter:blur(1px) saturate(.6) and scale(.95); the hovered card gets translateY + scale; :has() can be used to support keyboard focus)", "tag": ":has()", "style": "Focus Dim Other Cards hover Highlight Focus Dim Siblings Highlight Spotlight Cards Group", "txt": "Beginner Advanced Master Team"}, "221": {"desc": "Click add to cart, and the product thumbnail flies in an arc into the cart while the count jumps", "prompt": "When the \"Add to Cart\" button on a product card is pressed, the button gives a light press feedback, a copy of the product thumbnail flies along a parabolic arc to the cart icon at the top right, gradually shrinking during flight; on arrival the cart bounces and enlarges once, and the count badge in the corner increments by 1 and pops out. About 0.75 seconds, giving the user clear \"added\" feedback. (GSAP: tween the flying element's x with power1.in and y with back.in separately to form an arc, while scaling from 1 to 0.15; on completion remove the element and update the badge, with the badge scale using back.out(3))", "tag": "GSAP arc", "style": "Cart Add E-commerce Fly In Parabola Feedback Add To Cart Fly Ecommerce Shop Feedback Cards Group", "txt": "Handmade Ceramic Cup"}, "222": {"desc": "A soft, large gradient flows slowly, with a layer of fine, flickering film grain on top", "prompt": "A Hero background of three large, soft-edged gradient glows that slowly move in an interlaced pattern and drift back and forth on a cycle of about 12 seconds; on top is a layer of very fine film grain (noise) texture, with the grain flickering several times per second, giving the image an analog print-like texture, while the foreground title stays clear. (CSS: multiple radial-gradients layered in the same background, with keyframes animating background-position; the grain layer uses noise generated by SVG feTurbulence as its background-image, with mix-blend-mode:overlay and low opacity, using steps() keyframes with random displacement to create the flicker)", "tag": "SVG noise", "style": "Grain Noise Film Grain Gradient Texture Grain Noise Film Gradient Texture Mesh Gradient mesh gradient Background Atmosphere", "txt": "Grain"}, "223": {"desc": "A striped sunset above the horizon, and a perspective grid floor continuously advancing forward", "prompt": "An 80s synthwave-style background: in the middle of the screen is a horizon line; above it is a circular sunset whose lower half is cut by horizontal stripes, with a soft glow; below is a perspective-tilted grid floor whose grid lines continuously advance toward the viewer and fade out in the distance, creating a feeling of endlessly driving forward; the title floats above the sunset with a slight glow. (CSS: the floor is two sets of linear-gradient grid lines, with transform:perspective + rotateX(72deg), and keyframes advancing background-position by one grid length for a seamless loop; the far end fades out with a mask; the sunset stripes use a repeating-linear-gradient mask)", "tag": "CSS 3D", "style": "Retro Synthwave synthwave vaporwave Perspective Grid Floor Horizon Sunset 80s Retro Grid Horizon Perspective Background Atmosphere", "txt": "RETRO WAVE"}, "224": {"desc": "Soft-focus light spots of different sizes slowly float upward, fading in and out", "prompt": "In the background float more than ten circular light spots of different sizes with a soft-focus blur; each slowly floats upward from below at a different speed (about 7-14 seconds), drifting slightly left and right along the way, fading in as it appears and fading out near the top, each with different opacity, creating a dreamy, warm atmosphere; the title in the center stays clear. (CSS: each light spot uses CSS variables to set its size, horizontal position, duration, negative animation-delay and offset, with filter:blur, and keyframes control translate and opacity)", "tag": "CSS blur", "style": "Bokeh Light Spots Soft Focus Bubbles Floating Rise Dreamy Bokeh Lights Bubbles Floating Blur Background Atmosphere", "txt": "Bokeh"}, "226": {"desc": "A center point pulses regularly, and rings expand outward one after another and fade out", "prompt": "At the center of the screen is a solid dot that gently pulses regularly; from its position, thin rings continuously expand outward one after another, growing larger and gradually fading away, with multiple rings offset in time to form continuous ripples, like radar, sound waves, or a \"live\" signal; a short label can be placed on the center dot. (CSS: 3-4 rings share the same keyframes: scale 0.15 to 1.25, opacity 0.9 to 0, evenly offset with negative animation-delay; the center dot uses another scale keyframes)", "tag": "CSS keyframes", "style": "Concentric Circles Expand Pulse Radar Sound Waves Live Location Signal Pulse Rings Ripple Radar Signal Live Background Atmosphere", "txt": "Live"}, "227": {"desc": "Radial rays slowly rotate behind the title, brightest at the center and fading outward", "prompt": "Behind the title is a ring of ray stripes radiating outward from the center; the whole ring slowly rotates at a speed of about 30 seconds per revolution, brightest at the center and gradually blending into the background outward, like the spotlight effect of an award, prize draw, or celebration scene. (CSS: repeating-conic-gradient draws the radial stripes and is enlarged beyond the container, keyframes rotate 360deg linear infinite; a radial-gradient layer on top makes the center bright and the edges dark)", "tag": "conic-gradient", "style": "Rays Radiate Sunlight Rotating Celebration Award Prize Draw Sunburst Rays Rotating God Rays Conic Background Atmosphere", "txt": "WINNER"}, "228": {"desc": "Stars all over the sky twinkle individually, a meteor occasionally streaks past, and the starry sky shifts with slight parallax as the cursor moves", "prompt": "A night-sky background: darker at the top with a soft glow lower down, filled with more than two hundred stars of different sizes and brightness, each twinkling slowly at its own speed and phase; when the brightest few reach peak brightness, fine cross-shaped sparkles appear; every few seconds a meteor streaks from the upper right diagonally down to the lower left, trailing a fading tail; when the cursor moves, the starry sky makes reverse parallax shifts of different magnitudes depending on the stars' depths. (Canvas 2D: each star records its position, radius, depth, twinkle frequency and phase, with brightness = sin(time x frequency + phase); meteors are line segments drawn with createLinearGradient; parallax displacement is smoothed with lerp)", "tag": "Canvas 2D", "style": "Starry Sky Stars Twinkle Meteor Night Sky Universe Parallax Twinkling Stars Night Sky Shooting Star Canvas particles requestAnimationFrame Interactive Background Background Atmosphere", "txt": "Good Night"}, "229": {"desc": "Three layers of graphics, front, middle and back, move in reverse following the cursor at different magnitudes according to distance, creating a sense of depth", "prompt": "A Hero background made of three layers of decorative graphics: the far layer is a blurred large circle, the middle layer is a rounded square, and the front layer is a hollow ring, with the title sandwiched between the middle and front layers; when the cursor moves inside the section, each layer moves in the opposite direction from the cursor, with layers closer to the viewer moving more (for example far layer 15%, middle layer 45%, front layer 100%), and the title moves only slightly, creating a three-dimensional sense of depth, with smooth delayed following in the movement. (JS: mousemove calculates the cursor's ratio relative to the center, -0.5 to 0.5; each layer's translate = -ratio x that layer's coefficient, smoothed with a CSS transition or lerp)", "tag": "JS parallax", "style": "Parallax Depth Layers Three-Dimensional Mouse Cursor Mouse Parallax Depth Layers 3D Hero Background Atmosphere", "txt": "Depth"}, "230": {"desc": "A whole field of fine lines undulates like fabric, and the places the cursor passes are gently arched up", "prompt": "The entire background is about 26 horizontal fine lines, each undulating from the superposition of two sets of sine waves of different frequencies and flowing slowly over time, with adjacent lines slightly offset in phase, so the whole field looks like flowing fabric or terrain lines; among them, every few lines are accented with a thicker, brighter line; where the cursor passes, nearby lines are smoothly arched upward, and recover after it leaves. (Canvas 2D: each line takes 80 points, y = baseline + sin(x*f1 + t + j*phase) * A1 + sin(x*f2 - t + j*phase) * A2, minus a Gaussian function centered on the cursor times height)", "tag": "Canvas 2D", "style": "Lines Waves Undulate Fabric Terrain Contour Lines Wavy Lines Wave Field Terrain Canvas Interactive Background requestAnimationFrame Background Atmosphere", "txt": "Flow"}, "231": {"desc": "Geometric shapes such as circles, squares, triangles and rings randomly float and rotate slowly in the background", "prompt": "More than ten simple geometric shapes are scattered in the background: solid circles, rounded squares, triangles, hollow rings and crosses, of different sizes; on entrance each appears in sequence with an elastic scale-up, after which each shape continuously drifts slowly in a random direction and rotates, choosing a new random target on each round trip, looking natural and non-repetitive; the title sits in the middle. (GSAP: for each shape, gsap.to on x / y / rotation uses \"random(-40,40)\" strings, with duration random(3,6), ease sine.inOut, repeat:-1, yoyo:true, repeatRefresh:true; entrance with gsap.from scale:0 paired with back.out)", "tag": "repeatRefresh", "style": "Floating Geometric Shapes Random Decoration Background Floating Shapes Geometric Random Decoration Background Atmosphere", "txt": "Shapes"}, "232": {"desc": "There is a layer of thickness beneath the button; when pressed, the whole button presses down and the thickness disappears, like a physical key", "prompt": "A button with the feel of a physical key: below the button body is a layer of \"thickness\" in the same color family but darker (made with an unblurred shadow below), with another layer of soft shadow around the outside; when the mouse hovers, the button lifts slightly and the thickness increases; when pressed, the whole button presses down until almost flat, the thickness and shadow shrink, and it springs back on release. About 0.12 seconds, crisp and responsive. (CSS: box-shadow: 0 6px 0 darker color, 0 10px 20px semi-transparent; on :active, translateY(5px) and shrink the first shadow layer to 1px)", "tag": "CSS :active", "style": "Three-Dimensional Press Physical Key 3D Pressable Button Push Tactile Game Button", "txt": "Get Started Now"}, "233": {"desc": "On hover or click, the button is squashed flat like jelly, stretched long, then bounces back", "prompt": "When the mouse hovers over or clicks it, the button, like jelly, is first squashed horizontally flat (width 1.18, height 0.82), then stretched vertically long (width 0.85, height 1.15), then wobbles back and forth a few times with decreasing amplitude until it returns to its original shape; the whole sequence is about 0.7 seconds, bouncy and cute. (CSS keyframes: in sequence scale(1.18,.82) then (.85,1.15) then (1.08,.92) then (.97,1.03) then (1,1); when triggered by a click, first remove the class, force a reflow, then add it back so it can replay)", "tag": "CSS keyframes", "style": "Jelly Bounce Bouncy Squash Stretch Jelly Rubber Squash Stretch Bounce Button Button", "txt": "Try Clicking Me"}, "234": {"desc": "A ripple spreads out from the exact position the finger taps, the classic Material Design feedback", "prompt": "When the button is clicked, a circular ripple spreads out from the exact point the finger (cursor) pressed, semi-transparent, growing from small to large enough to cover the whole button while fading out at the same time, about 0.7 seconds; consecutive clicks can produce multiple ripples at once. (JS: on pointerdown, calculate the click position and the distance to the farthest corner x 2 as the diameter, insert a circular span, CSS keyframes scale 0 to 1 with opacity fading, and remove it on animationend; the button has overflow:hidden)", "tag": "JS + CSS", "style": "Ripple Water Wave Click Feedback Material Design Ripple Click Feedback Ink Button", "txt": "Submit Form"}, "235": {"desc": "Drag the round knob all the way to the end to confirm; if it does not reach the end it springs back, and the text has a shimmer hint", "prompt": "A capsule-shaped slide track, with a round handle on the left (with a right arrow inside), and a beam of light sweeps across the hint text in the middle from left to right; when the user drags the handle, the track the handle has passed is filled and the hint text gradually fades out; only releasing near the far right counts as confirmation - the whole track fills and the text becomes \"Done ✓\"; if released before reaching the end, the handle springs back to the start with elasticity. (GSAP Draggable type:\"x\", with bounds limiting it to the track, onDrag updates the filled width, onRelease checks whether it exceeds 85%; the shimmer uses background-clip:text with a moving gradient)", "tag": "Draggable", "style": "Slide Confirm Unlock Payment Drag Slide To Unlock Confirm Swipe Button Payment Button", "txt": "Slide to Pay"}, "236": {"desc": "Holding it down slowly fills the progress, releasing rolls it back, and only a full fill executes it, suitable for dangerous actions like deletion", "prompt": "A button for dangerous actions (such as deletion): an outline style; when the user holds it down, a fill layer fills the whole button from left to right at a constant speed over about 1.2 seconds, and the button shrinks slightly; if released midway, the fill quickly rolls back and nothing is executed; once fully filled, the button gives a slight bounce and the text becomes \"Deleted ✓\". This prevents accidental taps. (CSS: the fill layer has transform:scaleX(0); while held, a class changes it to scaleX(1) with a 1.2s linear transition; on release the class is removed and it rolls back with a shorter transition; JS starts a 1.2-second timer on pointerdown and cancels it on pointerup / pointerleave)", "tag": "CSS transition", "style": "Long Press Hold Confirm Delete Dangerous Action Progress Hold To Confirm Long Press Delete Destructive Button", "txt": "Hold to Delete"}, "237": {"desc": "On hover, the arrow on the right slides out to the right while a new arrow slides in from the left, and the text makes way", "prompt": "A capsule button with a right-pointing arrow to the right of the text; when the mouse hovers, the right arrow slides out of the button to the right and fades out, while another identical arrow slides in from outside the left of the button to the left of the text, and the text shifts right in sync to make way, like an arrow relay pushing forward; when the mouse leaves, it reverses back. About 0.4 seconds, ease-in-out. (CSS: the button has overflow:hidden; the two arrows and the text each have transform and transition settings, switching displacement on hover)", "tag": "CSS hover", "style": "Arrow Icon Slide In Slide Out Relay Icon Slide Arrow Button Hover CTA Button", "txt": "Learn More"}, "238": {"desc": "The border and glow brighten and dim like breathing; on hover it fills and glows strongly", "prompt": "A neon-style button: the thin border and text use an accent color, surrounded by a ring of soft outer glow and inner glow, with the halo brightening and dimming like breathing on a cycle of about 2.4 seconds; when the mouse hovers, the whole button fills, the text inverts to white, and it emits multiple layers of strong, wide-range glow. (CSS: multiple layers of box-shadow (including inset) create the glow, and keyframes change the halo size and opacity; on hover, the breathing animation stops and changes to a larger multi-layer box-shadow, with a 0.35 second transition)", "tag": "box-shadow", "style": "Neon Glow Halo Breathing Neon Glow Pulse Button Cyberpunk Button", "txt": "Join Us"}, "239": {"desc": "After pressing copy, the icon rotates into a checkmark, and a small \"Copied\" hint pops up above", "prompt": "A copy button beside a line of code (or text): when pressed, the copy icon rotates, shrinks and disappears, a check icon appears with an elastic scale-up, and the button background becomes the accent color; at the same time a small \"Copied\" hint box pops up above the button, and after about 1.5 seconds everything returns to its original state. (CSS: the two SVG icons are stacked in the same cell, using a class to switch transform and opacity, with a transition using a bouncy cubic-bezier(.3,1.5,.5,1); the hint box is absolutely positioned above the button; JS calls navigator.clipboard.writeText, then adds the class and removes it with setTimeout)", "tag": "CSS transition", "style": "Copy Clipboard Check Hint tooltip Feedback Copy To Clipboard Feedback Check Code Button", "txt": "npm i gsap"}, "240": {"desc": "Usually only a round \"+\" icon; on hover it expands to the right to reveal text, and the plus rotates", "prompt": "A floating action button that is usually a circle with only a \"+\"; when the mouse hovers, the button smoothly expands to the right into a capsule shape, revealing a text label (for example \"New Project\"), while the plus rotates 90 degrees at the same time; the text fades in only after the expansion is halfway; when the mouse leaves, it retracts into a circle. About 0.5 seconds. (CSS: the button has overflow:hidden, using max-width to transition from the circle's width to a larger value, the text opacity is paired with a transition-delay; the plus uses rotate(90deg))", "tag": "CSS max-width", "style": "Expand Floating Button FAB Plus Icon Button Expanding Icon Button Floating Action Reveal Label Button", "txt": "New Project"}, "241": {"desc": "Press send, and the paper plane flies away from the button; the text changes to \"Sent\" and then recovers", "prompt": "A send button with a paper plane icon on its left: when pressed, the button first gives a light press and rebound, the text fades out to the right, and the paper plane first pulls back to build momentum, then accelerates up and to the right, flying out of the button and disappearing; next the text changes to \"Sent\" and slides in from the left; after about 1 second the text changes back to the original content, and the paper plane flies back to its original position from the lower left. (GSAP timeline: button scale 0.94 to 1, text x and opacity, the paper plane uses keyframes going up and to the right on x/y/rotation accelerating with power2.in, then add() switches the text content; the button's overflow:hidden clips the plane as it flies out)", "tag": "GSAP timeline", "style": "Send Paper Plane Send Out Message Form Success Send Paper Plane Submit Button Success Button", "txt": "Send Message"}, "242": {"desc": "When checked, the box gives a bounce, the checkmark is drawn as if with a pen, and the item text gets a strikethrough", "prompt": "A checkbox for a to-do list: when clicked to check it, the box first shrinks and then bounces slightly larger (about 0.4 seconds), and its background fills; the checkmark inside is drawn from bottom-left to top-right as if with a pen; the item text on the right fades and gains a strikethrough line. When unchecked, it reverses back. (CSS: hide the native checkbox and customize the box and an SVG checkmark; the checkmark path uses stroke-dasharray and stroke-dashoffset going from full length to 0; :checked plus style switching; the box bounces with a scale keyframes; keep a :focus-visible outline for keyboard users)", "tag": "stroke-dashoffset", "style": "Checkbox Checkbox Check To-Do List todo Checkbox Check Animation Todo List Form Control", "txt": "Buy Coffee Beans Reply to Emails Tidy Desk"}, "243": {"desc": "A row of options has a slider block underneath; clicking one slides it over with a slight elasticity and changes its width", "prompt": "A capsule-shaped segmented control, for example \"Day / Week / Month / Year\"; beneath the current option is a solid slider block; when another option is clicked, the slider slides to the new position with a slight rebound and changes its width at the same time to fit the new option's text length; the selected text becomes a color that contrasts with the slider. About 0.45 seconds. (CSS: the slider is absolutely positioned; JS reads the clicked button's offsetLeft and offsetWidth into CSS variables, and transform:translateX(var(--x)) and width transition with cubic-bezier(.5,1.5,.5,1))", "tag": "CSS transition", "style": "Segmented Control Switch Tabs tabs Slider Segmented Control Tabs Pill Switcher iOS Form Control", "txt": "Day Week Month Year"}, "244": {"desc": "While typing a password, the strength bar below grows segment by segment, changing with strength and showing a hint", "prompt": "Below a password input field are four strength segments: as the user types, the strength is calculated in real time (whether the length reaches 8 characters, and whether it has uppercase letters, numbers and symbols); the more conditions met, the more segments grow out from left to right; the higher the strength, the stronger the segments' visual, and the text below shows in sequence \"Too Weak / Fair / Good / Very Strong\"; on the right of the input is an eye button to show/hide the password; when the input is focused its border lights up. (JS: the input event calculates a score of 0-4, sets data-level and each segment's class; newly lit segments grow with a scaleX 0 to 1 keyframes)", "tag": "JS + CSS", "style": "Password Strength Signup Validation Form Password Strength Meter Signup Validation Form Control", "txt": ""}, "245": {"desc": "While dragging the slider, a value bubble pops up above, moves with the handle, and shrinks back on release", "prompt": "A range slider: the portion of the track already dragged over is filled; when the handle is held or dragged, it enlarges slightly, and a value bubble with a small triangle pops up directly above it; the bubble moves horizontally with the handle and displays the number in real time; on release the bubble shrinks and fades out. (CSS: customize the track of input[type=range] and its ::-webkit-slider-thumb; the track fill uses a background linear-gradient with a CSS variable percentage; the bubble is an absolutely positioned output, with left = handle width / 2 + (track width - handle width) x percentage, popping with scale and opacity)", "tag": "input range", "style": "Slider Lever Value Bubble Range Volume Range Slider Tooltip Bubble Value Input Form Control", "txt": "Volume"}, "246": {"desc": "A four-box verification code; typing one box auto-advances to the next; the boxes jump up in sequence when correct, and the whole row shakes when wrong", "prompt": "A four-box verification code input: each box can hold only one digit; after typing, that box gives a light bounce and focus automatically advances to the next box; pressing Backspace in an empty box returns to the previous box and clears it; once all four boxes are filled it automatically verifies: when correct, each box jumps up in sequence and its background fills; when wrong, the whole row shakes left and right and the border changes to a warning style. (JS: each box has maxLength=1 and inputMode=\"numeric\"; the input event focuses the next box, keydown Backspace handles going back; the result triggers CSS keyframes with a class, staggering the jumps with animation-delay; on mobile the font size is at least 16px to avoid auto-zoom)", "tag": "JS + CSS", "style": "Verification Code OTP One-Time Password SMS Login PIN Code Input Verification Auto Focus Form Control", "txt": ""}, "247": {"desc": "Usually only a round magnifier button; clicking it expands it to the left into a search box", "prompt": "Search in a navigation bar: usually just a round magnifier button; when clicked, the button smoothly expands to the left into a long search box (about 0.5 seconds), the text inside the input fades in only after the expansion is halfway, the magnifier rotates 90 degrees and a ring border lights up around it; when the input loses focus and has no content, it retracts back into a round button. (CSS: the container has overflow:hidden, width transitions from the round button's width to the expanded width with cubic-bezier(.6,0,.2,1); the input opacity is paired with a transition-delay; JS toggles the class and focuses the input)", "tag": "CSS transition", "style": "Search Magnifier Expand Collapse Navigation Bar Expanding Search Bar Icon Input Header Form Control", "txt": "Search works..."}, "248": {"desc": "When a dropdown is opened, the panel pops out from the top, options slide in one after another, and the arrow flips", "prompt": "Dropdown menu: when the menu button is clicked, the arrow on the right flips 180 degrees, and the options panel below expands from its top edge with a slight bounce (scaleY 0.6 → 1, fading in), with the options inside sliding down and fading in one after another (each spaced about 0.05 seconds apart); when hovering over an option, its background lights up faintly; after a selection, the panel collapses and the button displays the selected value. (CSS: panel transform-origin: top, transition using cubic-bezier(.3,1.3,.5,1); each option sets --i, and on expansion transition-delay: calc(var(--i) × 0.05s))", "tag": "transition-delay", "style": "Dropdown Menu Expand Options Sequential Dropdown Select Menu Stagger Reveal Form Control", "txt": "Taipei Taichung Kaohsiung Hualien Tainan"}, "249": {"desc": "Type text and press Enter to turn it into a popping tag; press × or Backspace and the tag shrinks away", "prompt": "Tag input field: after the user types text and presses Enter (or a comma), the text becomes a capsule tag, enlarging from 0 with a bounce to appear in front of the input cursor; each tag has a × button on its right side, and when clicked — or when Backspace is pressed in an empty input — the last tag shrinks and fades out and the content behind it smoothly moves up to fill the gap; when the whole field is focused, its border lights up. (JS: keydown handles Enter / comma / Backspace, new elements are inserted before the input; CSS keyframes: entrance scale 0→1 using cubic-bezier(.3,1.6,.5,1), exit scale→0 using a negative margin-right to collapse, and the element is removed after animationend)", "tag": "JS + CSS", "style": "Tag tag chip Input Keywords Interests Tag Input Chips Token Field Form Control", "txt": "Design Motion Frontend Illustration Branding"}, "250": {"desc": "When switching radio options, the selected dot stretches into a droplet, slides to the new option, then bounces back into a circle", "prompt": "A set of vertically arranged radio options, where the selected dot is a separate solid small circle: when switching options, the small circle is first stretched into a vertically elongated droplet shape, slides in a straight line to the center of the new option's circle, and on arrival recovers into a circle with an elastic wobble, flowing over like a liquid; the selected outer ring changes style at the same time. (GSAP timeline: first scaleY 2.2 / scaleX 0.7, while tweening y to the new position with power3.inOut, finally scaleX/scaleY back to 1 using elastic.out(1.2,0.5); the native radio is hidden but keyboard operation is retained)", "tag": "GSAP elastic", "style": "Radio radio Options Droplet Liquid Stretch Liquid Radio Button Gooey Morph Form Control", "txt": "Standard Shipping Express Delivery Store Pickup"}, "251": {"desc": "When a file is dragged into the area, the border lights up and the icon floats up; after dropping, a file row appears and a checkmark pops in once the progress bar finishes", "prompt": "File drag-and-drop upload area: in the middle of a dashed border there is an upload icon and “Drag files here”; when a file is dragged over the area, the border becomes solid, the background lights up faintly, and the icon floats upward; after dropping, the area bounces lightly, a file information row (file name + progress bar) pops in from below at the bottom, the progress bar fills in about 1.3 seconds, a checkmark icon pops in on the right, and after staying for one second the file row moves up and fades out. Clicking the area also lets you select files. (JS: dragenter/dragover add a class, drop reads the file name; GSAP timeline chains the bounce, the file row entrance, the progress bar scaleX 0→1, and the checkmark with back.out)", "tag": "GSAP timeline", "style": "Upload File Drag-and-Drop Dragging Progress Bar Drag Drop File Upload Dropzone Progress Form Control", "txt": ""}, "252": {"desc": "A circular cursor that enlarges when passing over text, with colors inverting where it overlaps", "prompt": "The cursor is replaced with a solid circle that follows the mouse with a smooth delay; the circle uses the “difference” blend mode, and when it overlaps the text below, the colors of the text and background invert each other; when the cursor moves onto a large heading, the circle smoothly enlarges about three times so the inverted area covers more text, and shrinks back after leaving the heading. (CSS: the circle element has mix-blend-mode: difference, pointer-events: none; JS lerps toward the mouse coordinates every frame and detects whether it is within a heading's range to interpolate the scale; the container uses cursor: none to hide the native cursor)", "tag": "mix-blend-mode", "style": "Inverted Colors Inversion Blend Mode difference Cursor Circle Blend Mode Invert Cursor Hero Cursor Mouse", "txt": "INVERT"}, "253": {"desc": "When the cursor approaches a button it is attracted to it, deforms to wrap the whole button, and the button is also pulled slightly", "prompt": "A row of buttons in a navigation bar, with the cursor as a small circle: when the cursor approaches a button, the small circle is “sucked” over, deforms into a rounded rectangle that wraps the whole button, and its position still shifts slightly with the mouse inside the button; the button itself is also pulled slightly toward the mouse direction, and its text and background colors invert; when moving away from the button, the small circle shrinks back and the button bounces back to its original position. (GSAP: mousemove determines whether the cursor is within a button's range (with a little expansion), and if inside, tweens the cursor's x/y/width/height to the button's center and size + offset × 0.12, otherwise tweens back to a small circle; the button's x/y = offset × 0.15, power3.out)", "tag": "GSAP", "style": "Sticky Attraction Magnetic Deformation Wrap Navigation Sticky Cursor Magnetic Morph Nav Cursor Mouse", "txt": "Work About Contact"}, "254": {"desc": "A circular cursor stretches along its direction according to movement speed, and returns to a circle when it stops", "prompt": "A circular cursor follows the mouse with a smooth delay, calculating movement speed every frame: the faster it moves, the more the circle is stretched along the movement direction and flattened vertically, like elastic jelly; when the mouse stops, it slowly recovers into a perfect circle. (JS requestAnimationFrame: position lerps toward the target; speed = the length of this frame's displacement, angle = atan2(dy,dx); transform = translate → rotate(angle) → scale(1 + speed coefficient, 1 − speed coefficient × 0.45), and the speed coefficient itself is also lerped to avoid jitter)", "tag": "JS rAF", "style": "Velocity Stretch Elongation Elastic Direction Velocity Stretch Squash Cursor Elastic Cursor Mouse", "txt": "Stretch"}, "255": {"desc": "When the cursor moves onto different content, it becomes a large circle with text for the corresponding action, such as play, view, or drag", "prompt": "A card area in a portfolio, where the cursor is normally a small dot; when moving onto different types of content, the small dot elastically enlarges into a solid large circle, displaying the corresponding icon in the middle, with action text floating out below, for example a video shows “▶ Play”, a work shows “↗ View”, and a carousel shows “⇆ Drag”; when leaving the content it shrinks back to a small dot. (JS: each area sets its text and icon with a data-cursor attribute, mousemove detects the current area and updates the cursor content; CSS: the large circle scale 0 → 1 uses cubic-bezier(.3,1.5,.5,1), and the text fades in and moves up)", "tag": "JS + CSS", "style": "Context Label Cursor Play View Drag Portfolio Contextual Label Cursor View Play Drag Portfolio Cursor Mouse", "txt": ""}, "256": {"desc": "Two thin lines, horizontal and vertical, follow the cursor, with coordinate numbers displayed in real time beside it", "prompt": "On a background with faint grid lines, a horizontal line and a vertical line span the whole area and intersect at the cursor position, with a small circle at the intersection; at the lower right of the cursor there is a small label that displays the current X and Y coordinate numbers in real time in a monospace font (converted to 1920 × 1080), and near the edges the label automatically tucks inward so it does not go off screen. Suitable for technology, design tools, or portfolio homepages. (JS: on mousemove, transform moves the two lines and the label, coordinates = cursor position / container width and height × 1920, 1080, padded with zeros using padStart)", "tag": "JS + CSS", "style": "Cross Crosshair Coordinates Aiming Technology Blueprint Crosshair Coordinates Cursor Blueprint Tech Cursor Mouse", "txt": "Precision"}, "257": {"desc": "A pair of large eyes whose pupils keep staring and turning toward the cursor, blinking occasionally", "prompt": "A pair of large eyes (eye whites + pupils, with a small highlight dot on each pupil), whose pupils keep turning toward the cursor direction: the farther the cursor, the closer the pupils get to the edge of the eye socket, and when the cursor is directly in front of the eyes the pupils return to the center; every few seconds both eyes blink quickly together once (the eyes flatten vertically and recover, about 0.15 seconds). Suitable for a mascot, a 404 page, or playful interaction. (JS: each eye calculates the atan2 angle from its center point, the distance is min(1, distance / range) × maximum offset, and the pupils are moved with transform; blinking toggles a class on scaleY)", "tag": "JS atan2", "style": "Eyes Pupils Following Staring Cute Mascot 404 Googly Eyes Follow Cursor Mascot Cursor Mouse", "txt": ""}, "258": {"desc": "The cursor becomes a round magnifying glass, and the content inside the lens is shown enlarged", "prompt": "The cursor becomes a round magnifying glass with a border and shadow, and inside the lens the content below the cursor is displayed enlarged about 2.2 times; when moving, the lens content shifts in sync so small text or product details can be seen clearly. (JS + CSS: place a copy of the content inside the lens, set to the same width and height as the original content, transform-origin: 0 0, transform = translate(radius − cursor x × magnification, radius − cursor y × magnification) scale(magnification); the lens has border-radius: 50%, overflow: hidden, pointer-events: none)", "tag": "JS + CSS", "style": "Magnifying Glass Magnify Lens Details Product Magnifier Lens Zoom Loupe Cursor Product Cursor Mouse", "txt": "Magnified View"}, "260": {"desc": "A trail of balls follows the cursor, merging and stretching like goo between each other", "prompt": "Behind the cursor follows a string of balls decreasing in size, the first tightly following the mouse and each subsequent one following the one before it, forming a tail; through a blur-plus-contrast filter the balls fuse together, looking like a blob of goo being stretched long and pulling into thin strands, and shrinking back into a blob when it stops. Foreground text uses a blend mode, and the parts covered by the goo are inverted. (SVG filter: feGaussianBlur with stdDeviation about 6 + feColorMatrix amplifying alpha (for example 0 0 0 22 −9) creates the goo effect, applied to the container wrapping all the balls; JS makes each ball lerp toward the previous one every frame)", "tag": "SVG goo filter", "style": "Goo Fusion Trail Liquid Gooey Blob Trail Cursor SVG Filter Liquid Cursor Mouse", "txt": "Gooey"}, "261": {"desc": "Click anywhere on the screen and small patterns such as hearts and stars spray out from there and fall down", "prompt": "When clicking anywhere inside the area, about 7 small patterns (hearts, stars, small flowers) spray out from the click position, each flying out into a fan-shaped range above with random size and angle, and after reaching the highest point they fall while fading out; at the same time there is a thin ring at the click point that expands and disappears. Suitable for cute-style websites or like feedback. (GSAP: each small pattern uses fromTo starting at scale 0 at the click point, the first keyframe segment flies out to a random angle and distance with power3.out, the second segment goes down and opacity 0; the element is removed when the animation ends)", "tag": "GSAP keyframes", "style": "Click Spray Hearts Stars Confetti Feedback Cute Click Burst Hearts Confetti Pop Particles Cursor Mouse", "txt": "Click!"}, "262": {"desc": "When hovering over an image, the image slowly zooms in slightly within a fixed frame, and the title floats up from the bottom", "prompt": "A row of image cards, each image placed in a fixed-size, rounded frame (overflow: hidden): when the mouse hovers, the frame size does not change, and the image inside slowly enlarges to 1.1 times over about 0.8 seconds with a decelerating curve; the title bar at the bottom of the frame (with a gradient background from transparent to translucent) simultaneously moves up slightly from below and becomes completely clear; when moving away, the image slowly shrinks back. (CSS: container overflow: hidden; img sets transition: transform .8s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1), and when the container is :hover the img has transform: scale(1.1); the title's translateY and opacity transition together)", "tag": "CSS hover", "style": "hover Enlarge Zoom Image Zoom Inside Frame Fixed Frame overflow hidden Portfolio Product Image Image Zoom Hover Scale Thumbnail Gallery Image Media", "txt": "Seaside Forest City"}, "263": {"desc": "Hover over an image to zoom in two times, with the enlarged position following the cursor to view product details", "prompt": "A large product image: when the mouse moves into the image, the image smoothly enlarges to about 2.2 times within the original frame, and the center point of enlargement follows the cursor position — moving the cursor to the upper left shows the upper-left details, and moving it to the lower right shows the lower-right details; when the mouse leaves it shrinks back to the original size. There is a small hint “Hover to see details” in the lower right corner, which fades out when zoomed. (JS + CSS: on mousemove, set transform-origin to the cursor's percentage position in the image, the container scales to scale(2.2) on :hover with a 0.5 second transition; container overflow: hidden, cursor: zoom-in)", "tag": "transform-origin", "style": "Zoom View Details Product Image Ecommerce Follow Cursor Pan Zoom Pan Hover Product Detail Ecommerce Image Media", "txt": ""}, "264": {"desc": "Images are normally low-saturation and slightly dark, and on hover regain vividness and enlarge slightly", "prompt": "A row of team or work photos, normally presented in low saturation and slightly dark so the whole row looks quiet and unified; when the mouse hovers over one, that photo regains its full saturation and brightness within about 0.6 seconds and enlarges slightly within the frame to 1.05 times, and the name label at the bottom floats up. (CSS: img defaults to filter: grayscale(.9) brightness(.8), on :hover filter: none and scale(1.05), with filter and transform transitioning together)", "tag": "CSS filter", "style": "Grayscale Desaturate Saturation Awaken Filter Portfolio Team Photos Grayscale Saturate Filter Hover Team Image Media", "txt": "Spring Summer Autumn"}, "265": {"desc": "When hovering over an e-commerce product card, it switches to a second-angle photo, and the dots below switch along with it", "prompt": "E-commerce product card: above is the main product image, and when the mouse hovers over the card, a second photo (for example a worn or back-angle view) fades in and shrinks back from 1.08 times to the original size, while the main image simultaneously fades out and enlarges slightly, forming a soft image swap; the two small dot indicators below the image switch along to show which image is current; the product name and price are displayed below the card. (CSS: the two images are stacked absolutely positioned in the same frame, on :hover their opacity and scale are exchanged, transition about 0.5–0.7 seconds)", "tag": "CSS hover", "style": "Product Ecommerce Second Image Image Swap Switch Image Swap Hover Product Card Ecommerce Second Image Image Media", "txt": "Linen Shirt"}, "266": {"desc": "A video thumbnail is normally still; on hover the play button shrinks and disappears, the picture starts playing, and the progress bar advances", "prompt": "Video thumbnail card: normally the picture is slightly dark and still, with a round play button in the middle and the duration shown in the lower right corner; when the mouse hovers, the play button shrinks and fades out, the picture brightens and starts playing (in the demo a slow push-in is used instead), and a progress bar appears at the bottom and starts advancing; when moving away it pauses and returns to the still state. (Implementation: on hover call video.play(), on leave pause() and reset currentTime to zero; the play button transitions with scale and opacity; the video is set to muted and playsinline so it can autoplay)", "tag": "CSS hover", "style": "Video Preview Autoplay Thumbnail Play Button YouTube Video Preview Hover Play Thumbnail Image Media", "txt": "Travel Journal"}, "267": {"desc": "Click a thumbnail and it smoothly enlarges from its original position to the center of the screen, with the background darkening; click again and it shrinks back", "prompt": "A row of square thumbnails; when clicking any one, that image smoothly enlarges from its original position and size to a large size in the center of the screen (about 0.55 seconds, easing in and out), while a translucent overlay is laid behind it darkening the other content; clicking the large image or the overlay makes the image smoothly shrink back to its original position in the thumbnail row and the overlay fade out. (GSAP Flip: Flip.getState records the thumbnail → add the “enlarged” class (changed to absolute positioning centered, larger size) → Flip.from tweens it; reverse when collapsing; the overlay uses an opacity transition)", "tag": "Flip", "style": "Lightbox lightbox Zoom Image View Album Modal Zoom Gallery Photo Viewer Flip Image Media", "txt": ""}, "268": {"desc": "Click a thumbnail below and the large image pushes in from the side to change, shrinking back slightly, while the indicator bar slides to the current thumbnail", "prompt": "Product album: one large image above and a row of thumbnails below; when clicking a thumbnail, the new large image pushes in from the corresponding direction (from the right when clicking forward, from the left when clicking backward), the old image moves out slightly in the opposite direction, and inside the new image it simultaneously shrinks slowly back from 1.25 times to the original size, adding a sense of depth; in the thumbnail row the current one becomes fully opaque and the others translucent, and an indicator bar below slides and aligns to the current thumbnail; it can also auto-play as a carousel. (GSAP: the new image fromTo xPercent ±100 → 0, the old image to xPercent ∓30, power3.inOut 0.6 seconds; the indicator bar transitions with CSS transform and width)", "tag": "GSAP", "style": "Album Thumbnails Large Image Product Images Carousel Gallery Thumbnails Slider Product Images Carousel Image Media", "txt": ""}, "269": {"desc": "An image is cut into vertical strips that slide away in sequence, one up and one down, revealing the next image", "prompt": "An image carousel transition: the current image is cut into 6 equal-width vertical strips, and when changing to the next image, these strips in sequence (each spaced about 0.06 seconds apart) slide out of the screen alternating one up and one down, revealing the next image underneath, while the next image simultaneously shrinks slowly back from 1.15 times to the original size. (Implementation: each vertical strip is an overflow: hidden container, with the same image inside shifted left by “strip width × index” so that assembled they form a complete image; GSAP applies yPercent ±110 to all strips, stagger 0.06, power3.in)", "tag": "GSAP stagger", "style": "Slice Vertical Strips Transition Image Change Blinds Slice Strips Image Transition Slideshow Venetian Image Media", "txt": ""}, "270": {"desc": "A stack of slightly crooked Polaroid photos; click and the top one is pulled out and tucked back to the bottom", "prompt": "A stack of Polaroid-style photos (with a wide border all around and a small caption written in the wider space at the bottom), each slightly crooked at a different angle and stacked together; when clicked, the top one is pulled out to the right and rotated, then returns to the very bottom of the stack, while the other photos simultaneously adjust their positions and angles to fill in, forming a shuffle effect that can be clicked repeatedly. (GSAP timeline: the top one x +120%, rotation 18 → adjust z-index to place it at the bottom → return to the stack position; each photo sets rotation and small x/y offsets according to stacking order)", "tag": "GSAP timeline", "style": "Polaroid Photo Stack Shuffle Album Polaroid Photo Stack Shuffle Deck Image Media", "txt": ""}, "271": {"desc": "On hover, an image splits into two color layers offset left and right, flickering in segments like a bad signal", "prompt": "When the mouse hovers over an image it triggers a glitch effect: the image overlays two copies in different color versions, stacked on the original with a “screen” blend mode, each offset left and right by a few percent, using clip-path to show only random horizontal bands, flickering and jumping rapidly; the original image itself also jitters slightly left and right; the title text in the middle shows two color edges offset left and right; when moving away it returns to normal. (CSS: the two copies use filter: sepia + saturate + hue-rotate to make different color versions, mix-blend-mode: screen; keyframes combined with steps() change transform and clip-path: inset(...))", "tag": "CSS clip-path", "style": "Glitch glitch Offset Color Version Signal Cyberpunk Glitch Image RGB Split Distortion Cyberpunk Image Media", "txt": "SIGNAL"}, "272": {"desc": "When scrolling down, a card flips in 3D to its back, while enlarging slightly", "prompt": "A card is located in the center of the screen, its front an image and its back text (the back uses an accent color): when the user scrolls down, the card flips in 3D along the vertical axis by 180 degrees according to scroll progress, while enlarging from 0.85 times to 1 times; halfway through scrolling it is exactly side-on to the viewer, and when scrolling is complete the back is fully displayed; scrolling back flips it back to the front. (GSAP ScrollTrigger scrub: the container is pinned or sticky, timeline fromTo rotationY 0 → 180; the parent sets perspective, the card transform-style: preserve-3d, both front and back faces backface-visibility: hidden, the back pre-rotated rotateY(180deg))", "tag": "ScrollTrigger", "style": "Flip Flip Over 3D Card Front and Back Scroll Scroll Flip Card 3D RotateY Scroll Trigger ScrollTrigger", "txt": "Back Story"}, "273": {"desc": "A 3D cube rotates with scrolling, each face written with a different keyword", "prompt": "In the center of the screen is a 3D cube, its six faces each written with a keyword and using a different theme color: as the user scrolls down, the cube tilts slightly down (rotateX −20 degrees) and rotates around the vertical axis, turning 270 degrees according to scroll progress so each face turns in sequence to face front. (GSAP ScrollTrigger scrub: the cube has transform-style: preserve-3d, its six faces are composed with rotateY / rotateX ± 90 degrees plus translateZ(half the side length); scrolling tweens rotationY)", "tag": "ScrollTrigger", "style": "Cube 3D Rotation Block cube Scroll Scroll Rotate Cube Faces Scroll Trigger ScrollTrigger", "txt": "Design Develop Motion Brand Strategy Test"}, "274": {"desc": "A huge title keeps enlarging with scrolling, as if the camera passes through a letter into the next screen", "prompt": "A huge English title (for example ZOOM) is in the center of the screen, and when the user scrolls down the title starts enlarging, enlarging faster the more they scroll (an accelerating curve), finally enlarging to several tens of times, as if the camera passes through the gap in the middle of a letter, and after the screen is filled by the letter it transitions to the next section of content (the next section fades in from behind and enlarges from 0.8 times to 1 times). (GSAP ScrollTrigger scrub: inside a sticky area, fromTo scale 1 → 38, ease power2.in, transform-origin aligned to the letter gap to pass through; the next section fades in after 70% progress)", "tag": "ScrollTrigger", "style": "Enlarge Pass Through Large Text Camera Transition Zoom Through Text Scale Scroll Transition Scroll Trigger ScrollTrigger", "txt": ""}, "275": {"desc": "An image list skews with speed when scrolling fast, and returns to straight when it stops", "prompt": "A scrollable row of image cards, normally arranged neatly; when the user scrolls quickly, all cards skew vertically (skewY) according to scroll speed, the faster the scroll the more the skew, the direction following the scroll direction, up to about 12 degrees; when scrolling slows or stops it smoothly returns to straight, bringing out inertia and a sense of speed. (GSAP: in ScrollTrigger.create's onUpdate, get self.getVelocity(), convert it to an angle and clamp it, and use gsap.quickTo(element, \"skewY\", {duration: .5, ease: \"power3.out\"}) to set it smoothly)", "tag": "getVelocity", "style": "Tilt Skew Velocity Inertia skew Scroll Scroll Velocity Skew Images List Scroll Trigger ScrollTrigger", "txt": "Mountain Sea City Forest"}, "276": {"desc": "Letters scattered around, flipped and scaled, fly back into place with scrolling to form a title", "prompt": "Each letter of a title starts randomly scattered around the screen, each with a different rotation angle, scale size, and transparency; when the user scrolls down, the letters in random order fly back in sequence to their original positions, straighten, and recover their size and opacity, assembling into the complete title; scrolling back scatters them again. (GSAP ScrollTrigger scrub: SplitText splits the characters, timeline.from(letters, { x/y/rotation/scale use functions returning random values, opacity: 0, stagger: {each: .02, from: \"random\"} }))", "tag": "ScrollTrigger", "style": "Scattered Assemble Combine Letters Fly Back Piece Together Scattered Letters Assemble Scroll Scroll Trigger ScrollTrigger", "txt": "ASSEMBLE"}, "277": {"desc": "A shape morphs in sequence with scrolling into a star, a heart, and a square, rotating as it morphs", "prompt": "In the center of the screen is a solid circular SVG shape, and as the user scrolls down it smoothly morphs in sequence into a five-pointed star, a heart, and a rounded square, rotating 90 degrees with each morph; the morph progress is fully controlled by scrolling, and scrolling back morphs it in reverse. (GSAP MorphSVGPlugin + ScrollTrigger scrub: the timeline in sequence does to(path, {morphSVG: the d of the next shape, rotation: \"+=90\", transformOrigin: \"50% 50%\"}))", "tag": "MorphSVG", "style": "Morph Shape morph Star Heart SVG Scroll Scroll Shape Morph Scroll Trigger ScrollTrigger", "txt": ""}, "278": {"desc": "Cards stacked together spread out into a fan with scrolling", "prompt": "Five image cards start neatly stacked in a pile; when the user scrolls down, the cards, pivoting on a point below their bottom, spread out to the left and right like opening a fan: the middle card does not move, the outer cards rotate at larger angles (each differing by about 14 degrees), while displacing to both sides and downward; scrolling back retracts them into a stack. (GSAP ScrollTrigger scrub: card transform-origin: 50% 120%, fromTo rotation / x / y calculated with a function according to index (i − middle index))", "tag": "ScrollTrigger", "style": "Fan Spread Cards Stacked Cards Works Scroll Scroll Fan Out Cards Spread Scroll Trigger ScrollTrigger", "txt": "Seaside Forest Night Sky Afternoon City"}, "279": {"desc": "Section headings go from blurred to clear as they scroll into view, and blur again as they scroll out", "prompt": "Several large headings in a long page: each heading is blurred, transparent, and slightly smaller when it scrolls in from below the screen, becomes clearer the closer it gets to the center of the screen, and is completely clear at the center; continuing to scroll up out of the screen it gradually blurs, fades out, and enlarges slightly, like a camera focusing as it sweeps past, guiding the gaze to stay on the current section. (GSAP ScrollTrigger scrub: each heading start \"top bottom\", end \"bottom top\", the timeline first fromTo filter blur(12px) → blur(0), opacity 0 → 1, scale .92 → 1, then to blur(12px), opacity 0, scale 1.06)", "tag": "ScrollTrigger", "style": "Blur Focus Clear blur Depth of Field Scroll Blur To Focus Scroll Depth Scroll Trigger ScrollTrigger", "txt": "Slowly See Clearly Then Leave"}, "280": {"desc": "A line of text moves along a curved line, with scrolling deciding how far it runs", "prompt": "In the screen there is a curved wavy line spanning across (a faint thin line), and a line of text is arranged hugging this curve; when the user scrolls down, the text flows along the curve from right to left, the text turns with the curve where it bends, scroll speed determines text movement speed, and scrolling back reverses it. (SVG: <path id> + <text><textPath href=\"#id\">; GSAP ScrollTrigger scrub tweens the textPath's startOffset attribute from 100% → −100%)", "tag": "SVG textPath", "style": "Curve Path Text Marquee textPath Wave Scroll Text On Path Curve Scroll Scroll Trigger ScrollTrigger", "txt": "Follow the curve"}, "281": {"desc": "The whole screen is cut down the middle into left and right doors that pull open to the sides with scrolling, revealing the next section", "prompt": "A transition between two sections of content: the previous section is a full screen of an accent color, with a huge character in the middle; when the user scrolls down, this screen is cut vertically from the exact center into left and right doors (the big character is also cut in half along with it), and the two doors slide open to the left and right sides according to scroll progress, revealing the next section behind, while the next section simultaneously enlarges from 0.8 times and becomes clear. (GSAP ScrollTrigger scrub: two blocks each 50% wide with overflow: hidden on the left and right, inside each placing one copy of the same big character at 200% width (the left aligned left, the right aligned right) so it looks like the same character; the timeline moves the two doors to xPercent −100 / 100)", "tag": "ScrollTrigger", "style": "Double Doors Opening Pull Open Split Transition Reveal Split Doors Curtain Reveal Scroll Transition Scroll Trigger ScrollTrigger", "txt": "Welcome"}, "282": {"desc": "On hover, a title is cut along its horizontal midline into upper and lower halves that offset in opposite directions, revealing a line of small text in the middle", "prompt": "A large title, which when the mouse hovers is cut along the text's horizontal midline into upper and lower halves: the upper half offsets to the upper left, the lower half offsets to the lower right (about 0.5 seconds, easing in and out), and in the gap that cracks open between the two halves, a line of small text (for example OPEN) unfolds vertically and fades in; when moving away the two halves rejoin. (CSS: the same text stacked in two layers, one layer clip-path: inset(0 0 50% 0) showing only the top half, the other inset(50% 0 0 0) showing only the bottom half, on :hover each transforms and displaces in the opposite direction)", "tag": "clip-path", "style": "Cut Apart Split Top Bottom Offset Title clip-path Split Text Slice Hover Reveal hover Hovering Hover Over", "txt": "SPLIT"}, "283": {"desc": "On hover, letter spacing slowly pulls open and font weight becomes bolder, like taking a deep breath", "prompt": "Text in a navigation bar or large menu: when the mouse hovers over an item, the letter spacing smoothly pulls open from 0 to about 0.35em, the font weight changes from thin to bold, and the text becomes clearer, expanding like taking a deep breath; when moving away it retracts. About 0.5 seconds, with a decelerating curve. (CSS: transition letter-spacing and font-weight (using a variable font gives the smoothest effect), :hover changes the values)", "tag": "letter-spacing", "style": "Letter Spacing Pull Open Font Weight Breathing Menu Navigation Letter Spacing Tracking Expand Weight Hover Menu hover Hovering Hover Over", "txt": "ABOUT WORK CONTACT"}, "284": {"desc": "When hovering over a list row, the background color brushes in from the left, the text makes way to the right, and an arrow slides out", "prompt": "A list of service items, each row with a number, an item name, and an arrow on the right, with thin divider lines between rows: when the mouse hovers over a row, a solid background color brushes in from the left to fill the whole row, the item name moves a little to the right to make way, the arrow on the right slides in from the left and appears, and the text color inverts to stay readable; when moving away the background color retracts to the right. About 0.5 seconds. (CSS: inside each row an absolutely positioned background layer transform: scaleX(0), on hover scaleX(1) with transform-origin from left; on leave transform-origin changes to right, forming “in from the left, out to the right”)", "tag": "CSS hover", "style": "List Rows Service Items Menu Background Fill Arrow List Row Hover Fill Sweep Arrow Services Menu hover Hovering Hover Over", "txt": "Brand Identity Website Design Motion Graphics Packaging Design"}, "285": {"desc": "On hovering over icons, each performs a small action matching its meaning: a bell shakes, a heart jumps, a gear turns, a trash can lifts its lid", "prompt": "A row of function icon buttons (notifications, favorites, settings, delete); when the mouse hovers, the icon's background lights up, and each performs a micro-animation matching its meaning: the bell shakes left and right a few times pivoting on its top, then stops; the heart fills and jumps once; the gear's teeth rotate 90 degrees with a little bounce; the trash can's lid lifts open at an angle pivoting on its left end. It makes the interface livelier without being distracting. (CSS: specific parts of the SVG icons set transform-origin (remember transform-box: fill-box for elements inside SVG), on :hover apply each one's keyframes or transform transition)", "tag": "CSS keyframes", "style": "Icon icon Micro-animation Bell Heart Gear Trash Can Icon Micro Animation Bell Heart Gear Trash Hover hover Hovering Hover Over", "txt": ""}, "286": {"desc": "Image cards normally only show a title; on hover an information panel slides up from the bottom, while the image moves up and enlarges", "prompt": "A row of vertical image cards, normally only a title bar is exposed at the bottom of the card; when the mouse hovers, the translucent frosted information panel at the bottom slides all the way up, displaying the title, a short description, and a “View →” link, while the image behind it moves up slightly and enlarges; when moving away the panel slides back leaving only the title. About 0.5 seconds. (CSS: panel transform: translateY(calc(100% − title bar height)), on :hover translateY(0); the panel uses a translucent background + backdrop-filter: blur; the image scale 1.08 + translateY)", "tag": "CSS hover", "style": "Card Information Panel Slide Up Description Work Card Info Slide Up Overlay Details Hover hover Hovering Hover Over", "txt": "Seaside Forest Night Sky"}, "287": {"desc": "When hovering over a round social icon, its background fills up from below, the icon swaps upward for another one, and the button floats up slightly", "prompt": "A row of round social icons in the footer (thin outline border, line icons in the middle): when the mouse hovers over an icon, a solid background rises from the bottom of the circle to fill it, the original icon slides up and out, an inverted-color version of the same icon slides in from below to replace it, and the whole button floats up slightly; when moving away it reverses back. About 0.45 seconds. (CSS: circle overflow: hidden, background layer translateY(101%) → 0; two icons stacked in the same cell, one moving up and out, the other moving in from below)", "tag": "CSS hover", "style": "Social Icon icon Fill Footer IG Threads Social Icon Fill Hover Footer hover Hovering Hover Over", "txt": ""}, "288": {"desc": "When hovering over key words in a paragraph, a stroke like a highlighter pen sweeps behind them from left to right", "prompt": "Several key words in a paragraph of text; when the mouse hovers over them, behind them a color block with a slight slant, a little lower than the text's midline, sweeps quickly like a highlighter pen from left to right, and the text color inverts at the same time to stay readable; when moving away the color block retracts. About 0.55 seconds. (CSS: the mark element's background uses linear-gradient to draw a color band with a slanted edge, background-size transitions from 0% to 100%, background-position set lower so it looks like a hand-drawn highlighter)", "tag": "background-size", "style": "Highlighter Mark Highlighting highlight Key Point Highlighter Marker Hover Emphasis Text hover Hovering Hover Over", "txt": "Good Design Is Easy To Grasp At A Glance"}, "289": {"desc": "A collectible card tilts in 3D following the cursor, and the iridescent foil shine and reflections on its surface flow with the angle", "prompt": "A collectible card (an image above, a title and number below) tilts in 3D space following the cursor (up to about 13 degrees); the card's surface has a layer of iridescent holographic foil shine, the foil shine position follows the cursor movement, the more it tilts the more obvious the foil shine, and there is also a soft reflection following the cursor position; when the cursor leaves the card straightens and the foil shine fades. (CSS + JS: mousemove calculates the cursor's relative position on the card 0~1, sets rotateX/rotateY and CSS variables --px, --py; the foil layer is iridescent stripes of repeating-linear-gradient, mix-blend-mode: color-dodge, background-position using --px/--py; the reflection layer is a radial-gradient overlaid with overlay; the parent sets perspective)", "tag": "mix-blend-mode", "style": "Holographic Foil Card Iridescent Foil Card Game Pokemon Tilt Reflection Holographic Foil Card Tilt Glare Shiny Trading Card hover Hovering Hover Over", "txt": "HOLO"}, "290": {"desc": "When you hover over a link in an article, a small card pops up above it, previewing the linked page's image and title", "prompt": "An underlined link in a paragraph of an article: when the mouse hovers over it (or it receives keyboard focus), a preview mini-card pops up directly above the link with a slight elasticity, containing the linked page's thumbnail, title and URL, appearing by enlarging and moving up from a slightly smaller, slightly lower, transparent state; when the mouse moves away it shrinks back and fades out. Suitable for external links in blogs, wikis or portfolios. (CSS: the preview card is absolutely positioned above the link with transform-origin at the bottom center, scale .9 + translateY → none, transition using cubic-bezier(.3,1.4,.5,1); trigger it with :has(a:hover) or :focus-within)", "tag": ":has()", "style": "Link Preview Pop-out Mini Card popover tooltip Hyperlink Link Preview Hover Card Wiki hover Hover Mouseover", "txt": "Hannah"}, "291": {"desc": "When you hover over a cell in a table, its entire row and column light up faintly, and that cell enlarges to stand out", "prompt": "A data table: when the mouse hovers over a cell, the entire row and column containing that cell light up faintly to form a cross, and the cell being pointed at fills with an accent background color, its text becomes bold and it enlarges slightly, so you can quickly cross-check the row heading and column heading; as you move to other cells the cross moves with it, and when you leave the table everything resets. (JS: on pointerover, find the td's cellIndex and its containing tr, and add a class to each; CSS: .row and .col use a very faint translucent background color, the pointed-at cell uses the accent background color + scale(1.12), transition 0.25 seconds)", "tag": "JS + CSS", "style": "Table Data Row Column Highlight Crosshair Table Row Column Highlight Crosshair Hover Data hover Hover Mouseover", "txt": ""}, "292": {"desc": "The strokes of the text are drawn one stroke at a time as if written with a pen, then fill in once finished", "prompt": "A piece of text (for example a signature or \"Thank you\") presented in a handwritten-style font: at first you see only blank space, then the outline strokes of the text are drawn along the letterforms one stroke at a time (about 2.4 seconds), as if someone is writing with a pen; after the strokes are drawn, the inside of the letters fades in to fill them. (SVG: set stroke and fill on the <text>; use a stroke-dasharray equal to or greater than the total path length, and tween stroke-dashoffset from the total length to 0; after drawing, fill-opacity 0 → 1. For greater precision, convert the text to a path and use DrawSVG)", "tag": "stroke-dashoffset", "style": "Handwriting Signature Stroke Drawing Writing Handwriting Signature Stroke Draw Text SVG Text Heading Animated Text", "txt": "Thank you"}, "293": {"desc": "Each character's weight changes in turn, like a wave sweeping from left to right", "prompt": "Each character of a heading alternates in font weight between the thinnest and the boldest, with adjacent characters delayed in sequence, so it looks like a wave of thickness continuously sweeping from left to right; at its boldest, a character also turns into the accent color. (CSS: use a font that supports variable font weight, split each character into its own element, share one keyframes that varies font-weight between 100 ↔ 900, with animation-delay increasing by index)", "tag": "variable font", "style": "Font Weight Thickness Variable Font Wave Breathing Variable Font Weight Wave Breathing Text Heading Animated Text", "txt": "WEIGHT"}, "294": {"desc": "The cursor is like a lamp, and the text's long shadow always extends in the direction opposite the cursor", "prompt": "There is a large heading in a section, and the cursor position is a small glowing light source: behind the text is a long shadow made of multiple shadow layers, and the shadow always extends in the direction \"away from the cursor\", with layers farther away becoming fainter in color; as the cursor moves, the shadow's direction turns in real time to follow, as if the light source is moving around the text. (JS: on mousemove, compute the direction vector of the cursor relative to the text's center, and generate 18 layers of text-shadow, each layer's offset = direction × layer number, with the color gradually fading by layer number)", "tag": "text-shadow", "style": "Light Source Projection Shadow Long Shadow 3D Cursor Light Source Long Shadow Cursor 3D Text Text Heading Animated Text", "txt": "SHADOW"}, "295": {"desc": "A landscape image fills the inside of large text, and the image slowly pans and zooms inside the letters", "prompt": "An extra-large, extra-bold English heading whose letters are filled with a landscape photo (the image is not visible anywhere outside the letters); the photo slowly pans and enlarges slightly inside the letters, going back and forth about once every 9 seconds, like looking at scenery through a text-shaped window; there is a very faint thin outline around the outer edges of the letters. (CSS: color:transparent + background-image + background-clip:text, with keyframes changing background-position and background-size)", "tag": "background-clip", "style": "Image Text Fill Knockout Background Text Mask Image Text Background Clip Knockout Mask Text Heading Animated Text", "txt": "WILD"}, "296": {"desc": "Each character in turn becomes clear and settles into place from a blurred, slightly larger state", "prompt": "Each character of a heading in turn changes from a \"blurred, transparent, slightly larger, slightly lower\" state to become clear and settle into position, with about 0.07 seconds between each character, giving an overall soft, refined feel; after lingering for a while, they blur out in sequence and replay. (GSAP + SplitText: fromTo on the characters {opacity:0, filter:\"blur(10px)\", y:\".25em\", scale:1.15} → {opacity:1, filter:\"blur(0px)\", y:0, scale:1}, ease power2.out, stagger 0.07)", "tag": "SplitText", "style": "Blur Emergence Letter by Letter Soft Entrance Blur In Letters Soft Reveal Stagger Text Heading Animated Text", "txt": "Slowly Emerging"}, "297": {"desc": "A word is struck through with one stroke, and a new word is written out above it in handwriting, one character at a time", "prompt": "A word originally in the copy (for example \"cheap\") is first struck through from left to right by a slightly slanted thick line, and the original word fades; then below it, a new word (for example \"affordable\") pops out one character at a time in a handwritten-style font in the accent color, as if someone is revising the copy by hand, to emphasize the better wording. (GSAP timeline: the strikethrough element scaleX 0 → 1, transform-origin:left; the original word's opacity drops to 0.4; the new word is split into characters with SplitText and pops out in sequence from below with back.out)", "tag": "GSAP timeline", "style": "Strike Through Strikethrough Rewrite Correction Handwriting Copy Strikethrough Rewrite Correction Copywriting Text Heading Animated Text", "txt": "Cheap Affordable"}, "298": {"desc": "The other person first shows the three \"typing\" dots, which then turn into a message, and then your reply pops out", "prompt": "Simulate a chat interface: the other person's chat bubble first appears on the left, containing three dots bouncing up and down in sequence (typing…); after about 1.4 seconds the bubble turns into a message (for example \"Are you there? I have a question~\") and bounces lightly; then your reply bubble pops out on the right in the accent color (appearing by enlarging from the bottom-right corner); after lingering, they move up and fade out together, then start again. (GSAP timeline: bubbles scale 0 → 1, transform-origin set at the corner of the bubble's tail, ease back.out; the three dots use CSS keyframes with staggered animation-delay)", "tag": "GSAP timeline", "style": "Chat Message Chat Box Bubble Typing Typing Indicator Customer Service Chat Bubble Typing Indicator Message Pop Text Heading Animated Text", "txt": "Yes! Feel free to ask 😊"}, "299": {"desc": "Several hollow copies are stacked behind the text, unfolding diagonally backward in sequence, then drawing back in", "prompt": "A bold large heading, behind which 5 layers of hollow outlined copies of the same text are stacked, each layer's outline fainter the farther back it goes; during the animation these copy layers unfold in sequence (each layer delayed by about 0.06 seconds) diagonally up and to the right, forming an afterimage like an echo or a 3D staircase, linger for a moment, then draw back in to overlap the original text, looping back and forth. (CSS: multiple spans stacked in the same grid cell, using the CSS variable --i to compute the translate distance, outline opacity and animation-delay; -webkit-text-stroke creates the hollow text)", "tag": "CSS keyframes", "style": "Afterimage Stacking Copies Hollow 3D Echo Echo Stack Outline Layers Repeat Text Text Heading Animated Text", "txt": "ECHO"}, "301": {"desc": "\"Hello\" in different languages takes turns appearing, blurring in and out, while the frame's width smoothly follows along", "prompt": "At the Hero heading position, \"hello\" in different languages is shown in rotation (Hello, Ni Hao, Konnichiwa, Bonjour, Hola, Annyeonghaseyo, Ciao), switching about every 1.6 seconds: the old word blurs and fades out upward, and the new word blurs in from below and becomes clear; because each word has a different length, the width of the container wrapping the text smoothly scales to the new word's width, so the small dot following behind it also moves smoothly instead of jumping instantly. (GSAP: first measure the new word's width (with a hidden measuring element), tween the container's width to the new width with power3.inOut; fade the text out and in with opacity, filter:blur and y)", "tag": "GSAP", "style": "Multilingual Greeting Hello Hello Switching International Multilingual Greeting Hello Languages Rotate Text Heading Animated Text", "txt": ""}, "302": {"desc": "Drag a row up or down, the other rows automatically make way, and on release it springs back into place and the numbering updates", "prompt": "A list that can be reordered by dragging, each row with a drag handle on the left and a sequence number on the right: when you press and hold a row it enlarges slightly and lifts up (deeper shadow and outline), and can be dragged up and down; as you drag past the positions of other rows, the rows you pass smoothly move up or down to make way; on release, the dragged row lands in its new position with a bit of elasticity, and all the numbers update to the new order. (GSAP Draggable type:\"y\": while dragging, compute the target index from y ÷ row height, change the array order and tween the other rows to index × row height; on release, align with back.out)", "tag": "Draggable", "style": "Drag Sorting Reorder List To-do sortable Drag Reorder List Sortable Cards Group", "txt": "Planning Design Development Launch"}, "304": {"desc": "When you click a card to select it, an outline and a checkmark appear, and an action bar reading \"N selected\" pops up at the bottom", "prompt": "A row of multi-selectable image cards: when you click a card, an accent-colored outline appears around the card and it shrinks slightly, the image enlarges slightly inside the frame, and the circular checkbox in the top-right corner fills in and draws a checkmark (with a bounce-back); as long as anything is selected, a capsule-shaped action bar pops up from the bottom of the screen, showing \"N selected\" (the number rolls up and down when it changes) and a \"Next →\" button; when everything is deselected, the action bar slides back and hides. (JS toggles aria-pressed, CSS changes the outline, scale and the checkmark's stroke-dashoffset based on [aria-pressed=true]; the action bar uses translateY and opacity transitions)", "tag": "JS + CSS", "style": "Select Multi-select Check Cards Action Bar Selectable Cards Multi Select Checkbox Action Bar Cards Group", "txt": "Seaside Mountains Night Sky Afternoon"}, "305": {"desc": "As the cursor moves among a group of cards, the borders and interiors of the cards near it are lit up by a pool of light", "prompt": "A set of cards in a feature-introduction section arranged in a grid, each card's border a fine ring: as the cursor moves within the whole section, each card draws a soft pool of light at \"the cursor's position relative to itself\", so the borders of cards close to the cursor are lit up in the accent color and their interiors also carry a faint glow, while cards farther away barely light up at all; as the cursor moves between cards, the light naturally crosses the borders of neighboring cards. (CSS: the card's outer layer uses 1px of padding as the border, with background radial-gradient(circle at var(--x) var(--y), accent color, transparent); the inner layer uses another, fainter radial-gradient; on mousemove over the container, JS computes the relative coordinates for each card and writes them into --x and --y)", "tag": "radial-gradient", "style": "Border Spotlight Glow Grid Feature Introduction SaaS Linear Border Spotlight Glow Grid Feature Cards Cards Group", "txt": "Speed Security Collaboration Integration Analytics Support"}, "306": {"desc": "Cards form a ring and slowly rotate in 3D space, and can be dragged left and right with the mouse to spin them", "prompt": "Eight image cards form a ring in 3D space, and the whole ring slowly rotates on its own at about 24 seconds per revolution; cards at the front are larger and nearer, cards at the back are smaller and farther, and cards facing away from the viewer are hidden; the user can press and drag left and right to rotate the ring, and on release it continues rotating on its own from the current angle. (CSS 3D: perspective on the container, transform-style:preserve-3d on the ring, each card rotateY(i × 360/N) translateZ(radius), backface-visibility:hidden; GSAP loops the ring's rotationY, and Draggable pauses it while dragging and sets the angle from the displacement)", "tag": "GSAP 3D", "style": "3D Ring Carousel Carousel Ring Ring Carousel 3D Rotate Gallery Drag Cards Group", "txt": "Seaside Mountains Night Sky Afternoon City Forest Lakeside Desert"}, "307": {"desc": "Click two cards to flip them over; if they match they stay and bounce, if not they flip back", "prompt": "A 4 × 2 card-flipping memory mini-game: all the cards start face down, and clicking one flips it in 3D to show the pattern on its front; after two cards are flipped, if the patterns are the same, both stay face up, their background turns into the accent color and they bounce; if they differ, after lingering about 0.8 seconds both flip back face down together; text below shows the matching progress, and after all pairs are matched successfully it shows celebratory text, shuffles and starts again. (CSS: cards use transform-style:preserve-3d, front and back faces use backface-visibility:hidden, and .on applies rotateY(180deg); JS manages the flipped cards and the match checking)", "tag": "JS + CSS", "style": "Card Flip Matching Memory Game Mini-game Interactive Memory Match Card Game Flip Pairs Cards Group", "txt": ""}, "308": {"desc": "Three stat cards float up in sequence, the numbers count up, a mini line chart draws itself, and the growth rates fade in", "prompt": "Three stat cards on an admin dashboard (revenue, orders, conversion rate): on entry they float up and fade in from below in sequence (about 0.12 seconds apart), the large number in each card counts up from 0 to its target value (including thousands separators and decimals), the mini line chart below draws itself from left to right, and finally the growth percentage fades in from the left. (GSAP timeline: cards from y:30, opacity:0, with stagger; numbers use an object tween + onUpdate formatting; the line chart's polyline uses DrawSVG 0% → 100% (or stroke-dashoffset))", "tag": "GSAP timeline", "style": "Dashboard Data Statistics KPI Line Chart sparkline Admin Dashboard Stat Cards KPI Sparkline Count Up Cards Group", "txt": ""}, "309": {"desc": "Click a page and it flips in 3D to the left around the spine as its axis; after flipping through them all, they flip back together to the first page", "prompt": "Like a book: on the right is a stack of pages, each page's front has an image and a page number; when clicked, the topmost page flips to the left in 3D space around the spine on its left side as its axis (about 0.9 seconds, ease-in-out), and halfway through the flip you can see the page's 3D angle; after flipping over, it shows that page's back; after flipping through them page by page, all the pages quickly flip back in sequence to the first page. (CSS 3D: each page uses transform-origin:left, transform-style:preserve-3d, front and back faces use backface-visibility:hidden, and the back uses rotateY(180deg); GSAP tweens rotationY 0 → −180, and adjusts the z-index during the flip so flipped pages stack on top)", "tag": "GSAP 3D", "style": "Page Flip Book Pages Magazine Catalog E-book Page Flip Book Magazine Catalog 3D Cards Group", "txt": "Prologue Journey Encounter Epilogue"}, "310": {"desc": "A scattered stack of photos smoothly arranges into a tidy grid with one click, and stacks back up with another click", "prompt": "A scattered stack of photos (each with a wide border, randomly tilted at different angles, stacked in the center): when clicked, the photos fly one after another (about 0.04 seconds apart) smoothly into a tidy 3 × 2 grid position and straighten up; click again and they fly from the grid back into a scattered stack. About 0.7 seconds, ease-in-out. (GSAP Flip: Flip.getState(photos) → switch the container's class (from absolutely-positioned stacking to a grid layout, rotate reset to zero) → Flip.from(state, {absolute:true, stagger:.04}))", "tag": "Flip", "style": "Photos Stack Spread Out Grid Album Organize Photo Pile Stack To Grid Spread Flip Cards Group", "txt": ""}, "311": {"desc": "Like a physical card, the cover opens in 3D around its left edge as its axis, revealing the image and text inside", "prompt": "A folded invitation card: at first you only see the cover (accent-colored background, a large heading and \"Click to open\"); when clicked, the cover flips open 180 degrees to the left in 3D space around its left side as its axis (about 0.9 seconds); the back of the cover is an image, and the right side reveals the invitation text and date on the card's inner page; at the same time the whole card shifts to the right so the opened whole stays centered; click again to close it. (CSS 3D: perspective on the container; the cover uses transform-origin:left, preserve-3d, front and back faces use backface-visibility:hidden, and the back uses rotateY(180deg); a GSAP timeline simultaneously tweens the cover's rotationY 0 → −180 and the card's xPercent 0 → 50, toggling play / reverse)", "tag": "GSAP 3D", "style": "Card Folded Invitation Card Greeting Card Open 3D Folding Greeting Invitation Card Open Cards Group", "txt": "YOU ARE INVITED"}, "312": {"desc": "When changing pages, a thin line at the top of the page quickly runs halfway, crawls slowly, then rushes to the end and disappears once loaded, and the content then emerges in sequence", "prompt": "When the site changes pages or loads content, a thin accent-colored progress bar (with a slight glow) appears at the very top of the page: it first quickly runs to about 30%, then slowly crawls to about 70% (giving the feeling of \"loading\"), and when loading completes it quickly rushes to 100% and fades out; at the same time the page content (heading, paragraphs, cards) fades in and floats up in sequence from below. (GSAP timeline: the progress bar uses transform-origin:left, scaleX 0 → .3 (power2.out) → .7 (slower) → 1 (fast), then opacity 0; the content fades in with stagger)", "tag": "GSAP", "style": "Loading Progress Bar Top Page Change NProgress YouTube Loading Bar Page Load Progress Layout Page", "txt": "Article Title"}, "313": {"desc": "Step dots above a multi-step form: completed ones get a checkmark, the current step enlarges, and the connecting line fills along with it", "prompt": "A step indicator above a multi-step form (for example sign-up or checkout): a row of circular step numbers connected by a line; the dots of completed steps fill in and a checkmark appears with a bounce-back, the current step's outer ring lights up and it enlarges slightly, and steps not yet reached stay faint; the filled length of the connecting line smoothly extends along with the steps; below there are \"Previous / Next\" buttons. (CSS: the connecting line's inner layer uses transform:scaleX(current index / (total − 1)), transition 0.5 seconds; steps switch styles with .done / .on classes, and the checkmark uses keyframes from scale 0 → 1)", "tag": "CSS transition", "style": "Steps Progress Multi-step Form Checkout Wizard Stepper Multi Step Form Wizard Progress Checkout Layout Page", "txt": "Account Details Payment Done"}, "314": {"desc": "When you hover over a navigation bar item, a large multi-column menu expands below it, and each column slides in in sequence", "prompt": "A website navigation bar: when the mouse moves over \"Products\", a large, wide menu panel expands below it (sliding down from slightly higher up and fading in); inside, the panel is divided into three columns: two columns are link lists with small icons, and one column is a featured image card; the three columns slide up and in in sequence (about 0.06 seconds apart); when the mouse leaves the navigation area, the panel collapses. (CSS: by default the panel has opacity 0, translateY(−8px), pointer-events:none, restored when the parent has :hover or .open; each column is given a transition-delay to create the sequential appearance)", "tag": "CSS transition", "style": "Mega Menu Dropdown Navigation Bar Multi-column mega menu Dropdown Navigation Header Layout Page", "txt": "Brand Design Web Development Motion Video Social Media Case Studies Design Guide"}, "315": {"desc": "Click a list item and the new page pushes in from the right while the old page retreats to the left and darkens; pressing back reverses it", "prompt": "Simulate an app's page-stack navigation: when you click an item in the list, the detail page pushes in as a full page from the right (with a shadow on its left side), while the original list page simultaneously moves about 30% to the left and darkens, as if covered over by the new page; clicking \"‹ Back\" in the top-left reverses it: the detail page exits to the right, and the list page moves back into place and regains its brightness. About 0.5 seconds, ease-in-out. (GSAP: the new page xPercent 100 → 0, the old page xPercent 0 → −30 with filter: brightness(.6); the reverse when going back)", "tag": "GSAP", "style": "Push In Page Change Back Navigation iOS Stack Push Pop Navigation Stack Page Transition App Layout Page", "txt": "Settings Notifications Privacy About"}, "316": {"desc": "When there are no search results, an empty box bounces down, its lid flips open and a question mark pops out, and the text and button appear in sequence", "prompt": "An empty state for when a search has no results or a list is empty: a simple box illustration drops from above and bounces to a stop, then the box's lid flips open around one corner as its axis, and a question mark emerges from inside and floats gently up and down; the heading, description text and \"Browse all\" button below fade in and move up in sequence; afterwards the lid closes and the question mark disappears. It keeps the blank screen from feeling cold and guides the next step. (GSAP timeline: the illustration from y:-20 with ease bounce.out → the lid rotation −28 with back.out → the question mark from scale 0 → the text fades in with stagger → the question mark floats with yoyo)", "tag": "GSAP timeline", "style": "Empty State No Results Not Found 404 Illustration Empty State No Results Illustration Layout Page", "txt": "No matching effects found"}, "317": {"desc": "A cookie consent card pops up at the bottom, the cookie icon wiggles; after pressing a button it shrinks back and slides away", "prompt": "A cookie consent card at the bottom of the website: when entering the page, the card slides up from below with a bounce-back, and the cookie icon on the left elastically straightens and enlarges from a small, tilted state; inside the card there is a heading, a brief description and two buttons (Essential only / Accept all); when either button is pressed, the button presses down lightly, and the card then slides down and out and fades away. (GSAP: the card fromTo yPercent 140 → 0, ease back.out(1.4); the icon rotation −40 → 0, scale .4 → 1, ease elastic.out; on close, yPercent → 140, power3.in)", "tag": "GSAP", "style": "Cookie Consent Banner Privacy GDPR Notice Consent Banner Privacy Notice Layout Page", "txt": "This site uses cookies"}, "318": {"desc": "When the \"+\" button in the bottom-right corner is clicked it turns into a \"×\", and several small action buttons and labels pop out above it in sequence", "prompt": "A circular floating action button (+) in the bottom-right corner of the screen: when clicked, the button rotates 135 degrees into a ×, a translucent overlay covers the background, and three small circular action buttons pop out above it from bottom to top in sequence, each with a text label on its left (for example New note, Take a photo, Share a link), appearing by enlarging with a bounce-back from a smaller, slightly lower position; click again or click the overlay to retract them in the reverse order. (CSS: when .open, the main button uses rotate(135deg); each action item is given a --i, transitions transform: translateY + scale, with transition-delay computed by index, in the reverse order when collapsing)", "tag": "CSS transition", "style": "Floating Button FAB Expand Quick Actions Speed Dial Floating Action Button Menu Layout Page", "txt": ""}, "319": {"desc": "When you scroll to the bottom, a spinning \"loading more\" appears, and new content then floats up one item after another", "prompt": "Infinite scrolling on a social feed wall or article list: when the user scrolls to the bottom of the list, a spinning loading indicator and \"Loading more…\" appear at the bottom; after about a second, a new batch of cards is appended after the list, fading in and floating up from below in sequence (about 0.12 seconds apart), and the user can keep scrolling down. (Implementation: use IntersectionObserver to watch a sentinel element at the bottom of the list; when it enters the viewport, show the loading indicator and request the next page; after the new cards are inserted, use GSAP from y:24, opacity:0, with stagger for the entrance)", "tag": "GSAP", "style": "Infinite Scroll Load More Pagination Feed Wall Infinite Scroll Load More Feed Pagination Layout Page", "txt": ""}, "320": {"desc": "Click to collapse an admin sidebar to just icons, the text fades out, and the main content area widens in sync", "prompt": "The sidebar on the left of an admin interface: when you click the collapse button at the top of the sidebar, the sidebar's width smoothly narrows to fit only the icons (about 0.45 seconds), the text of each item simultaneously fades out to the left, and the main content area on the right widens in sync; click again to expand and the text fades back in; the currently active item has a faint accent background color. (CSS: the sidebar uses a width transition, cubic-bezier(.6,0,.2,1); item text transitions opacity and translateX, with white-space:nowrap + overflow:hidden to prevent wrapping; the main content uses flex:1 to fill automatically)", "tag": "CSS transition", "style": "Sidebar Collapse Expand Admin Dashboard Collapsible Sidebar Nav Dashboard Admin Layout Page", "txt": "Home Reports Messages Settings"}, "321": {"desc": "Press ⌘K and a search panel pops up; as you type it filters the commands, the selected item lights up, and pressing Enter runs it", "prompt": "A command palette like ⌘K: when the shortcut is pressed, the background blurs and darkens, and a search panel pops up at the top center of the screen (appearing by enlarging from a slightly smaller, slightly higher position); the input field has a blinking cursor, and all the commands are listed below; as the user types, the list filters in real time to keep only the matching items, and the first matching item lights up with an accent background color and shows a ↵ hint; pressing Enter makes that item flash once and closes the panel. (JS: a keydown listener for Meta/Ctrl + K opens it; an input event filters the list; CSS transitions the panel from opacity + scale(.95) → 1, and the background uses backdrop-filter:blur)", "tag": "GSAP timeline", "style": "Command Palette Shortcut Search Cmd K Command Palette Spotlight Quick Search Layout Page", "txt": ""}, "322": {"desc": "Map pins drop down in sequence on a map, a route is drawn from the start point to the end point, and a small dot advances along the route", "prompt": "A simplified map background (faint landmass outlines and latitude/longitude grid lines), on which three map pins drop down from above in sequence and bounce to a stop, each labeled with a place name below it; then a route is drawn from the start point along a curved path all the way to the end point (about 2.2 seconds), while a small dot with a halo advances along the route; on reaching the end point, the end-point pin bounces once. (GSAP: the pins from y:-30 + bounce.out with stagger; the route uses DrawSVG 0% → 100%; the small dot uses MotionPathPlugin to move along the same path, with a duration matching the line drawing; beneath it there is also a faint dashed line indicating the full route)", "tag": "MotionPath", "style": "Map Route Navigation Pin Location Journey Delivery Logistics Map Route Path Pin Delivery Journey Graphics SVG", "txt": "Taipei Taichung Kaohsiung"}, "323": {"desc": "An analog clock showing the current time, whose second hand ticks one mark each second with a slight bounce-back", "prompt": "An analog clock showing the actual current time: the dial has 60 tick marks (every 5th one thicker and longer), the hour and minute hands move continuously and smoothly, and the second hand, in the accent color, ticks one mark every second, slightly overshooting within about 0.15 seconds as it ticks and then bouncing back into place, like a real mechanical watch. (JS requestAnimationFrame: read the hours, minutes, seconds and milliseconds from Date and compute each hand's angle; second hand angle = (seconds − 1 + bounce-back curve(milliseconds/150)) × 6 degrees; SVG lines use transform rotate)", "tag": "JS rAF", "style": "Clock Hands Second Hand Real-time Time Clock Analog Watch Time Real-time Graphics SVG", "txt": "Current Time"}, "324": {"desc": "A sunny sun slowly rotates, clouds drift, raindrops fall, and lightning flashes", "prompt": "A set of weather icon cards: in the sunny one, the sun and its rays slowly rotate on their own; in the cloudy one, the clouds drift gently left and right; in the rainy one, raindrops continuously fall from below the cloud at staggered times and fade out; in the thunderstorm one, the lightning is dim most of the time and occasionally flashes twice quickly. The weather name is labeled below each icon. (SVG + CSS keyframes: the sun rotates, one revolution in 10 seconds; the clouds move back and forth with translateX; the raindrops use translateY + opacity with staggered animation-delay; the lightning flickers using keyframes with steps(1))", "tag": "CSS keyframes", "style": "Weather Icons Sun Cloud Rain Lightning icon Weather Icons Animated Sun Cloud Rain Thunder Graphics SVG", "txt": ""}, "325": {"desc": "The lines of a dashed selection box flow continuously, there are handles at its four corners, and the size figures update in real time as the box changes size", "prompt": "A selection box like those in design tools: a dashed rectangle frames the content, the dashes flow continuously in the same direction (commonly called marching ants), and there are square handles at the four corners; the selection box's size changes smoothly between two sizes, and the size label below it (width × height) updates its figures in real time along with it. (SVG rect: stroke-dasharray 6 5, with keyframes looping stroke-dashoffset from 0 to −11 infinitely; the box's width/height are changed with CSS keyframes; JS periodically reads the size and updates the label)", "tag": "stroke-dashoffset", "style": "Selection Box Dashed Line Marching Ants Handles Design Tool Figma Marching Ants Selection Box Handles Graphics SVG", "txt": "Design Tool"}, "326": {"desc": "An irregular, soft blob keeps slowly morphing, with another fainter shadow layer behind it", "prompt": "An organic, irregular blob (like soft liquid or jelly) whose edges are driven by multiple sets of sine waves at different frequencies, continuously and slowly morphing and never repeating; behind it there is also a slightly larger, fainter shadow layer in the same color morphing at a different rhythm, adding depth; text is placed in the center of the blob. (JS requestAnimationFrame: take 8 control points distributed around a circle, radius = base + the sum of several sin(time + index × phase) values, and use Catmull-Rom to convert them into a smooth cubic Bézier curve written into the path's d)", "tag": "JS + SVG", "style": "Organic Blob Spot Flowing Morphing Liquid Blob Organic Shape Morph Liquid Graphics SVG", "txt": "Blob"}, "327": {"desc": "A hexagonal badge's outline is drawn, a star shrinks from large and stamps onto it, and rays radiate all around", "prompt": "A badge animation for when an achievement is earned: the outline of the hexagonal badge is first drawn in one stroke along its edges, then its interior fades in to fill it; a star quickly shrinks from a very large, rotating, transparent state down to the center of the badge with a bounce-back, like stamping it on; at the same time, a ring of short rays around the badge shoots rapidly outward from the inside and disappears, and the badge as a whole bounces lightly once; the achievement name and the words \"Achievement unlocked\" below emerge in sequence. (GSAP timeline: DrawSVG draws the outline → fillOpacity → the star fromTo scale 3 → 1, rotation −60 → 0, back.out → the rays DrawSVG \"0% 0%\" → \"0% 100%\" → \"100% 100%\")", "tag": "DrawSVG", "style": "Badge Achievement Unlock Reward Gamification Badge Achievement Unlock Reward Gamification Graphics SVG", "txt": "7-day login streak"}, "328": {"desc": "An ECG waveform is drawn from left to right, a glowing cursor dot advances along the line, and the heart-rate figure beside it pulses", "prompt": "An ECG display for a medical or health app: on a dark screen with fine grid lines, a glowing ECG waveform (flat line, small wave, the sharp QRS wave, T wave, repeating) is drawn from left to right, and a glowing cursor dot advances along with the drawing front; after drawing to the end, the line begins disappearing from the left side and is redrawn; the top-right shows a heart-rate figure (occasionally varying slightly) and a heart beating regularly. (GSAP: DrawSVG \"0% 0%\" → \"0% 100%\" to draw it out, then to \"100% 100%\" to make it disappear; the cursor dot uses MotionPathPlugin along the same path; the heart uses scale yoyo)", "tag": "DrawSVG", "style": "ECG Heartbeat Waveform Health Medical Monitoring ECG Heartbeat Pulse Monitor Health Graphics SVG", "txt": ""}, "329": {"desc": "The trunk grows first, then branches split off, and finally the leaves emerge one by one", "prompt": "A tree grows from the bottom up: first the ground line and the main trunk are drawn (about 0.8 seconds), then branches to the left and right grow out in sequence, followed by finer twigs; after the branches are drawn, leaves pop out one by one from the ends of the branches in random order (enlarging from 0 to 1, with a bounce-back); finally text emerges below. Suitable for brand stories, growth or sustainability themes. (GSAP timeline: each branch is an SVG path, drawn in sequence with DrawSVG 0% → 100%; the leaves use scale 0 → 1, transform-origin at the leaf stem, stagger from:\"random\")", "tag": "DrawSVG", "style": "Tree Growing Plant Branches Leaves Growth Sustainability Growing Tree Plant Branches Leaves Growth Graphics SVG", "txt": "Growing Slowly"}, "330": {"desc": "Three gears of different sizes mesh together, driving each other at different speeds according to their tooth-count ratio", "prompt": "Three gears of different sizes and tooth counts mesh with each other: the largest gear rotates clockwise at a fixed speed, and the two smaller gears meshing with it rotate counterclockwise at higher speeds according to their tooth-count ratio (the one with fewer teeth turns faster), with tooth aligned to tooth and no clipping, like a mechanical system in operation; suitable for \"processing\", settings or system-status screens. (SVG: generate each gear's outline path programmatically from its radius and tooth count; GSAP loops each gear's rotation infinitely, with a small gear's angular velocity = the large gear × (large tooth count ÷ small tooth count), in the opposite direction, and sets the initial phase so the teeth align)", "tag": "GSAP", "style": "Gears Linked Mechanism Running Settings System Gears Cogs Mechanism Rotation Settings Graphics SVG", "txt": "System Running"}, "331": {"desc": "Fingerprint ridges are drawn ring by ring, a scanning light bar sweeps up and down, and after success the frame glows and a checkmark appears", "prompt": "A phone fingerprint-unlock screen: in a rounded-square sensing area, the fingerprint's curved ridges are drawn in sequence ring by ring from the inside out; then a glowing scanning light bar sweeps from top to bottom and back from bottom to top, and the text below shows \"Scanning…\"; after the scan completes, the fingerprint ridges fade, a thick checkmark is quickly drawn, the sensing area's frame emits a glow, and the text changes to \"Verified\". (GSAP timeline: the fingerprint arcs are drawn with DrawSVG stagger; the scanning bar top 0% → 100% yoyo; on completion, add a class to make the frame's box-shadow glow, and the checkmark DrawSVG 0% → 100%)", "tag": "DrawSVG", "style": "Fingerprint Scan Unlock Biometric Verification Login Fingerprint Scan Biometric Unlock Auth Graphics SVG", "txt": "Verified"}};
